window.EXAM = [{"id":"red1-1","src":"red1","n":1,"cat":"vascular","stem":"60-year-old female presents with a chronic ankle wound and deep vein thrombosis that occurred 10 years ago.\nWhich one of following cannot identify venous reflux?","opts":[["A","CT-venography"],["B","Trendelenburg test"],["C","Air plethysmography"],["D","Descending venography"],["E","Duplex color ultrasound"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"โจทย์ถาม \"cannot\" → หา test ที่ดูแค่ภาพนิ่ง/โครงสร้าง ไม่ได้ดูทิศการไหลย้อน","e":"Venous reflux ต้องดู \"เลือดไหลย้อนลง\" แบบ dynamic: Trendelenburg test (แยก superficial vs deep/perforator reflux ข้างเตียง), air plethysmography (venous filling index), descending venography (เดิมเป็น gold standard ของ reflux) และ duplex ultrasound (first-line ปัจจุบัน วัด reflux time > 0.5 s). CT venography ให้ภาพกายวิภาค/ดู obstruction (เช่น May-Thurner, iliac vein) แต่ไม่ได้วัดการไหลย้อน → ตอบ A. (LP ลังเลระหว่าง B/C แต่เฉลย Med46 และไฟล์ edit = A)"},{"id":"red1-2","src":"red1","n":2,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 35-year-old male who is a heavy smoker with mitral stenosis presented with an abrupt onset of left leg pain that started 4 hours before arrival\nPE\nRt Lt\nFemoral 2+ 2+\nPopliteal 2+ 0\nDP/PT 2+ 0\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","CT angiography"],["B","Intravenous opioid"],["C","Endovascular stent"],["D","Emergency embolectomy"],["E","Systemic rTPA (recombinant tissue plasminogen activator)"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ขาปวดเฉียบพลัน + แหล่ง emboli (MS) + pulse หายใต้ popliteal → embolic ALI → ไม่ต้องรอ imaging","e":"Mitral stenosis → AF/thrombus ใน LA → embolus ไปติด popliteal (femoral 2+ แต่ popliteal 0). อาการ 4 ชม. ประวัติชัดเจนว่าเป็น embolic → ให้ heparin แล้ว emergency Fogarty balloon embolectomy. CTA ทำให้เสียเวลาในเคส embolic ที่ชัดเจน; systemic rTPA ไม่ใช้ใน ALI (ใช้ catheter-directed thrombolysis ในบางเคส thrombotic); stent ใช้กับ thrombosis บน atherosclerosis ไม่ใช่ embolus."},{"id":"red1-3","src":"red1","n":3,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 65-year-old female with a history of long-standing DM presented with a wound at her right foot for 2 months.\nPE: Well-granulated ulcer at plantar surface of right big toe. The distal pulses are palpable.\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Off-loading shoes"],["B","Angioplasty"],["C","Big toe amputation"],["D","Femorotibial bypass graft"],["E","Oral antibiotics and daily wound care"]],"key":"E","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"แผล DM → ถาม 3 ข้อ: เลือดพอไหม (pulse) · ติดเชื้อไหม · แรงกดไหม","e":"แผลฝ่าเท้าใต้นิ้วโป้ง granulation ดี + pulse คลำได้ = neuropathic ulcer ไม่มี ischemia ไม่มี infection → หัวใจการรักษาคือ off-loading (total contact cast/half-shoe) + ตัด callus + moist dressing. Oral ATB ใช้เมื่อมี infection (LP เขียนกำกับว่า \"E = infected wound\"). Angioplasty/bypass ใช้เมื่อมี PAD; amputation เกินเหตุ. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) กา E แต่เฉลย LP แก้เป็น A ซึ่งตรงกับ IWGDF."},{"id":"red1-4","src":"red1","n":4,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old man sustained a blast injury at his right chest. He underwent ICP which reveal led 500 mL of fresh blood and continuous air leak. The patient still complained of dyspnea. PI : RR 30/min, decreased breath wounds at Rt lung. The doctor performed endotracheal tube intubation and connected him to a mechanical ventilator. then the patient developed sudden cardiac arrest.\nWhich of the following is the most likely cause of cardiac arrest?","opts":[["A","Air embolism"],["B","Tension pneumothorax"],["C","Open pneumothorax"],["D","Flail chest with lung contusion"],["E","Massive hemothorax"]],"key":"B","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Sudden arrest \"ทันทีหลังเริ่ม positive pressure ventilation\" ในคนที่มี lung injury + air leak","e":"Blast/penetrating lung injury ทำให้เกิด bronchovenous fistula; เมื่อใส่ ventilator แรงดันในหลอดลมสูงกว่าใน pulmonary vein → ลมเข้า systemic circulation → coronary/cerebral air embolism → arrest ทันที (classic ATLS). Tension pneumothorax ก็เกิดหลัง PPV ได้ แต่ผู้ป่วยมี ICD อยู่แล้ว (ระบายลมได้). เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = B แต่ตามหลัก ATLS และบทเรียน Day 3 ตอบ air embolism."},{"id":"red1-5","src":"red1","n":5,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old man stabbed at the Lt chest, at the left parasternal border. He is agitated.\nPE: BP 80/60 mmHg; RR 28/min; neck vein engorged; lungs - breath sounds. Rt.=Lt.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Tension pneumothorax"],["B","Open pneumothorax"],["C","Cardiac tamponade"],["D","SVC obstruction"],["E","Simple pneumothorax"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Beck's triad = hypotension + neck vein engorged + (heart sound เบา) แต่เสียงปอดเท่ากัน","e":"แผลแทง parasternal ซ้าย (\"cardiac box\") + BP ต่ำ + JVD + breath sound Rt = Lt → cardiac tamponade. Tension pneumothorax ก็ JVD + hypotension ได้แต่ต้องมี breath sound ลดข้างเดียว/trachea shift. รักษา: pericardiocentesis เป็น bridge → OR (thoracotomy/sternotomy)."},{"id":"red1-6","src":"red1","n":6,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 20-year-old man developed chest discomfort after a motorcycle crash. The chest X-ray revealed a visible visceral pleural edge.\nWhich one of the following is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hemothorax"],["B","Lung contusion"],["C","Pneumothorax"],["D","Mediastinal emphysema"],["E","Subcutaneous emphysema"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Visceral pleural line ที่เห็นแยกจากผนังอก = เส้นปอดที่ยุบ","e":"เห็น visceral pleural edge และไม่มี lung marking นอกเส้นนั้น = pneumothorax. Hemothorax เห็นเป็น opacity/blunted angle; lung contusion = patchy opacity ไม่ตาม segment; mediastinal emphysema เห็นลมรอบ mediastinum; subcutaneous emphysema เห็นลมในชั้นใต้ผิวหนัง."},{"id":"red1-7","src":"red1","n":7,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 48-year-old has acute limb ischemia at right leg for 12 hours . After reperfusion, the EKG showed\nWhat is the next step in management?","opts":[["A","IV hydration"],["B","Defibrillation"],["C","Calcium gluconate IV"],["D","Verapamil"],["E","Start CPR"]],"key":"B","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q7-1.jpg"],"t":"หลัง reperfusion → K⁺ จากกล้ามเนื้อที่ตายทะลักเข้าเลือด; EKG sine wave = hyperK ระยะท้าย (ยังมีชีพจร)","e":"Reperfusion syndrome → hyperkalemia + acidosis + myoglobinuria. EKG sine wave ต้องให้ 10% calcium gluconate IV ทันทีเพื่อ stabilize membrane แล้วตามด้วย insulin+glucose, ขับ K. Defibrillation ใช้กับ VF/pulseless VT ไม่ใช่ sine wave ที่ยังมี pulse. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) กา B แต่เฉลย LP แก้เป็น C ซึ่งถูกตามหลัก."},{"id":"red1-8","src":"red1","n":8,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old male suffered from a motorcycle crash 30 min PTA. The examination revealed vital signs of BP 80/30 mmHg, PR 90 bpm, RR 35 bpm, and O 2 sat 70%. The Glasgow Coma Scale score was E2VIM4\nWhich of the following is the appropriate diagnosis for this patient?","opts":[["A","Mild head injury"],["B","Moderate head injury"],["C","Severe head injury"],["D","Minimal head injury"],["E","Undetermined"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"คำนวณ GCS ก่อน: E2 + V1 + M4 = 7 → ≤ 8 = severe","e":"GCS 13–15 mild, 9–12 moderate, ≤ 8 severe → GCS 7 = severe head injury (และต้อง intubate). แม้ shock + hypoxia อาจทำให้ GCS ต่ำกว่าความจริง (บางคนตอบ undetermined) แต่การจัดระดับตาม ATLS ใช้ GCS ที่วัดได้ หลัง resuscitate แล้วค่อยประเมินซ้ำ."},{"id":"red1-9","src":"red1","n":9,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"60-year-old man was admitted in the hospital for a 25% B A bum. Three weeks after admission. he developed abdominal distension, no fever, no passing stool.\nAbdominal film:\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis ?","opts":[["A","Paralytic ileus"],["B","ischemic bowel"],["C","Toxic megacolon"],["D","Pseudo-colonic obstruction"],["E","Pseudomembranous colitis"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q9-1.jpg"],"t":"ผู้ป่วยหนัก/นอนนาน (burn) + ท้องอืด + colon โป่งมากโดยไม่มีจุดอุด และไม่มีไข้ = Ogilvie","e":"ฟิล์มเห็น colon โป่งทั้งแนวถึง rectum ไม่มีจุดตัด, ไม่มีไข้/diarrhea → acute colonic pseudo-obstruction (Ogilvie syndrome) ซึ่งพบในผู้ป่วยหนัก burn, หลังผ่าตัด, electrolyte ผิดปกติ, ยา opioid. Toxic megacolon ต้องมี colitis + toxic (ไข้ tachycardia); pseudomembranous colitis มี diarrhea; paralytic ileus มักโป่งทั้ง SB และ colon แบบไม่มาก."},{"id":"red1-10","src":"red1","n":10,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 40-year-old man sustained injuries in a car crash.\nPE: He has good consciousness BP 120/80 mmHg. PR 110/min\nAbd: Generalized guarding\nFAST: -ve\nWhich of the following is the most proper management?","opts":[["A","Serial serum lactate"],["B","CT scan abdomen"],["C","Exploratory laparotomy"],["D","Diagnostic peritoneal lavage"],["E","NSS 2 L iv free flow"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Blunt abdominal trauma: ถาม 2 ข้อ — hemodynamic? peritonitis? ถ้ามี peritonitis → ผ่าตัด แม้ FAST ลบ","e":"Generalized guarding = peritonitis (สงสัย hollow viscus injury) → exploratory laparotomy เลย. FAST ไวต่อเลือดแต่พลาด hollow viscus ได้; CT ใช้ในคน stable ที่ตรวจท้องไม่ชัด ไม่ใช่คนที่มี peritonitis แล้ว; DPL ใช้ใน unstable ที่ FAST ไม่ชัด. LP เขียนกำกับ \"peritonitis\"."},{"id":"red1-11","src":"red1","n":11,"cat":"infection","stem":"What is the alternative antibiotic for uncomplicated appendectomy in penicillin allergic patients?","opts":[["A","Cefalexin"],["B","Cefazolin"],["C","Augmentin"],["D","Ciprofloxacin with metronidazole"],["E","Vancomycin with metronidazole"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Prophylaxis appendectomy ปกติ = cefoxitin หรือ cefazolin + metronidazole; แพ้ penicillin (anaphylaxis) เลี่ยง β-lactam","e":"ทางเลือกในคนแพ้ penicillin ตาม ASHP/IDSA สำหรับ colorectal/appendectomy = metronidazole ร่วมกับ fluoroquinolone (ciprofloxacin) หรือ aminoglycoside, หรือ clindamycin + aminoglycoside. Cephalosporin มี cross-reactivity; Augmentin เป็น penicillin; vancomycin ไม่คลุม gram-negative. เฉลยเดิมบางฉบับกา cefazolin แต่ LP แก้เป็น D."},{"id":"red1-12","src":"red1","n":12,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old male developed pain at the surgical site after lipoma excision 3 days ago. Physical examination showed swelling, redness, warmth, and marked tenderness with pus discharge from the wound. What is the most likely pathogen in this case?","opts":[["A","Escherichia coli"],["B","Mixed organism"],["C","Anaerobe bacteria"],["D","Staphylococcus aureus"],["E","Beta hemolytic streptococcus"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"SSI ของแผล clean (ตัด lipoma) วันที่ 3 มีหนอง = เชื้อจากผิวหนัง","e":"Clean wound infection เกิดจาก skin flora → Staphylococcus aureus พบมากที่สุด. Mixed organism/E. coli/anaerobe พบใน clean-contaminated/contaminated (ผ่าตัดลำไส้). Beta-hemolytic strep ทำให้ cellulitis เร็วภายใน 24–48 ชม. และมักไม่มีหนอง."},{"id":"red1-13","src":"red1","n":13,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 50-year-old female with a 10-year history of poorly controlled DM developed a wound with pus discharge at the Rt. big toe for 1 month.\nPE : Swelling of the Rt. big toe with redness, 0.5 cm sinus tract, and pus discharge him of the Rt. foot showed an osteolytic lesion at the head of the metacarpal bone of the big toe.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Wet dressing"],["B","Debridement"],["C","IV antibiotic"],["D","Incision and drainage"],["E","Amputation of the Rt. big toe"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"DM foot + sinus tract + osteolytic lesion = osteomyelitis → ต้องเอากระดูก/เนื้อตายออก","e":"Osteomyelitis จากแผลเบาหวาน หลักคือ surgical debridement (เอาเนื้อตาย + กระดูกที่ติดเชื้อออก, ส่งเพาะเชื้อกระดูก) ร่วมกับ antibiotic ตามผลเพาะ. ATB อย่างเดียวไม่พอเพราะมี sequestrum; I&D เหมาะกับ abscess; amputation นิ้วทำเมื่อนิ้วตาย/ทำลายมากจนรักษาไม่ได้ (โน้ตรุ่นพี่: debride ก่อน แต่ถ้าทั้งนิ้วเสียค่อย amputate). เฉลยไฟล์และ LP = B."},{"id":"red1-14","src":"red1","n":14,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 60-year-old female with no underlying disease was diagnosed with pancreatic head tumor. She underwent Whipple's operation.\nWhich one or the following factors increases post-op wound infection?","opts":[["A","Prophylactic antibiotics"],["B","Preoperative biliary drainage"],["C","Keep blood sugar between"],["D","Prevention of intraoperative hypothermia"],["E","Adequate oxygenation during and post operation"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ข้อใด \"เพิ่ม\" SSI → ตัวเลือกอื่นเป็นมาตรการลด SSI ทั้งหมด","e":"Preoperative biliary drainage (ERCP stent/PTBD) ก่อน Whipple ทำให้ bile ติดเชื้อ (bactibilia) → SSI และ infectious complications เพิ่มขึ้น จึงทำเฉพาะเมื่อจำเป็น (cholangitis, bilirubin สูงมาก, ต้องรอ neoadjuvant). Prophylactic ATB, คุมน้ำตาล, กัน hypothermia, ให้ O₂ เพียงพอ ล้วนลด SSI."},{"id":"red1-15","src":"red1","n":15,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 40-year-old male was punctured by a nail while working I hour prior to presenting at the ER. He has a history of full course tetanus toxoid administration in the past year.\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Wound irrigation, wet dressing, and antibiotic"],["B","Open wound, wound irrigation, wet dressing, and discharge"],["C","Dressing wound with Betadine, oral antibiotic, and discharge"],["D","Open wound, wet dressing, oral antibiotic, and single dose of tetanus toxoid"],["E","Dressing wound with Betadine, oral antibiotic, and single dose of tetanus toxoid"]],"key":"A","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"บาดทะยัก: ดู \"ครบชุดไหม + นานแค่ไหน\" · แผล: ตะปูตำ = puncture wound ห้ามเย็บ","e":"ได้ TT ครบชุดภายใน 1 ปี → ไม่ต้องให้ TT (แผลสกปรกให้เมื่อ > 5 ปี). แผลตะปูตำต้องเปิดแผล ล้างสะอาด wet dressing ไม่ปิดแผล และไม่จำเป็นต้องให้ ATB ในแผลไม่ติดเชื้อ → B. Betadine ทำลายเนื้อเยื่อ ไม่ใช้ราดแผล. เฉลยไฟล์กา A (ให้ ATB ด้วย) แต่ตามหลักไม่ต้องให้ ATB prophylaxis ในแผลธรรมดา."},{"id":"red1-16","src":"red1","n":16,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"Which one of following is not a complication in patient corrosive esophagitis?","opts":[["A","Esophageal stricture"],["B","CA esophagus"],["C","Barrett’s esophagus"],["D","Gastric outlet obstruction"],["E","Pneumonitis"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Corrosive injury: ระยะยาว = stricture + CA (SCC) ; กรด/ด่างกระทบกระเพาะได้; Barrett มาจาก GERD","e":"Complication ของ corrosive ingestion: esophageal stricture, SCC esophagus (ความเสี่ยงเพิ่มหลายสิบปีต่อมา), gastric outlet obstruction (โดยเฉพาะกรด → pyloric stricture), aspiration pneumonitis. Barrett's esophagus เกิดจาก chronic GERD (intestinal metaplasia) ไม่ใช่จาก corrosive."},{"id":"red1-17","src":"red1","n":17,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 25-year-old male came with recurrent peri-anal fistula. He has a history of anorexia, weight loss, and chronic diarrhea with occasional mucus bloody stool.\nProctoscopy: normal appearing rectum\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Crohn’s colitis"],["B","Amebic colitis"],["C","Ischemic colitis"],["D","Ulcerative colitis"],["E","HIV +ve with CMV infection"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Fistula ซ้ำ + diarrhea เรื้อรัง + น้ำหนักลด ในคนหนุ่ม แต่ \"rectum ปกติ\" → นึกถึง Crohn's (rectal sparing)","e":"Crohn's disease มี perianal disease (fistula/abscess ซับซ้อน) และมักไม่เป็นที่ rectum (skip lesion). Ulcerative colitis เริ่มที่ rectum เสมอ → proctoscopy ต้องผิดปกติ และไม่ค่อยมี fistula. Amebic/ischemic colitis ไม่มี fistula ซ้ำ."},{"id":"red1-18","src":"red1","n":18,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 12-year-old girl, self-palpated left breast mass with mild pain but without other symptoms. Physical examination revealed well-circumscribed mass 1.5 cm in diameter beneath the nipple. Ultrasonography showed echo-poor mass beneath left nipple\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Reassure"],["B","Core-needle biopsy"],["C","Excisional biopsy"],["D","Ultrasonography guide biopsy"],["E","Subcutaneous mastectomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"เด็กหญิงก่อน/ช่วงวัยรุ่น + ก้อนใต้ nipple พอดี = breast bud","e":"ก้อนใต้หัวนม 1.5 cm ในเด็ก 12 ปี เจ็บนิดหน่อย = physiologic breast development (thelarche/breast bud). ห้าม biopsy/ตัด เพราะจะทำลาย breast bud → เต้านมไม่เจริญ. ให้ reassure และนัดติดตาม."},{"id":"red1-19","src":"red1","n":19,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 30-year-old female ingested a corrosive agent 6 hour ago.\nV/S: temp 38 ℃, BP130/90 mmHg, HR 120/min, RR 30/min\nPE: drooling, stridor, erythematous oral mucosa: Crepitus at the neck and chest wall\nWhich one of following is the most proper initial management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Bronchoscopy"],["B","Esophagoscopy"],["C","Neutralized agent"],["D","Retained NG tube"],["E","Endotracheal tube intubation"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Corrosive + stridor/drooling/crepitus คอ → airway ก่อนทุกอย่าง (A ของ ABC)","e":"Stridor และ drooling บ่งว่ามี airway edema กำลังจะอุด → ต้องรักษา airway ด้วย endotracheal intubation (ถ้าใส่ไม่ได้ทำ surgical airway). Crepitus บ่งว่าอาจมี perforation. ห้าม neutralize (ปฏิกิริยาความร้อน), ห้ามใส่ NG แบบ blind, esophagoscopy ทำหลัง airway ปลอดภัย (ภายใน 12–24/48 ชม.)."},{"id":"red1-20","src":"red1","n":20,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 28-year-old female 2-week postpartum developed right breast pain from 3 days ago. The physical examination revealed swelling, hyperemia, warmth, marked tenderness and fluctuation at upper outer quadrant of right breast with thinning and necrosis of overlying skin.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Breast feeding cessation with warmth compression"],["B","Serial ultrasound"],["C","Advice breast feeding cessation and IV ATB"],["D","Aspiration with oral antibiotic"],["E","Incision and drainage"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Lactational breast abscess: ขนาดเล็กผิวดี → aspiration; ผิวบาง/เนื้อตาย → I&D","e":"มี fluctuation + ผิวหนังบางและ necrosis = abscess ที่ใกล้แตก ไม่เหมาะกับ needle aspiration → incision and drainage + ATB (cloxacillin/dicloxacillin) และให้นมต่อ/ปั๊มนมได้. Breastfeeding cessation ไม่จำเป็น (การระบายน้ำนมช่วยให้หาย)."},{"id":"red1-21","src":"red1","n":21,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"Which one of following is not a treatment in patients with esophageal cancer?","opts":[["A","Gastrostomy"],["B","Esophageal expandable stent"],["C","Heller’s operation"],["D","Esophagectomy"],["E","Radiation therapy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Heller myotomy = ผ่า LES สำหรับ achalasia","e":"CA esophagus รักษาด้วย esophagectomy (resectable), chemoradiation, ส่วน palliative = expandable stent หรือ gastrostomy/jejunostomy เพื่อให้อาหาร. Heller's myotomy ใช้รักษา achalasia ไม่ใช่มะเร็ง."},{"id":"red1-22","src":"red1","n":22,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old man presented with progressive dysphagia for 1 month with weight loss of 3 kg in 1 month. EGD:\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Esophagitis"],["B","Esophageal ulcer"],["C","Esophageal cancer"],["D","Barrett's esophagus"],["E","Hiatal hernia"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q22-1.jpg"],"t":"Progressive dysphagia + น้ำหนักลด (alarm) + EGD เห็นก้อน friable ยื่นเข้า lumen","e":"ภาพ EGD เป็น exophytic/ulcerated mass ทำให้ lumen แคบ ร่วมกับประวัติ progressive dysphagia + weight loss → esophageal cancer. ขั้นต่อไป biopsy และ staging ด้วย CT chest + upper abdomen."},{"id":"red1-23","src":"red1","n":23,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 50-year-old women presented with dysphagia for a year. No weight loss.\nPE\nGA: No cachexia\nHEENT: Anemia. glossitis, no lymphadenopathy\nExt: No pitting edema. koilonychia\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Achalasia"],["B","Esophageal cancer"],["C","Nutcracker esophagus"],["D","Esophageal diverticulum"],["E","Cervical esophagus web"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Dysphagia + iron deficiency anemia (glossitis, koilonychia) ในหญิงวัยกลางคน = Plummer–Vinson","e":"Plummer–Vinson (Paterson–Kelly) syndrome = iron deficiency anemia + cervical (post-cricoid) esophageal web + dysphagia; เสี่ยง SCC ของ hypopharynx/upper esophagus. รักษา iron + dilatation. ไม่มีน้ำหนักลดและเป็นมา 1 ปีช่วยตัด CA."},{"id":"red1-24","src":"red1","n":24,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 55-year-old man was admitted with recurrent acute upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage. Previously, an endoscopic examination revealed a 3-cm ulcerative mass at the antrum and the pathological biopsy showed adenocarcinoma with moderate differentiation. At this admission, endoscopy shows active bleeding from the ulcer and the bleeding fails to stop.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Gastrotomy with cauterizing and over-sewing of the bleeding site"],["B","Highly selective vagotomy, cauterizing and over-sewing of the bleeding ulcer"],["C","Truncal vagotomy, pyloroplasty, cauterizing and over-sewing of the bleeding ulcer"],["D","Excision of ulcer"],["E","Subtotal gastrectomy with lymph node dissection"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"เลือดออกจาก \"มะเร็งกระเพาะ\" ไม่ใช่ peptic ulcer → ผ่าตัดต้องเป็นการผ่าตัดมะเร็ง","e":"Endoscopic hemostasis ล้มเหลวในก้อน adenocarcinoma ที่ antrum → ทำ subtotal (distal) gastrectomy + D2 lymphadenectomy ซึ่งหยุดเลือดและรักษามะเร็งไปพร้อมกัน (ถ้ายัง resectable). Vagotomy/oversewing เป็นการผ่าตัดของ peptic ulcer bleeding; excision ulcer อย่างเดียวไม่ใช่ oncologic resection."},{"id":"red1-25","src":"red1","n":25,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"Which one of following is not a genetic mutation in patients with colorectal cancer?","opts":[["A","Adenomatous polyposis coli (APC)"],["B","CAG triplicate repeat sequence"],["C","K-ran"],["D","DCC/p53"],["E","hMLH1 / hMLH2"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"CAG repeat = trinucleotide repeat ของโรคทางประสาท (Huntington)","e":"Colorectal carcinogenesis: APC (adenoma–carcinoma sequence เริ่มต้น), KRAS, DCC/SMAD4 (18q), p53 และ mismatch repair genes (hMLH1, hMSH2 – Lynch/HNPCC). CAG triplet repeat เป็นกลไกของ Huntington disease ไม่เกี่ยวกับ CRC."},{"id":"red1-26","src":"red1","n":26,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 72-year-old female presented with severe generalized abdominal pain for 1 day. Two days ago, she had left lower quadrant abdominal pain. She also had low grade fever and nausea without vomiting. Today the pain was progressing. She had no history of abdominal surgery. The physical examination revealed generalized severe tenderness and involuntary guarding of her entire abdomen.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis ?","opts":[["A","Ruptured appendicitis"],["B","Ulcerative colitis"],["C","Sigmoid diverticulosis"],["D","Peptic ulcer perforation"],["E","Sigmoid colon cancer perforation"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"LLQ pain 2 วัน แล้วกลายเป็น generalized peritonitis ในผู้สูงอายุ → อวัยวะที่ LLQ ทะลุ","e":"ในตัวเลือก โรคที่เริ่ม LLQ แล้วทะลุจนปวดทั่วท้อง = sigmoid perforation (มะเร็งหรือ diverticulitis). \"Sigmoid diverticulosis\" เฉยๆ ไม่ทำให้ peritonitis (ต้องเป็น diverticulitis), ruptured appendicitis เริ่มที่ RLQ, PU perforation เริ่มที่ epigastrium ทันที. เลยเหลือ sigmoid colon cancer perforation."},{"id":"red1-27","src":"red1","n":27,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 90-year-old status bed-ridden patient underwent right hemicolectomy after developing gut obstruction. The pathological report was adenocarcinoma which invaded the outer muscular layers and positive malignancy 6 of 15 pericolic lymph nodes. The chest and abdominal CT scan did not demonstrate any abnormal lesions in the pulmonary or hepatic areas.\nWhat is the appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Targeted therapy"],["B","Chemoradiotherapy"],["C","Surveillance"],["D","Oral form of chemotherapy"],["E","Intravenous chemotherapy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Stage III colon cancer ปกติต้องให้ adjuvant chemo — แต่ดู performance status ก่อน","e":"T3N2 (6/15 nodes) = stage III ซึ่งปกติให้ adjuvant chemotherapy แต่ผู้ป่วย 90 ปี ติดเตียง (ECOG 4) ทนพิษยาไม่ได้และได้ประโยชน์น้อย → surveillance/supportive care. Chemoradiation ใช้กับ rectal cancer ไม่ใช่ colon."},{"id":"red1-28","src":"red1","n":28,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 28-year-old female presented with right bloody nipple discharge.\nPE : The Rt breast had a blood discharge from a single duct without a breast mass.\nWhich of the following is the most proper management?","opts":[["A","Observation"],["B","Modified radical mastectomy"],["C","Microdochectomy"],["D","Wild excision"],["E","Mammography"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Bloody nipple discharge จากรูเดียว ไม่มีก้อน ในหญิงอายุน้อย = intraductal papilloma จนกว่าจะพิสูจน์ได้ว่าไม่ใช่","e":"Pathologic discharge (spontaneous, unilateral, single duct, bloody) สาเหตุบ่อยสุด intraductal papilloma → ทำ imaging (U/S ± mammogram อายุ ≥ 30–40) แล้ว microdochectomy (ตัดท่อที่ผิดปกติ) เพื่อทั้งวินิจฉัยและรักษา. ในตัวเลือก C ดีที่สุด (อายุ 28 mammogram มีประโยชน์น้อย)."},{"id":"red1-29","src":"red1","n":29,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 45-year-old female presented with a left breast mass for 2 months. No other abnormal symptoms.PE: ill-defined mass 2 cm in diameter at upper outer quadrant of left breast.\nMammography: Hyperdense mass 2 cm in diameter with cluster of microcalcification and spiculated border.\nWhich of the following the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Fat necrosis"],["B","Fibroadenoma"],["C","Intraductal papilloma"],["D","Ductal ectasia"],["E","Carcinoma of left breast"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Mammogram: spiculated margin + clustered pleomorphic microcalcification = BI-RADS 5","e":"Hyperdense spiculated mass + cluster microcalcification → highly suggestive of malignancy (BI-RADS 5) → carcinoma ต้อง core biopsy ยืนยัน. Fat necrosis อาจ spiculate ได้แต่มักมีประวัติ trauma และ oil cyst; fibroadenoma ขอบเรียบ calcification แบบ popcorn."},{"id":"red1-30","src":"red1","n":30,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 50-year-old female was diagnosed as CA breast from tissue pathology. PE: 5 cm mass at Lt breast with peau de orange appearance. LN 2 cm at Lt. axillar Work-up for distant metastasis: -ve .\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","Modified radical mastectomy (MRM)"],["B","Breast conserving surgery (BCS)"],["C","Radiation"],["D","Neoadjuvant chemotherapy"],["E","Hormonal therapy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Peau d'orange = T4b → locally advanced breast cancer","e":"ก้อน 5 cm + peau d'orange (skin involvement, T4) + axillary node → LABC (stage III) ไม่มี distant mets → neoadjuvant chemotherapy ก่อน (shrink tumor) แล้วตามด้วย MRM + radiation. ผ่าตัดเลยมักได้ margin ไม่ดี; BCS ห้ามใน T4."},{"id":"red1-31","src":"red1","n":31,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"Which of the following is the most common tumor marking used to follow-up a patient who has CA thyroid that is well differentiated?","opts":[["A","serum thyroglobulin"],["B","Serum antimicrosomal antibody"],["C","Serum TSH"],["D","Serum thyrocalcitonin"],["E","No standard tumor marker"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Well-differentiated thyroid CA (papillary/follicular) สร้าง thyroglobulin","e":"หลัง total thyroidectomy ± RAI, serum thyroglobulin (คู่กับ anti-Tg antibody) ใช้ติดตาม recurrence. Calcitonin ใช้ติดตาม medullary thyroid CA; TSH ใช้ปรับ suppression ไม่ใช่ tumor marker."},{"id":"red1-32","src":"red1","n":32,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"35-year-old female presented with neck mass at midline, no tenderness for 4 months.\nPE:\nHEENT: A mass 2 cm in diameter just above hyoid bone. The mass moves with tongue protrusion.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Thyroglossal duct cyst"],["B","Branchial cleft cyst"],["C","Nodular goiter"],["D","Lymphadenopathy"],["E","CA thyroid"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ก้อนแนวกลางคอ เหนือ/ระดับ hyoid ขยับตามการแลบลิ้น","e":"Thyroglossal duct cyst อยู่แนวกลางคอ (มักใกล้ hyoid) เพราะติดกับ foramen cecum ของลิ้นผ่าน tract → เคลื่อนขึ้นเมื่อแลบลิ้น. Branchial cleft cyst อยู่ด้านข้าง ขอบหน้า SCM; goiter/thyroid nodule ขยับตามการกลืนแต่ไม่ตามการแลบลิ้น. รักษา Sistrunk operation."},{"id":"red1-33","src":"red1","n":33,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old man from the northeast region presented with tenderness at his right upper quadrant off and on with fever and chills for 3 months. Sometimes he noticed he had dark yellow urine and yellowish sclera which spontaneously resolved.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","CBD stone"],["B","Liver abscess"],["C","Cholangiocarcinoma"],["D","Chronic cholecystitis"],["E","Periampullary carcinoma"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Charcot's triad เป็นๆหายๆ (ปวด RUQ + ไข้หนาวสั่น + เหลือง) → intermittent obstruction = นิ่ว","e":"Jaundice ที่หายได้เอง (fluctuating) + cholangitis ซ้ำ = CBD stone ทำให้อุดเป็นพักๆ (ในอีสานอาจเป็น primary hepatolithiasis/recurrent pyogenic cholangitis). มะเร็ง (cholangiocarcinoma, periampullary) มักเหลือง progressive ไม่หาย; liver abscess ไม่เหลืองเป็นพักๆ."},{"id":"red1-34","src":"red1","n":34,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 56-year-old-man presented at the outpatient clinic with abdominal discomfort for 3 weeks. The physical examination showed hepatomegaly with an ill-defined mass of 5 cm at the xyphoid. Computed tomography showed a hypovascular mass about 10 cm at the left lobe of the liver with a moderate amount of ascites and no other suspicious primary lesion. The percutaneous tumor biopsy revealed suspected adenocarcinoma.\nWhat is the proper management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Left hepatectomy"],["B","Repeat percutaneous tumor biopsy"],["C","Ascites fluid cytology"],["D","Diagnostic laparoscopy"],["E","Start systemic chemotherapy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Adenocarcinoma ในตับ + ascites (น่าจะ peritoneal spread) = stage IV","e":"ก้อน hypovascular 10 cm + ascites + biopsy adenocarcinoma (เช่น intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma) — ascites ในบริบทนี้คือ peritoneal carcinomatosis = unresectable/stage IV → systemic chemotherapy. Hepatectomy ทำไม่ได้เมื่อมี peritoneal mets; diagnostic laparoscopy ใช้ staging ในคนที่ดูเหมือน resectable. รุ่นพี่วงทั้ง A, E แต่เขียน \"ต้องตอบนี้ stage 4\" ที่ E."},{"id":"red1-35","src":"red1","n":35,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 40-year-old woman is found to have a 2-cm dominant nodule located in the right thyroid lobe.\nWhich one of the following is the most important test in this patient?","opts":[["A","Blood TSH level"],["B","Serum thyroglobulin level"],["C","Ultrasound"],["D","Core needle biopsy"],["E","Fine-needle aspiration biopsy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Thyroid nodule: ขั้นแรกตาม ATA = TSH + ultrasound → แล้วตัดสิน FNA","e":"ATA guideline: nodule ทุกก้อนให้ตรวจ serum TSH ก่อน (ถ้า TSH ต่ำ → radionuclide scan หา hot nodule ซึ่งไม่ต้อง FNA) และทำ thyroid US. เฉลยไฟล์ตอบ A (TSH). FNA ยังเป็นการตรวจที่ \"ให้การวินิจฉัย\" มากที่สุด — ถ้าโจทย์ถาม \"most accurate test to diagnose\" ให้ตอบ FNA."},{"id":"red1-36","src":"red1","n":36,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"Which of the following is/are correct about the treatment of Graves’ disease?","opts":[["A","The best treatment is subtotal thyroidectomy"],["B","Radioactive iodine is the treatment that has the highest rate of recurrence"],["C","The recurrent rate are note different between the treatment with surgery and radioactive iodine"],["D","Exophthalmos will improve after underwent subtotal thyroidectomy"],["E","The recurrent rates are not different between the treatment with surgery and medication."]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"เปรียบเทียบ 3 ทางรักษา Graves: ATD (relapse สูงสุด ~50%) · RAI · surgery (relapse ต่ำสุด)","e":"ATD มี recurrence สูงสุด (30–70%) ส่วน surgery (total/near-total) recurrence ต่ำสุด และ RAI ต่ำ. Exophthalmos ไม่ดีขึ้นแน่นอนหลังผ่าตัด (RAI อาจทำให้แย่ลง). ตัวเลือก E \"recurrence ไม่ต่างระหว่าง surgery กับยา\" จริงๆ แล้วไม่ถูกต้องตามหลักฐานปัจจุบัน — แต่เฉลยไฟล์ = E (ข้อนี้คำถามเก่าและกำกวม; LP วง A ซึ่งก็ไม่ถูกตามปัจจุบันที่ total thyroidectomy แทน subtotal). จำ concept: ATD relapse สูงสุด, surgery ต่ำสุด."},{"id":"red1-37","src":"red1","n":37,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 40-year-old male was in the fasting stage before elective operation.\nWhich one of followings is the first source of energy in this patient?","opts":[["A","Liver"],["B","Body fat"],["C","Gut mucosal"],["D","Adrenal gland"],["E","Skeleton muscle"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ช่วงอดอาหารแรก (< 24 ชม.) ร่างกายใช้ glycogen ก่อน","e":"ระยะ fasting ต้นๆ แหล่งพลังงานแรกคือ hepatic glycogenolysis (glycogen ในตับมี ~ 24–36 ชม.) จากนั้น gluconeogenesis จาก amino acid ของกล้ามเนื้อ และระยะยาวเปลี่ยนเป็น fat/ketone. กล้ามเนื้อมี glycogen แต่ปล่อย glucose เข้ากระแสเลือดไม่ได้ (ไม่มี glucose-6-phosphatase)."},{"id":"red1-38","src":"red1","n":38,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 60-year-old had underlying chronic pancreatitis. This admission, he presented with acute cholecystitis and was admitted for IV antibiotics for 1 week. During admission, he developed steatorrhea and diarrhea after his meals.\nWhich one of the following is the proper initial management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Colonoscopy"],["B","Antispasmodic"],["C","Stool examination"],["D","Switch diet to semi-elemental formula"],["E","Supplement parental nutrition"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Chronic pancreatitis + steatorrhea = pancreatic exocrine insufficiency; แต่ตัวเลือกไม่มี enzyme","e":"Steatorrhea หลังมื้ออาหารในคน chronic pancreatitis คือ maldigestion → ต้องให้ pancreatic enzyme replacement และสูตรอาหารที่ย่อยง่าย. เฉลยไฟล์ตอบ E (supplement parenteral nutrition) — หากตัวเลือกมี semi-elemental formula (D) ก็สมเหตุสมผลเพราะยังใช้ลำไส้ได้ (enteral first). ⚠ ข้อนี้กำกวม จำหลัก: diarrhea ระหว่างได้ ATB ต้องคิดถึง C. difficile ด้วย (stool exam)."},{"id":"red1-39","src":"red1","n":39,"cat":"fluid","stem":"What is the main cation in the intracellular fluid compartment?","opts":[["A","Magnesium"],["B","Potassium"],["C","Sodium"],["D","Protein"],["E","Calcium"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ICF: K⁺ เป็น cation หลัก · ECF: Na⁺","e":"Intracellular fluid มี K⁺ ~140–150 mEq/L เป็น cation หลัก (Mg²⁺ รองลงมา) ส่วน anion หลักคือ phosphate และ protein. Extracellular (plasma + interstitial) ใช้ Na⁺ เป็น cation หลัก."},{"id":"red1-40","src":"red1","n":40,"cat":"fluid","stem":"Which of the following is the condition from rapid correction of hyponatremia?","opts":[["A","Brain edema"],["B","Uncal herniation"],["C","Rebound hyponatremia"],["D","Intraventricular hemorrhage"],["E","Osmotic demyelination syndrome"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"แก้ Na ต่ำเรื้อรังเร็วเกิน → น้ำออกจากเซลล์สมองที่ปรับตัวแล้ว","e":"Rapid correction (> 8–10 mEq/L ใน 24 ชม.) ของ chronic hyponatremia → osmotic demyelination syndrome (central pontine myelinolysis: quadriparesis, dysarthria, locked-in). ส่วน brain edema/herniation เกิดจาก hyponatremia เฉียบพลันเอง หรือจากการแก้ hypernatremia เร็วเกิน."},{"id":"red1-41","src":"red1","n":41,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 60-year-old man underwent abdominoperineal resection. At post-operation the patient received D 5 NSS/2 IV 150 mL/hour and his urine output was 60 mL/hour.\nWhich one of the following is an electrolyte abnormality that has the highest probability to occur in the first 24 hours?","opts":[["A","Hypokalemia"],["B","Hyponatremia"],["C","Hypernatremia"],["D","Hypochloremia"],["E","Hyperglycemia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Postop + ได้ hypotonic fluid (D5NSS/2) ปริมาณมาก + ADH สูงจาก surgical stress","e":"หลังผ่าตัดใหญ่ ADH หลั่งมากจาก stress/pain/nausea → เก็บ free water. ให้ D5 N/2 150 mL/h (มี free water ~ครึ่งหนึ่ง) → dilutional hyponatremia พบบ่อยที่สุดใน 24 ชม.แรก. Hypokalemia ก็เกิดได้แต่ใช้เวลานานกว่า; การใช้ isotonic fluid ในช่วงหลังผ่าตัดช่วยลดปัญหานี้."},{"id":"red1-42","src":"red1","n":42,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 39-year·old underwent exploratory laparotomy from abdominal injury and received a transfusion of 10 units of PRC. At four days post-operation he was confused and drowsy and his BP was 90/60 mmHg.\nLab results glucose 50 mg/dL, Sodium 123 mEq/L, potassium 5.1 mEq/L. Which of the following is the most likely cause of the symptoms in this patient?","opts":[["A","Re-bleeding in intra-abdomen"],["B","5% dextrose in half-strength normal saline after surgery."],["C","Syndrome of inappropriate secretion of ADH"],["D","Acute adrenal in sufficiency"],["E","Severe sepsis"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Hypotension + hypoglycemia + hyponatremia + hyperkalemia = รูปแบบของ adrenal insufficiency","e":"ผู้ป่วยบาดเจ็บรุนแรง/sepsis/เลือดออกมาก อาจเกิด adrenal hemorrhage หรือ critical illness–related corticosteroid insufficiency → BP ต่ำไม่ตอบสนอง, glucose ต่ำ, Na ต่ำ, K สูง, ซึม. Re-bleeding ไม่อธิบาย glucose 50 และ K สูง; SIADH ไม่ทำให้ hypotension/hyperK; sepsis มักน้ำตาลสูง. รักษา hydrocortisone IV."},{"id":"red1-43","src":"red1","n":43,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with gastric outlet obstruction.\nLab results: BUN 40 mg/dL, Cr 1.3 mg/dL, Na+ 140 mEq/L, K+ 2.8 mEq/L, Cl- 82 mEq/L. HCO3 30 mEq/L.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate IV fluid?","opts":[["A","10% D/NSS"],["B","Lactated Ringer 's solution"],["C","Acetated Ringer's solution"],["D","0.9%NaCl"],["E","5%D/N/2 + KCL 40 mEq/1000 mL"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"GOO อาเจียน → เสีย HCl → hypochloremic hypokalemic metabolic alkalosis","e":"แก้ด้วยการให้ Cl⁻ + volume + K⁺: NSS-based fluid ที่มี KCl (เช่น 5%D/N/2 หรือ NSS + KCl 20–40 mEq/L) Cl ที่ได้จะช่วยให้ไตขับ HCO₃⁻. LRS/acetated Ringer มี buffer (lactate/acetate → HCO₃) ทำให้ alkalosis แย่ลงและ Cl ต่ำ. ในตัวเลือก E ให้ทั้ง Cl และ K (ถ้าคนไข้ shock/anuria ให้ NSS ก่อนแล้วค่อยเติม K เมื่อปัสสาวะออก — ดูไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 4)."},{"id":"red1-44","src":"red1","n":44,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 45-year-old female presents with metastasis breast cancer to spine and pelvic bone.\nLab results: BUN 40 mg/dL, Cr 1.1 mg/dL, serum calcium 14mg/dL.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment of electrolyte abnormality in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hemodialysis"],["B","Diuretics"],["C","Normal saline"],["D","Laxatives"],["E","Chemotherapy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Hypercalcemia of malignancy: ขั้นแรก = volume (NSS) → ตามด้วย bisphosphonate","e":"Ca 14 mg/dL (severe) ผู้ป่วยมัก dehydrated จาก nephrogenic DI → NSS 200–300 mL/h เพื่อเพิ่ม GFR และขับ Ca, จากนั้นให้ zoledronic acid ± calcitonin; loop diuretic ใช้เมื่อ volume เกินเท่านั้น. Hemodialysis เฉพาะไตวาย/รุนแรงมาก."},{"id":"red1-45","src":"red1","n":45,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 25-year-old man presented with head injury and pelvic fracture. He received lactated Ringer solution (LRS) IV 100 mL/hour. Three days after the injury he had oliguria (urine 20 mL/hour).\nLab results: Na 120 mEq/L (3 days ago Na 140 mEq/L)\nWhich of the following is the most proper treatment?","opts":[["A","Increase the rate of LRS"],["B","3% NaCl IV"],["C","Demecycline 600 mg/day"],["D","DDAVP"],["E","Discontinue IV infusion"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Head injury + Na ลดลงเร็ว (140 → 120 ใน 3 วัน) + urine น้อย → SIADH; ในสมองบาดเจ็บห้ามปล่อย Na ต่ำ","e":"Acute (< 48 ชม.) symptomatic/severe hyponatremia ในผู้ป่วย TBI เสี่ยง brain edema → ใช้ 3% NaCl (100–150 mL bolus หรือ drip) เป้าเพิ่ม 4–6 mEq/L แล้วไม่เกิน 8–10 ใน 24 ชม. การเพิ่ม LRS (hypotonic เล็กน้อย) ทำให้แย่; fluid restriction เป็นการรักษา SIADH ที่ไม่รุนแรง; DDAVP ทำให้เก็บน้ำเพิ่ม."},{"id":"red1-46","src":"red1","n":46,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"Which one is the most appropriate treatment for grade 1 hemorrhoid?","opts":[["A","Bulk-forming agents with water intake > 2 liter/day"],["B","Osmotic laxative and more water intake"],["C","Rubber band ligation"],["D","Sclerosing therapy"],["E","Colonoscopy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Hemorrhoid grade I = เลือดออกไม่ยื่น → conservative","e":"Grade I–II เริ่มด้วย high-fiber/bulk-forming agent + ดื่มน้ำ > 1.5–2 L/วัน + หลีกเลี่ยงการเบ่ง. ถ้าไม่ดีขึ้นจึงใช้ office procedure: rubber band ligation (grade I–III) หรือ sclerotherapy. Osmotic laxative ไม่ใช่ first-line เท่า fiber."},{"id":"red1-47","src":"red1","n":47,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 45-year-old male has bleeding per anus of 500 mL after hemorrhoidectomy 20 hours ago. He also has dizziness. PE: BP 90/60 mmHg, PR 120/min\nWhich one of the following is/are the most appropriate treatment(s)?","opts":[["A","Reassurance"],["B","NPO, IV fluid, serial Hct"],["C","Vaseline gauze packing, observe rectal bleeding"],["D","Loperamide"],["E","OR to stop the bleeding"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Secondary hemorrhage ต้องแยก: primary (< 24 ชม.) = ปัญหาทางเทคนิค/ligature หลุด → กลับ OR","e":"เลือดออก 500 mL ภายใน 20 ชม. หลัง hemorrhoidectomy + shock (BP 90/60 PR 120) = reactionary/primary hemorrhage จาก pedicle → resuscitate แล้วกลับห้องผ่าตัดเพื่อเย็บหยุดเลือด. Packing/NPO-observe ใช้ในเลือดออกน้อยที่หยุดเอง; secondary hemorrhage (วันที่ 7–14) จาก infection."},{"id":"red1-48","src":"red1","n":48,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. He complained of chest tightness and tenderness at the left side of chest wall. PE: R 24 mm, BP 100/60mmHg. P 110/min. SaO2 92%. decreased BS at left lung. Trachea in midline.\nWhich one of the following is the proper management in this patient?","opts":[["A","IV fluid"],["B","Intubation"],["C","ICD insertion"],["D","O2 therapy"],["E","Needle thoracentesis"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q48-1.jpg"],"t":"Chest trauma เสียงปอดซ้ายลด แต่ trachea กลาง, BP พอได้ = hemothorax/simple pneumothorax ไม่ใช่ tension","e":"ภาพ CXR ซ้ายมี opacity/pneumothorax ร่วมกับ SpO₂ 92% → ใส่ intercostal drainage (ICD) ที่ 5th ICS anterior–mid axillary line. Needle thoracentesis ใช้ใน tension pneumothorax (trachea shift + shock). O₂ และ IV fluid ให้ได้แต่ไม่ใช่ definitive."},{"id":"red1-49","src":"red1","n":49,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 40-year-old man presented with heartburn off and on for 1 year.\nEGD: Esophagitis at the lower part of esophagus but no mass\nWhich one of the following is the most proper management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Prokinetic drug"],["B","Esophagectomy"],["C","Esophageal dilatation"],["D","Esophageal pH monitoring"],["E","Esophageal manometry"]],"key":"D","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"GERD ที่มี esophagitis ยืนยันจาก EGD แล้ว → รักษาด้วยยาเลย (ตัวเลือกไม่มี PPI)","e":"Erosive esophagitis จาก GERD รักษาด้วย PPI 8 สัปดาห์ + lifestyle; ในตัวเลือกที่ไม่มี PPI ยาที่ใกล้สุดคือ prokinetic (เพิ่ม LES tone/gastric emptying). pH monitoring/manometry ใช้เมื่อ EGD ไม่พบ esophagitis แต่อาการไม่ตอบสนอง หรือก่อนทำ fundoplication. เฉลยไฟล์ไฮไลต์ทั้ง A และ D; LP ตอบ A."},{"id":"red1-50","src":"red1","n":50,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 40-year-old man underwent truncal vagotomy and pyloroplasty for treatment of duodenal ulcer perforation 2 months ago. He developed diarrhea which was not related with a meal.\nWhat is the cause of the symptom?","opts":[["A","Steatorrhea"],["B","Blind loop syndrome"],["C","Post vagotomy diarrhea"],["D","Early dumping syndrome"],["E","Late dumping syndrome"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"หลัง truncal vagotomy → diarrhea ที่ \"ไม่สัมพันธ์กับมื้ออาหาร\"","e":"Postvagotomy diarrhea เกิดจากการตัด vagal branches ของลำไส้/ทางเดินน้ำดี → bile acid เข้า colon มาก + motility เปลี่ยน; เป็นเป็นพักๆ ไม่สัมพันธ์มื้ออาหาร. Early dumping เกิด 15–30 นาทีหลังอาหาร (มีอาการ vasomotor + diarrhea); late dumping 2–3 ชม. หลังอาหารเป็น hypoglycemia."},{"id":"red1-51","src":"red1","n":51,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 25-year·old man presented with severe chest pain after he vomited while he was drunk.\nCXR:\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis is?","opts":[["A","Perforated duodenal ulcer"],["B","Spontaneous rupture of the esophagus"],["C","Spontaneous pneumothorax"],["D","Dissecting aortic aneurysm"],["E","Tracheo-esophageal fistula"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q51-1.jpg"],"t":"อาเจียนแรงหลังดื่มเหล้า + เจ็บอก + ภาพ pneumomediastinum/subcutaneous emphysema (Mackler's triad)","e":"Boerhaave syndrome = spontaneous transmural rupture ของ distal esophagus (มักซ้าย posterolateral) จากความดันสูงขณะอาเจียน. CXR: pneumomediastinum (ลูกศรตาม mediastinum), subcutaneous emphysema, left pleural effusion. ยืนยันด้วย water-soluble contrast esophagram/CT. รักษาเร็ว: NPO, ATB, ผ่าตัดซ่อม < 24 ชม."},{"id":"red1-52","src":"red1","n":52,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"Which of the following is the principal organism seen in acute appendicitis?","opts":[["A","Escherichia coli"],["B","Pseudomonas aeruginosa"],["C","Klebsiella species"],["D","Streptococcus species"],["E","Enterococcus species"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Appendicitis เป็น polymicrobial แต่ aerobe ที่พบบ่อยสุด = E. coli, anaerobe = Bacteroides fragilis","e":"เชื้อที่พบมากที่สุดใน acute appendicitis คือ Escherichia coli (aerobic gram-negative) ร่วมกับ Bacteroides fragilis (anaerobe). Pseudomonas, Klebsiella, Streptococcus พบได้แต่น้อยกว่า."},{"id":"red1-53","src":"red1","n":53,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 16-year-old woman had right lower quadrant abdominal pain for 10 hours. This pain started gradually at RLQ without migration or radiation. She has no anorexia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or dysuria. The physical examination revealed BT 37 °C , RLQ tenderness without rebound tenderness, soft abdomen, with normoactive bowel sounds. UA was normal. CBC showed WBC count of 8,000/mm3: and PMN 70%\nWhich of the following is the score of the Alvarado scale?","opts":[["A","2"],["B","4"],["C","6"],["D","8"],["E","10"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Alvarado (MANTRELS 10 คะแนน): Migration1 Anorexia1 N/V1 Tenderness RLQ2 Rebound1 Elevated temp1 Leukocytosis2 Shift1","e":"เคสนี้: ไม่ migrate (0), ไม่มี anorexia (0), ไม่มี N/V (0), RLQ tenderness (2), ไม่มี rebound (0), BT 37 (0), WBC 8,000 (0, ต้อง > 10,000), PMN 70% (0, ต้อง > 75%) → รวม 2. Score ≤ 4 = ไม่น่าเป็น appendicitis."},{"id":"red1-54","src":"red1","n":54,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 55-year-old man complained of enlargement of the Rt. scrotum for 1 month. The scrotum progressively enlarged with minimal pain. PE: Cystic mass 10x6x6 cm at the Rt. scrotum and able to get above the mass. The transillumination test was positive.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Femoral hernia"],["B","Hydrocele"],["C","Lymphadenopathy"],["D","Direct inguinal hernia"],["E","Indirect inguinal hernia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Scrotal mass: get above ได้ไหม · transillumination ไหม · แยก testis ได้ไหม","e":"Cystic mass, get above ได้ (ไม่ได้มาจากช่องท้อง), transillumination positive → hydrocele (น้ำใน tunica vaginalis). Inguinal hernia จะ get above ไม่ได้และมักดันกลับได้/มี cough impulse; femoral hernia อยู่ใต้ inguinal ligament ไม่ลงถุงอัณฑะ."},{"id":"red1-55","src":"red1","n":55,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 40-year-old female presented with a history of a reducible mass at right groin for 1 month. Today she developed a non-reducible mass with pain at the mass. PE: A mass below the inguinal canal and mildly tender.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Femoral hernia"],["B","Richter's hernia"],["C","Pantaloon hernia"],["D","Direct inguinal hernia"],["E","Indirect inguinal hernia"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ผู้หญิง + ก้อนใต้ inguinal ligament (below inguinal canal) + incarcerated ง่าย","e":"Femoral hernia พบในผู้หญิงมากกว่า อยู่ต่ำกว่าและด้านข้างของ pubic tubercle ใต้ inguinal ligament, คอแคบ (femoral ring) → incarceration/strangulation สูงสุดในบรรดา groin hernia → ต้องผ่าตัดเร็ว. Indirect inguinal hernia พบมากสุดในหญิงเช่นกัน แต่อยู่เหนือ ligament."},{"id":"red1-56","src":"red1","n":56,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 30-year-old male presented with right inguinal mas for 2 weeks. He described that the mass was easy to see in the upright position but disappeared in the supine position. Some dull pain was associated with the mass .He say he has no underlying disease. The physical examination revealed a reducible mass at the inguinal region that extended to the scrotal area without any sign of inflammation. The internal ring occlusion test resulted in no mass protrusion at the inguinal area.\nWhat is the standard surgical treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hemioplasty"],["B","Hemiotomy"],["C","Hydrocelcctomy"],["D","Orchidopexy"],["E","Orchidectomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ก้อนยุบเมื่อนอน + ลงถุงอัณฑะ = hernia; internal ring occlusion แล้วไม่โผล่ = indirect","e":"Indirect inguinal hernia ในผู้ใหญ่รักษาด้วย hernioplasty (tension-free mesh repair เช่น Lichtenstein หรือ laparoscopic TEP/TAPP). Herniotomy (ตัดถุงอย่างเดียว) ใช้ในเด็กที่ไม่มี posterior wall weakness. ตัวเลือกในไฟล์สะกด \"Hemioplasty\" = hernioplasty."},{"id":"red1-57","src":"red1","n":57,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 30-year-old man presented with enlargement of the Rt scrotum for a month. The scrotum has been enlarging slowly.\nPE: Cystic mas 10 x 6 x 6 cm at the Rt scrotum and could get above mass. The testis cannot be palpated. The transillumination test is positive.\nWhich one of the following is the proper treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","Core needle biopsy"],["B","Reassure and observe"],["C","Fine needle aspiration"],["D","Trans-scrotal hydrocelectomy"],["E","Trans-inguinal hydrocelectomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Hydrocele ที่ \"คลำ testis ไม่ได้\" → อาจซ่อน testicular tumor → อย่าเข้าทาง scrotum","e":"ถ้าคลำ testis ไม่ได้ต้องทำ scrotal ultrasound เพื่อตัด tumor ก่อน; หากยังสงสัยมะเร็ง การผ่าตัดต้องเข้าทาง inguinal (เพื่อควบคุม spermatic cord ก่อนและไม่ทำให้ lymphatic drainage เปลี่ยน). เฉลย LP = trans-inguinal hydrocelectomy (E); เฉลยไฟล์ Med46 = D (trans-scrotal) ซึ่งใช้ใน hydrocele ธรรมดาที่ testis ปกติ. ห้าม FNA/aspiration."},{"id":"red1-58","src":"red1","n":58,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 72-year-old man was admitted with 25% total body surface area burn. He underwent debridement with skin graft. On postoperative day 4, he developed abdominal distension, nausea and vomiting, obstipation and constipation. The abdominal film showed markedly dilated small bowel & colon with a cecal diameter of 9 cm.\nWhat is the appropriate initial management?","opts":[["A","IV neostigmine"],["B","Rectal tube insertion"],["C","Colonscopic decompression"],["D","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"],["E","NG tube decompression"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Ogilvie (colonic pseudo-obstruction) ในผู้ป่วย burn: cecum 9 cm (< 12 cm) → conservative ก่อน","e":"Initial management: NPO, NG tube decompression, rectal tube, แก้ electrolyte, หยุด opioid/anticholinergic, ให้ลุกเปลี่ยนท่า. ถ้า 24–48 ชม. ไม่ดีขึ้นหรือ cecum > 10–12 cm → IV neostigmine (ต้อง monitor bradycardia) → colonoscopic decompression → surgery เมื่อ perforation/ischemia."},{"id":"red1-59","src":"red1","n":59,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 73-year-old female with infrarenal abdominal aortic aneurysm presented with abdominal pain for 2 weeks. he had anorexia, nausea, and feculent vomiting without fever or obstipation. The physical examination revealed generalized mild tenderness without guarding and moderately abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sound. Acute abdominal series revealed multiple dilatations of the small bowel loops with some gas in a collapsed colon and no gas in the rectum.\nWhat is the provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Cecal cancer"],["B","Rectal cancer"],["C","Paralytic ileus"],["D","Cecal volvulus"],["E","Small bowel ischemia"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Pattern = SBO (SB โป่งหลาย loop, colon ยุบ) ในผู้สูงอายุไม่เคยผ่าตัด + feculent vomiting","e":"ผู้ป่วยไม่มีประวัติผ่าตัด (ไม่มี adhesion) → หาสาเหตุอื่นของ SBO: ก้อนที่ ileocecal valve เช่น cecal cancer ทำให้ภาพเหมือน SBO (ถ้า ileocecal valve competent). Paralytic ileus จะโป่งทั้ง SB และ colon; cecal volvulus เห็น cecum โป่งใหญ่ผิดตำแหน่ง; small bowel ischemia มักปวดมากกว่าที่ตรวจพบ. เฉลยไฟล์ไฮไลต์ A และ C — ตามหลักตอบ A."},{"id":"red1-60","src":"red1","n":60,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 80-year-old male without any history of abdominal symptoms presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. He had anorexia, nausea without vomiting. fever or obstipation. The physical examination revealed soft, not tender, moderate abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds an no rectal mass. The acute abdominal series revealed generalized small bowel and large bowel dilation until sigmoid colon with no gas in the rectum.\nWhat is the provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Rectal cancer"],["B","Diverticulitis"],["C","Paralytic ileus"],["D","Ulcerative colitis"],["E","Sigmoid volvulus"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"LBO (SB + LB โป่ง ถึง sigmoid, ไม่มีลมใน rectum) ในผู้สูงอายุ ไม่มี rectal mass","e":"จุดอุดอยู่ที่ sigmoid → ในผู้สูงอายุ (โดยเฉพาะติดเตียง/ท้องผูกเรื้อรัง) สาเหตุ classic คือ sigmoid volvulus (coffee bean sign). Rectal cancer ตัดได้จาก PR ไม่มีก้อน. ⚠ ไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 32 (โจทย์เกือบเดียวกัน) ไฮไลต์ rectal cancer — ถ้าโจทย์ไม่มีภาพ coffee bean ให้จำว่าสาเหตุ LBO ที่พบบ่อยสุดในผู้ใหญ่ = colorectal cancer; เฉลย LP ข้อนี้ = sigmoid volvulus."},{"id":"red1-61","src":"red1","n":61,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 23-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months age presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea without vomiting. fever or obstipation.\nPE: BT 38 C, PR 110/min\nAbdomen: Localized marked tenderness and guarding at RLQ, mild abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds.\nAcute abdominal series: 3 cm of one loop of small bowel dilation at RLQ with some gas in collapsed colon and no gas in the rectum.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Observe"],["B","IV Antibiotics"],["C","NG decompression and IV resuscitation"],["D","Rectal tube decompression"],["E","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"หลังผ่าตัด 3 เดือน + SB dilatation (partial SBO, ยังมีลมใน colon) → adhesive SBO → conservative ก่อน","e":"Adhesive partial SBO ที่ไม่มี sign ของ strangulation รักษาด้วย NPO + NG decompression + IV resuscitation + ตรวจซ้ำ (± water-soluble contrast). แต่เคสนี้มีไข้ PR 110 + localized guarding RLQ → ต้องระวัง strangulation/abscess; เฉลยไฟล์ C, LP เคยเขียน IV ATB. ไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 52 (ตัวเลือกมี CT) ไฮไลต์ emergency laparotomy. หลักคิด: ไข้ + tachycardia + localized peritonitis = สงสัย strangulation → CT/ผ่าตัด."},{"id":"red1-62","src":"red1","n":62,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"What is the most common manifestation of cryptoglandular abscess?","opts":[["A","Perianal abscess"],["B","Ischiorectal abscess"],["C","Intersphincteric abscess"],["D","Supralevator abscess"],["E","Pelvic abscess"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Cryptoglandular abscess เริ่มที่ anal gland ใน intersphincteric plane แล้วแผ่ลง","e":"ตำแหน่งที่พบบ่อยที่สุด: perianal (~60%) > ischiorectal (~20–30%) > intersphincteric > supralevator. Perianal abscess มาด้วยก้อนแดงร้อนเจ็บที่ anal verge → I&D."},{"id":"red1-63","src":"red1","n":63,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"30-year-old male had a painful lump at his anus for 2 months. He has also had severe pain at his anus for 3 hours. After every defecation, some streaks of fresh blood stained the toilet paper.\nPE: A rubbery brown mass at the posterior midline of the anal verge.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Perianal abscess"],["B","Acute anal fissure"],["C","Chronic anal fissure"],["D","Internal hemorrhoid"],["E","External hemorrhoid"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Fissure ที่ posterior midline + sentinel pile (ก้อนสีน้ำตาลยางๆ) = chronic","e":"อาการปวดมากขณะ/หลังถ่าย + เลือดสดเปื้อนกระดาษ + เป็นมานาน 2 เดือน (> 6–8 สัปดาห์) + sentinel pile ที่ posterior midline = chronic anal fissure. Chronic features: sentinel tag, hypertrophied anal papilla, เห็น internal sphincter fibers. รักษา: topical nitrate/diltiazem, botox, lateral internal sphincterotomy."},{"id":"red1-64","src":"red1","n":64,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 38-year-old female presented with colicky abdominal pain. nausea, and vomiting for 3 days. She has not had a bowel movement for 3 days and any gas for 8 hours. She has history of right salphingo- oophorectomy due to twist of benign ovarian cyst 8 years ago.\nPE: BT 37.7°C, P 108/min. RR 18/min. BP 110/80 mmHg\nAbdomen: Old surgical scare at midline, marked distension and high-pitched bowel sounds, no tenderness. There is no evidence of incisional hernia or inguinal hernia.\nCBC: WBC 11,000, PMN 78% no bands , UA: Specific gravity 1.030, no WBCs or RBCs\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Enteroscopy"],["B","Colonoscopy"],["C","Diagnosis laparoscopy"],["D","IV fluid resuscitation"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"SBO (เคยผ่าตัดท้อง) ไม่มี sign of strangulation → ขั้นแรก resuscitate","e":"Colicky pain + vomiting + obstipation + high-pitched BS + old midline scar = adhesive SBO. ไม่มี tenderness/fever สูง → เริ่มด้วย IV fluid resuscitation (UA SG 1.030 = dehydrated), NPO, NG decompression, แก้ electrolyte และตรวจซ้ำ. ผ่าตัดเมื่อมี strangulation หรือไม่ดีขึ้นใน 48–72 ชม."},{"id":"red1-65","src":"red1","n":65,"cat":"infection","stem":"What is the appropriate duration of antimicrobial prophylaxis for exploratory laparotomy in complete colonic obstruction?","opts":[["A","No need ATB prophylaxis"],["B","At admission"],["C","Within 30 minutes prior to creation of the incision"],["D","More than 30 minutes prior to creation of the incision"],["E","No further antibiotic needs after close incision"]],"key":"D","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Prophylactic ATB ต้องอยู่ในเนื้อเยื่อขณะลงมีด → ให้ภายใน 60 นาทีก่อน incision","e":"Prophylaxis: ให้ภายใน 60 นาที (vancomycin/fluoroquinolone 120 นาที) ก่อน skin incision; ไม่ต้องให้ตั้งแต่ admit. Complete colonic obstruction = ผ่าตัดลำไส้ที่สกปรก (clean-contaminated/contaminated) จึงต้องให้. เฉลยในไฟล์ขัดกัน (Med46 = D, LP วง \"within 30 min\"/ข้อความในไฟล์คลุมเครือ). ตามหลัก \"within 60 min\" ตัวเลือกที่ตรงที่สุดคือ C (ให้ใกล้เวลา incision)."},{"id":"red1-66","src":"red1","n":66,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 65-year-old previously healthy man presents with severe abdominal pain that came on suddenly. He has abdominal tenderness and guarding in all four quadrants on physical examination.\nAcute abdomen series:\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Observation"],["B","Abdominal ultrasound"],["C","Abdominal computed tomography"],["D","Upper gastrointestinal study"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q66-1.jpg"],"t":"Sudden severe abdominal pain + guarding ทั้ง 4 quadrant (generalized peritonitis) + ฟิล์ม free air","e":"Acute abdomen series เห็น pneumoperitoneum (free air ใต้กระบังลม) + generalized peritonitis = hollow viscus perforation (เช่น perforated peptic ulcer) → resuscitate + ATB + exploratory laparotomy. ไม่ต้อง CT/U/S เพิ่มเมื่อวินิจฉัยได้จากคลินิกและฟิล์ม."},{"id":"red1-67","src":"red1","n":67,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"One day before the midpoint her menstrual cycle, 17-year-old female suddenly developed pain in the right lower quadrant of the abdomen. Abdominal examination reveals tenderness in the right lower quadrant and a rectal examination also revealed right-sided tenderness. Her temperature is 37.2°C and her leukocyte count is 100/mm3, PMN 60%. The most likely diagnosis","opts":[["A","Acute appendicitis"],["B","Pelvic inflammatory disease"],["C","Meckel diverticulitis"],["D","Infection of the urinary tract"],["E","Ruptured graafian follicle"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"ปวด RLQ เฉียบพลัน \"กลางรอบเดือน\" + ไม่มีไข้ + WBC ปกติ = mittelschmerz","e":"Ruptured graafian follicle (mittelschmerz) เกิดช่วง ovulation (กลางรอบ) ปวดทันที ไม่มีไข้/leukocytosis หายเองใน 24–48 ชม. Appendicitis ปวดค่อยเป็นค่อยไป + anorexia + ไข้ + WBC สูง; PID มีไข้ discharge cervical motion tenderness."},{"id":"red1-68","src":"red1","n":68,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 65-year-old previously healthy man presents with severe left lower quadrant abdominal pain for 1 day, fever of 38.5 °C and nausea and vomiting. Laboratory include a WBC count of 16,300 with 7 % bands. On physical examination his abdomen is soft, but he has marked tenderness in the left lower quadrant.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Serial physical examination"],["B","Abdominal ultrasound"],["C","Abdominal computed tomography"],["D","Colonoscopy"],["E","Barium enema"]],"key":"D","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"สงสัย acute diverticulitis (LLQ pain + fever + leukocytosis ในผู้สูงอายุ) → CT abdomen","e":"CT with contrast เป็น investigation of choice: ยืนยันวินิจฉัยและจัด Hinchey (abscess/perforation). Colonoscopy และ barium enema ห้ามในระยะ acute (เสี่ยง perforation) ทำหลังหาย 6–8 สัปดาห์เพื่อตัดมะเร็ง. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = D ซึ่งขัดหลัก; ตอบ C."},{"id":"red1-69","src":"red1","n":69,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 58-year-old male was in the hospital on postoperative day 5 after he underwent a laparoscopic low anterior resection. He had no bowel movement and had not passed gas despite normal electrolytes. NG content is 700 mL/day. Today he developed a high-grade fever. PE: BT 39°C, abdominal distension, and hypoactive bowel sound . Other exams are normal.\nWhat is the most likely cause of this condition?","opts":[["A","Atelectasis"],["B","Deep surgical site infection"],["C","Iliac vein thrombosis"],["D","Urinary tract infection"],["E","Intra-abdominal collection"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"ไข้ตาม \"วัน\" หลังผ่าตัด: POD5 + ileus ไม่หาย + ท้องอืด หลัง anastomosis = leak/collection","e":"Fever POD 5–7 หลัง low anterior resection ที่ไม่มีลม/อุจจาระ + NG ออกมาก + ท้องอืด = anastomotic leak/intra-abdominal abscess → CT abdomen + ATB ± percutaneous drainage/ผ่าตัด. Atelectasis ทำให้ไข้ POD 1–2; deep SSI มักเห็นแผลแดงบวม; UTI/DVT ไม่ทำให้ ileus."},{"id":"red1-70","src":"red1","n":70,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 50-year-old man presented with progressive jaundice. Work up: U/S before admission shows normal liver and no space-occupying lesion with IHD and CBD dilatation. Suspected periampullary CA. He underwent ERCP and found an ampullary mass. Three-day post-ERCP he revisited with fever and RUQ pain.\nCT abdomen: A 5-cm loculated rim enhancing hypodense lesion at right lobe of liver.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Pyogenic liver abscess"],["B","Echinococcal cyst"],["C","Liver metastasis"],["D","Hepatocellular carcinoma"],["E","Hemangioma"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"หลัง ERCP (มี biliary instrumentation) → ไข้ + ก้อน rim-enhancing loculated ในตับ","e":"Ascending cholangitis หลัง ERCP/biliary obstruction เป็นสาเหตุหลักของ pyogenic liver abscess. CT: hypodense, rim enhancement, loculated (cluster sign). Echinococcal cyst มี daughter cyst/calcified wall; metastasis ไม่มาพร้อมไข้เฉียบพลัน; HCC มี arterial enhancement + washout."},{"id":"red1-71","src":"red1","n":71,"cat":"hpb","stem":"What is TRUE regarding the pathophysiology of biliary colic from gallstone?","opts":[["A","The pain develops when a stone drops and causes obstruction of the common bile duct."],["B","The pain is the result of the progressive increase of tensions in the gallbladder wall."],["C","The biliary colic occurs only in secondary bacterial infections due to bile stasis"],["D","The biliary colic occurs when the gallbladder becomes nonfunctioning with gross transmural fibrosis and adhesions to nearby structures."],["E","All of the above."]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Biliary colic = gallbladder หดตัวไล่น้ำดีผ่าน cystic duct ที่ถูกนิ่วอุดชั่วคราว","e":"นิ่วอุด cystic duct/Hartmann pouch ขณะ GB หดตัว (หลังอาหารมัน, CCK) → ความดัน/แรงตึงผนัง GB เพิ่มขึ้นเรื่อยๆ → ปวด (visceral) ที่ epigastrium/RUQ 30 นาที–หลายชม. แล้วหายเมื่อนิ่วหลุดกลับ. ไม่จำเป็นต้องมี infection และไม่ใช่จากนิ่วใน CBD (นั่นคือ choledocholithiasis)."},{"id":"red1-72","src":"red1","n":72,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 69-year-old male underwent laparoscopic cholecystectomy. She developed abdominal pain, distension, and fever on postoperative day 2.\nPE: T 38.5°C, R 22/min, BP 160/90 mmHg, P 118/min, mild jaundice, moderate abdominal distension and right upper quadrant tenderness without guarding, hypoactive bowel sound.\nCBC: WBC 13,200 /cu.mm,N 92%, L 3%, Hb 13 g/dL Hct 39%, Plt 136,000 /microliter;\nLFTs: DB 1.2 mg/dL,TB 2.1 mg/dL, AST 30 units, ALT 30 units, ALP 165 U/L, TP 5 gm/dL, Alb 2 gm/dL\nWhat is the most possible surgical complication in this patient?","opts":[["A","Bile duct injury"],["B","Hepatic vascular injury"],["C","Liver parenchymal injury"],["D","Small bowel perforation"],["E","Gastric perforation"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"POD2 หลัง LC: ปวด + ท้องอืด + ไข้ + เหลือง (DB ขึ้น, ALP สูง) → bile leak/bile duct injury","e":"Bile duct injury/bile leak หลัง laparoscopic cholecystectomy: biloma/bile peritonitis → ปวด ท้องอืด ileus ไข้ และ bilirubin สูงจากการดูดซึมน้ำดีกลับทาง peritoneum หรือท่อตีบ. วินิจฉัยด้วย U/S/CT หา collection → percutaneous drain → MRCP/ERCP stent. Vascular injury จะมี transaminase สูงมาก; bowel perforation มักไม่มี jaundice."},{"id":"red1-73","src":"red1","n":73,"cat":"hpb","stem":"The annual check-up of a 50-year-old female at a private hospital detected DM and gallstones. She has no other abdominal signs or symptoms.\nWhat is the appropriate suggestion for her gallstones?","opts":[["A","Medical treatment"],["B","Observe abdominal symptoms"],["C","Extracorporeal Shock Wave Lithotripsy"],["D","Laparoscopic cholecystectomy"],["E","Open cholecystectomy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Asymptomatic gallstone → ส่วนใหญ่ observe (แม้เป็น DM)","e":"นิ่วไม่มีอาการ: ความเสี่ยงเกิดอาการ ~1–2%/ปี → ไม่ต้องผ่าตัด prophylactic ยกเว้นกลุ่มเสี่ยงสูง (porcelain GB, นิ่ว > 3 cm, polyp > 1 cm ร่วม, sickle cell, ไปอยู่ที่ห่างไกลการแพทย์). DM เคยถูกจัดเป็นข้อบ่งชี้แต่ปัจจุบันไม่แนะนำแล้ว → ให้ observe อาการและสอนอาการเตือน."},{"id":"red1-74","src":"red1","n":74,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 45-year·old man present with upper abdominal pain for 1 day.The physical examination reveal tachycardia, not pale no icteric sclera with dry mucous membranes. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, no palpable mass, and hypoactive bowel sounds. Blood chemistry: amylase 700 IU/L. LFT : T.bil 0.5 mg/dl, D.bil 0.2 mg/dL, ALP 300 U/\nWhich one of the following is the next step in management?","opts":[["A","Urine amylase"],["B","Ultrasound abdomen"],["C","Total parenteral nutrition"],["D","Broad-spectrum antibiotics"],["E","Endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ปวด epigastrium + amylase สูง (> 3 เท่า) = acute pancreatitis → หาสาเหตุด้วย U/S","e":"Acute pancreatitis ทุกรายต้องทำ abdominal ultrasound เพื่อหา gallstone (สาเหตุบ่อยสุด) ตั้งแต่แรก. Urine amylase ไม่จำเป็น; ไม่ให้ prophylactic antibiotic; TPN ไม่ใช่ (enteral ดีกว่า); ERCP ทำเมื่อมี cholangitis หรือ CBD obstruction ต่อเนื่อง."},{"id":"red1-75","src":"red1","n":75,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 57-year-old man presents with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 2 days. He has not experienced this type of pain before. The physical examination reveals a high grade fever and tachycardia. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness with guarding and hypoactive bowel sounds.\nBlood chemistry: amylase 1000 IU/L. CT abdomen revealed a 4-cm collection of air and debris with rim enhancement at body and tail of pancreas.\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Conservative treatment"],["B","Percutaneous drainage"],["C","Endoscopic cyst gastrotomy"],["D","Video-assisted retroperitoneal debridement"],["E","Open necrosectomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Collection ของ \"air + debris + rim enhancement\" ที่ 2 วัน → ยังเป็นระยะแรก (< 4 สัปดาห์)","e":"เป็น acute pancreatitis วันที่ 2 → collection ระยะนี้เป็น acute necrotic collection ยังไม่ walled-off; หลัก step-up: เริ่ม conservative (resuscitation, ATB ถ้าสงสัย infected necrosis), ชะลอการ intervention ถึง ≥ 4 สัปดาห์เมื่อ walled-off necrosis แล้ว จึงทำ percutaneous/endoscopic drainage → VARD/necrosectomy. เฉลยไฟล์ = A; LP วง B (percutaneous drainage ตาม gas = infected necrosis) — หลักฐานปัจจุบันชะลอ drainage หากผู้ป่วยไม่ทรุด."},{"id":"red1-76","src":"red1","n":76,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 57-year-old man presents with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 1 day. Physical examination reveals good consciousness, T 38 °C , P 100/min, RR 24/min, BP 120/80 mmHg. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds.\nCBC/Blood chemistries: Hb 12 gm%, WBC 13,000/mm 3 , platelet 300,000/mm 3 , BUN 29 mg%, Cr 1.5 mg%, and amylase 1,500 IU/L\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Nasogastric intubation"],["B","Intravenous fluid"],["C","Intravenous antibiotics"],["D","Endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography"],["E","Laparotomy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Acute pancreatitis ขั้นแรกที่สำคัญสุด = aggressive (goal-directed) IV fluid","e":"Pancreatitis + BUN/Cr สูง (hemoconcentration, third spacing) → IV crystalloid (LRS) ตาม goal-directed. ไม่ต้องให้ prophylactic ATB; NG tube เฉพาะอาเจียนมาก/ileus; ERCP เฉพาะ cholangitis; ผ่าตัดไม่ใช่การรักษาระยะแรก."},{"id":"red1-77","src":"red1","n":77,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 73-year-old female presented with abdominal distension and massive bloody stool. NG lavage reveals bile content without blood. Vital signs show BP110/70 mmHg and PR 100/min.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Bleeding diverticulosis"],["B","Malignant neoplasm of rectum"],["C","ln1emal hemorrhoid"],["D","Anal fissure"],["E","Diverticulitis"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"LGIB ใหญ่ (NG ได้ bile ไม่มีเลือด = ตัด UGIB) ในผู้สูงอายุ ไม่ปวดท้อง","e":"Massive painless hematochezia ในผู้สูงอายุ: สาเหตุบ่อยสุด diverticular bleeding (diverticulosis) และ angiodysplasia. CA rectum เลือดออกน้อยๆ เรื้อรัง; hemorrhoid/fissure เลือดออกน้อยไม่ทำให้ hemodynamic เปลี่ยน; diverticulitis มักไม่ค่อยมีเลือดออกมาก."},{"id":"red1-78","src":"red1","n":78,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 73-year-old female presented at the hospital with abdominal distension and massive bloody stool. The physical examination shows BP 90/60 mmHg and PR 130/min. NG lavngc reveals bile content without blood. After 2 liters of crystalloid fluid resuscitation and 2 units of PRC transfusion, the vital signs showed BP 110/70 mmHg and PR 100/min. The patient also excreted an additional 200 mL of maroon stool during resuscitation.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","RBC scan"],["B","Colonoscopy"],["C","Mesenteric angiography"],["D","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"],["E","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Massive LGIB ที่ resuscitate แล้ว \"stable\" → colonoscopy (หลัง bowel prep)","e":"ACG: ผู้ป่วย LGIB ที่ hemodynamically stable หลัง resuscitate → colonoscopy ภายใน 24 ชม. หลัง rapid bowel prep (ทั้งวินิจฉัยและรักษา). ถ้ายัง unstable/เลือดออกต่อเนื่อง → CTA → angiographic embolization. Exploratory laparotomy เป็นทางสุดท้าย."},{"id":"red1-79","src":"red1","n":79,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 60-year-old male presented at the hospital with LLQ pain for 1 day.\nPE: T 38.5 °C, P 100/min\nAbd: Localized guarding at LLQ, Hypoactive bowel sounds PR: no mass\nAcute abdomen series: no free air, generalized small bowel dilatation without air-fluid level\nWhat is the most appropriate investigation?","opts":[["A","Colonoscopy"],["B","Barium enema"],["C","Ultrasonography"],["D","Diagnostic laparoscopy"],["E","Abdominal CT"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"LLQ pain + ไข้ + localized guarding ในผู้สูงอายุ = สงสัย diverticulitis → CT","e":"CT abdomen ยืนยัน diverticulitis และดู complication (abscess/perforation) เพื่อเลือกรักษา (ATB vs drainage vs surgery). ฟิล์มเห็น SB dilatation จาก ileus ข้างเคียง. Colonoscopy/barium enema ห้ามในระยะ acute; U/S ดูลำไส้ใหญ่ได้จำกัด."},{"id":"red1-80","src":"red1","n":80,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 60-year-old women with poorly controlled hypertension and a history of myocardiaI infarction presents with incidental finding of abdominal aortic aneurysm that is 4 cm in maximal diameter and 5.5 cm in lengths.\nWhat is the most appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","MRI abdomen"],["B","Exercise stress test"],["C","Echocardiography"],["D","CTA aorta"],["E","F/U Ultrasound"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"AAA ขนาด 4 cm ไม่มีอาการ → ยังไม่ถึงเกณฑ์ผ่าตัด (ผู้หญิง ≥ 5.0, ผู้ชาย ≥ 5.5 cm)","e":"AAA เล็ก ไม่มีอาการ → surveillance ด้วย ultrasound (4.0–4.9 cm ทุก 12 เดือน), คุม BP, เลิกบุหรี่, statin. Cardiac workup (echo/stress test) และ CTA ทำเมื่อวางแผนผ่าตัด."},{"id":"red1-81","src":"red1","n":81,"cat":"vascular","stem":"All of the following symptoms of chronic femoropopliteal vein thrombosis at the right leg are correct EXCEPT","opts":[["A","The right leg is more swollen than the left leg"],["B","Hyperpigmentation at the right median malleolus region of the right leg"],["C","Varicose vein is much more one the right side"],["D","Chronic wound with serum oozing at the right median malleolus"],["E","Tenderness along right superficial femoral vein"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Chronic DVT → post-thrombotic syndrome (venous hypertension) ไม่ใช่การอักเสบเฉียบพลัน","e":"อาการ chronic femoropopliteal DVT: ขาบวมกว่าข้างดี, hyperpigmentation/lipodermatosclerosis ที่ medial malleolus, secondary varicose vein, venous ulcer มี serous discharge. Tenderness ตามแนว vein เป็นลักษณะของ acute thrombosis/thrombophlebitis จึงไม่ใช่."},{"id":"red1-82","src":"red1","n":82,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 36-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash.\nAirway: clear\nBreathing: bilateral equal air entry, RR 24/min\nCirculation: BP 190/100 mmHg, PR 60 bpm\nDisability: hematoma at forehead GCS 6 (E1V2M3), dilated right pupil\nExposure/Environment: no obvious injury\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management in the next step?","opts":[["A","CT scan brain"],["B","Intubate and ventilate"],["C","Treatment of hypertension"],["D","Fluid resuscitation"],["E","Film trauma series"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"GCS ≤ 8 + pupil ขยายข้างเดียว + Cushing (BP สูง HR ช้า) → secure airway ก่อน","e":"GCS 6 = severe TBI → intubate + ventilate (normocapnia PaCO₂ 35–40, ใช้ hyperventilation ชั่วคราวเฉพาะ herniation) แล้วค่อย CT brain. BP สูง + HR ช้า = Cushing reflex จาก ICP สูง ห้ามลด BP; ไม่ต้อง fluid resuscitation เพราะไม่ shock."},{"id":"red1-83","src":"red1","n":83,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 40-year-old male suffered from a motorcycle crash 30 min PTA. His motor response of Glasgow Coma Scale was according to the figure.\nWhat is his M score in GCS?","opts":[["A","1"],["B","2"],["C","3"],["D","4"],["E","5"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q83-1.jpg"],"t":"ดูรูป: แขนเหยียดตรง + หมุนเข้า (extension) = M2","e":"GCS motor: 6 obey, 5 localize, 4 withdraw (normal flexion), 3 abnormal flexion (decorticate), 2 extension (decerebrate), 1 none. รูปแสดงแขนเหยียดและหมุนเข้าด้านในเมื่อกระตุ้น = decerebrate posturing = M2."},{"id":"red1-84","src":"red1","n":84,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 30-year-old male was involved in a motorcycle crash. He has good consciousness but is dyspneic with sweating. The vital signs are BP 70/50 mmHg, P 140/min, R 40/min, and SaO2 85%. Chest exam results show decreased breath sounds at right lung with dullness on percussion. Right ICD reveals 1,500 mL of fresh blood.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Clamp ICD"],["B","Infuse NSS until hemodynamics are stable"],["C","Insert another ICD"],["D","Connecting ICD to thoracic suction"],["E","Thoracotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Massive hemothorax: ICD ได้เลือด ≥ 1,500 mL ทันที (หรือ > 200 mL/h × 2–4 ชม.) + unstable → thoracotomy","e":"เกณฑ์ ATLS สำหรับ thoracotomy: initial drainage ≥ 1,500 mL, ต่อเนื่อง > 200 mL/h นาน 2–4 ชม., หรือต้องให้เลือดต่อเนื่อง/ hemodynamic ไม่ stable. Clamp ICD ไม่ช่วย; ใส่ ICD อีกเส้นไม่หยุดเลือด; ให้เลือด (ไม่ใช่ NSS อย่างเดียว) ระหว่างไป OR."},{"id":"red1-85","src":"red1","n":85,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. He complained of tenderness at the Rt side of the chest wall.\nPE: RR 30/min, Sa0, 94%, equal breath sounds at both lungs.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Lung contusion"],["B","Hemothorax"],["C","Massive hemothorax"],["D","Thoracic aortic injury"],["E","Diaphragmatic injury"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q85-1.jpg"],"t":"CXR: patchy opacity ไม่ตาม segment ใต้บริเวณที่ถูกกระแทก + breath sound เท่ากัน","e":"Lung contusion เห็นเป็น nonsegmental airspace opacity ใต้ตำแหน่งกระแทกภายใน 6 ชม. แรก, เสียงปอดยังเท่ากัน (ไม่มีของเหลวในช่องปอด). Hemothorax จะเห็น meniscus/opacity ที่ base และ breath sound ลด; aortic injury → widened mediastinum."},{"id":"red1-86","src":"red1","n":86,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 20-year-old male was involved in a motorcycle crash. He is unconscious with massive bleeding per nose, mouth, and both ears. The vital signs are BP 80/50 mmHg, P 140/min, R 30/min, and SaO2 85%. Chest exam: Decreased breath sounds at the right lung.\nWhat should be the most appropriate next step?","opts":[["A","Insert ICD"],["B","Stop the bleeding"],["C","Infuse 1-2 L of NSS"],["D","Apply cervical collar"],["E","Endotracheal intubation"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Unconscious + เลือดในปาก/จมูก + SpO₂ 85% → Airway ก่อน","e":"ATLS ABCDE: ผู้ป่วยหมดสติ เลือดท่วม airway SpO₂ 85% → endotracheal intubation (พร้อม c-spine protection). ICD สำหรับ breath sound ลดเป็นขั้น B ที่ตามมา; ห้ามเลือด/ให้ fluid เป็น C. (ใส่ cervical collar ทำร่วมกับการจัดการ airway แต่ไม่ใช่ next step ที่ช่วยชีวิตที่สุด)"},{"id":"red1-87","src":"red1","n":87,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 25-year-old man was stabbed at Rt thoracoabdominal area.\nWhich one of the following diagnostic tests should NOT be performed?","opts":[["A","Local wound exploration"],["B","eFAST"],["C","DPL"],["D","CT scan"],["E","Serial physical examination"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Thoracoabdominal stab: การ probe แผลเสี่ยงเปิดเข้า pleura → pneumothorax และประเมิน diaphragm ไม่ได้","e":"Local wound exploration ใช้กับแผลแทงที่ anterior abdominal wall เท่านั้น; ห้ามทำในแผล thoracoabdominal/flank/back เพราะอาจทำให้เกิด pneumothorax และประเมินไม่ได้. ใช้ eFAST, CT, DPL, serial exam หรือ diagnostic laparoscopy (ดู diaphragm injury) แทน."},{"id":"red1-88","src":"red1","n":88,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 23-year-old female was stabbed at the abdomen.\nPE: A 2-cm wound at paraumbilicus with omentum at the wound.\nVital signs: BP 100/50 mmHg, PR 100 bpm, RR 26/min\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Observe abdominal sign"],["B","DPL"],["C","CT scan abdomen"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy"],["E","Resuscitation with NSS IV 2 L free flow"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Stab wound + evisceration (omentum โผล่) = indication ผ่าตัด","e":"ข้อบ่งชี้ laparotomy ในแผลแทงท้อง: hemodynamic unstable, peritonitis, evisceration, GI bleeding/เลือดใน NG/rectum. แผลที่มี omentum โผล่ → exploratory laparotomy. Resuscitate ไปพร้อมกันแต่ไม่ต้อง CT/DPL."},{"id":"red1-89","src":"red1","n":89,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 26-year-old man sustained injuries in a motor bike injury. His abdomen was hit by the handlebar.\nPE: BP 100/60 mmHg, Pulse 120/min, RR 22/min, Abdomen: generalized guarding rigidity. FAST-ve\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Observe"],["B","Ultrasound abdomen"],["C","CT abdomen"],["D","Peritoneal lavage"],["E","Emergency laparotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Handlebar injury + BP ต่ำ PR 120 + generalized guarding rigidity → ผ่าตัดเลย","e":"Peritonitis + shock หลัง blunt abdominal trauma = hollow viscus/mesenteric injury → emergency laparotomy. FAST ลบไม่ตัด hollow viscus injury (handlebar = pancreas, duodenum, small bowel). ไม่ควรส่ง CT ในคนไม่ stable."},{"id":"red1-90","src":"red1","n":90,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 35-year-old male was involved in a motorcycle crash. He has good consciousness with abdominal pain and distension. The vital signs are BP 90/60 mmHg, P 120/min, R 30/min. FAST (focused abdominal sonography for trauma) shows free fluid in the abdomen. Repeated BP is 80/50 mmHg.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Pelvic binding"],["B","CT scan abdomen"],["C","Exploratory laparotomy"],["D","Diagnostic peritoneal lavage"],["E","Infuse NSS until hemodynamics are stable"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"FAST + และ BP ยังตกหลัง resuscitate = non-responder → OR","e":"Hemoperitoneum (FAST +) + hypotension ที่ไม่ตอบสนอง → exploratory laparotomy (damage control). CT ห้ามในคน unstable; DPL ไม่จำเป็นเมื่อ FAST บอกแล้ว; pelvic binding ใช้เมื่อสงสัย pelvic fracture. การให้ NSS \"จน stable\" ผิดหลัก (permissive hypotension + blood)."},{"id":"red1-91","src":"red1","n":91,"cat":"infection","stem":"How would you describe this wound?","opts":[["A","Flap wound"],["B","Puncture wound"],["C","Abrasion wound"],["D","Avulsion wound"],["E","Laceration wound"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s1-q91-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: ผิวถลอกเป็นแผ่นแดง ตื้น มีจุดเลือดซึม ไม่มีขอบแผลฉีก","e":"Abrasion = การสูญเสียผิวหนังชั้นตื้นจากการขูด/ครูด มีเลือดซึมเป็นจุดๆ. Laceration = ผิวฉีกขาดเป็นแนวขอบไม่เรียบ; avulsion = ผิวหลุดออก/แฟลปฉีกถึงชั้นลึก; puncture = แผลรูเล็กลึก. รักษา: ล้างเอาสิ่งสกปรกออก (ป้องกัน traumatic tattoo) + moist dressing."},{"id":"red1-92","src":"red1","n":92,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 40-year-old male stepped on a nail 1 hour ago. He has a wound at his Rt foot. He has a history of tetanus immunization 3 times in the past year.\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Debridement + wet dressing"],["B","Debridement + wet dressing + TT x1 dose"],["C","Irrigate with Betadine + Antibiotics +TT x1 dose"],["D","Debridement + irrigate with Betadine + Primary wound closure"],["E","Debridement +Wet dressing +Antibiotics + TT x1 dose"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"TT ครบ 3 ครั้งภายใน 1 ปี → ไม่ต้องให้ TT; puncture wound → debride + wet dressing ไม่เย็บ","e":"CDC: ผู้ได้ ≥ 3 doses ให้ booster เมื่อแผลสกปรกและ dose สุดท้าย > 5 ปี → คนนี้ไม่ต้องให้ TT. แผลตะปูตำเท้า: debride/เปิดแผล ล้าง wet dressing ไม่ปิดแผล, ATB ไม่จำเป็นถ้าไม่ติดเชื้อ. LP วง A (เฉลยเดิมกา B ซึ่งขัด CDC)."},{"id":"red1-93","src":"red1","n":93,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old man underwent right lobe hepatectomy. At postoperative day 1 he developed a fever.\nPE: BT 38.5°C, RR 18/min, BP 110/60 mmHg, PR 82/min\nLungs: clear\nAbdomen: good looking surgical site, soft, not tender, JP drain 100 mL of serosanguinous fluid\nWhat is the most likely cause of fever in this patient?","opts":[["A","Sepsis"],["B","Liver failure"],["C","Lung atelectasis"],["D","Pleural effusion"],["E","Intraabdominal collection"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ไข้ POD 1 + ปอดใส + แผลดี + drain ปกติ → atelectasis (Wind)","e":"ไข้ 24–48 ชม.แรกหลังผ่าตัดช่องท้องส่วนบน (hepatectomy, ปวดแผลหายใจตื้น) ส่วนใหญ่เป็น atelectasis/inflammatory response (5W: Wind POD1–2, Water/UTI POD3–5, Wound POD5–7, Walk/DVT POD5+, Wonder drug). Collection/sepsis มักเกิดหลัง POD 4–5. LP แก้เป็น C (เฉลยเดิมกา collection)."},{"id":"red1-94","src":"red1","n":94,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 69-year-old female with symptomatic gallstone. She underwent laparoscopic cholecystectomy. She developed abdominal pain, distension, and fever on postoperative day 2. The physical examination revealed T 38.5°C, R 22/min, BP 160/90 mmHg, P 118/min, mild jaundice, moderate abdominal distension, right upper quadrant tenderness without guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds. CBC: WBC 13.2 x 10°/L, N 92%, L 3%, Hb 13 g/dL, Hct 39%, Plt 136,000 /mL, LFTs: DB 1.2 mg/dL, TB 2.1 mg/dL, AST 30 units, ALT 30 units, ALP 165 U/L, TP 5 gm/dL, Alb 2 gm/dL\nWhat is the most appropriate initial management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Early enteral diet and oral rehydration"],["B","NPO, IV fluid hydration, Serial examination."],["C","Parenteral nutrition and IV fluid hydration."],["D","NPO, IV fluid resuscitation, parenteral antibiotic."],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"สงสัย bile leak/bile duct injury + SIRS (ไข้ HR 118 WBC สูง) → resuscitate + ATB ก่อน imaging/drain","e":"เริ่ม NPO, IV fluid resuscitation, parenteral broad-spectrum ATB → U/S/CT หา biloma → percutaneous drainage → MRCP/ERCP (sphincterotomy/stent). Exploratory laparotomy เฉพาะ bile peritonitis ทั่วท้อง/unstable หรือ major duct transection ที่ต้องซ่อม."},{"id":"red1-95","src":"red1","n":95,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 60-year-old female presented with anorexia, progressive headache, and nausea for 1 week. She was recently diagnosed with squamous cell carcinoma of the esophagus. She has no signs of volume deficit on physical examination. The neurological exam revealed normal and no focal neurological deficit. Her BW is 50 kg. Laboratory results: BUN 25 ( 5-23 mg%), Creatinine 0.73 (0.4-1.1 mg%), Na 112 (136-150 mmol/L), K 3.81 (3.5-5.1 mmol/L), CI 95 (98-106 mmol/L), T-CO, 22.2 (22-29 mmol/L), blood glucose 250 mg%\nWhat is the most serious consequence of the treatment electrolyte imbalance in this patient?","opts":[["A","Brain swelling and herniation"],["B","Osmotic demyelination syndrome"],["C","Syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone (SIADH)"],["D","Central diabetic insipidus"],["E","Papilledema"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Chronic severe hyponatremia (Na 112) ที่ไม่มีอาการรุนแรง → ความเสี่ยงหลักของ \"การรักษา\" คือแก้เร็วเกิน","e":"Hyponatremia เป็นมาหลายวัน (chronic) ในผู้ป่วยมะเร็ง (SIADH, ขาดอาหาร) + เสี่ยงสูง (Na < 120, malnutrition) → ถ้าแก้เร็ว > 8 mEq/L/24 ชม. เกิด osmotic demyelination syndrome. Brain swelling/herniation เป็นผลของ hyponatremia เอง ไม่ใช่ของการรักษา."},{"id":"red1-96","src":"red1","n":96,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"An 18-year-old man had right lower quadrant abdominal pain for 12 hours. This pain started gradually at the umbilical area which then migrated to the RLQ which has progressively worsened. He also has anorexia, nausea, and vomiting. He does not have chills, diarrhea or dysuria. The physical examination revealed BT38°C, RLQ tenderness with rebound tenderness, no palpable masses, soft abdomen with hypoactive bowel sounds. UA was normal. CBC showed WBC count of 12,000 /mm3 and PMN 80%.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Serial physical examination"],["B","Abdominal ultrasonography"],["C","Abdominal computed tomography"],["D","Cholecystectomy"],["E","Appendectomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Classic appendicitis: migration + A/N/V + ไข้ + rebound + WBC 12,000 PMN 80% → Alvarado 9","e":"Alvarado: migration 1, anorexia 1, N/V 1, RLQ tender 2, rebound 1, temp ≥ 37.3 1, WBC > 10,000 2, shift (PMN > 75%) 1 = 9 → ≥ 7 สูงมาก ผู้ชายวัยรุ่นอาการ classic → appendectomy ไม่ต้อง imaging (imaging ใช้ในหญิง/ผู้สูงอายุ/score กลางๆ)."},{"id":"red1-97","src":"red1","n":97,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 70-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months ago presented with pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea and bilious vomiting without fever or obstipation. The physical examination revealed soft, not tender, moderate abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds. Acute abdominal series revealed generalized small bowel dilation with some gas in collapsed colon and no gas in the rectum.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Observe"],["B","IV Antibiotics"],["C","NG decompression and IV resuscitation"],["D","Rectal tube decompression"],["E","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Adhesive partial SBO ไม่มี strangulation sign (ไม่ไข้ ไม่กดเจ็บ ยังมีลมใน colon)","e":"Generalized SB dilatation + ลมใน colon (partial) + ท้องนุ่ม ไม่เจ็บ → conservative: NPO, NG decompression, IV fluid, แก้ electrolyte, serial exam ± water-soluble contrast challenge. ผ่าตัดเมื่อมี strangulation หรือไม่ดีขึ้นใน 48–72 ชม."},{"id":"red1-98","src":"red1","n":98,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 45-year-old man presented with progressive jaundice. Work up: U/S before admission shows normal liver and no space-occupying lesion with IHD and CBD dilatation. Suspected periampullary CA. He underwent ERCP and found an ampullar mass. Three days post-ERCP he revisited with fever and RUQ pain. CT abdomen: A 5-cm loculated rim enhancing hypodense lesion at right lobe of liver. => pyogenic abscess\nWhich of the following is the most common pathologic organism?","opts":[["A","Klebsiella spp."],["B","Escherichia coli"],["C","Bacteroides fragilis"],["D","Staphylococcus spp."],["E","Streptococcus spp."]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Pyogenic liver abscess จาก biliary source: E. coli และ Klebsiella","e":"ตำราตะวันตก: E. coli พบมากสุดใน biliary-source abscess; ในเอเชีย (รวมไทย) Klebsiella pneumoniae เป็นสาเหตุอันดับ 1 ของ pyogenic liver abscess โดยรวม. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = B E. coli; เฉลยในบทเรียน Day 7 ระบุ E. coli (เอเชียพบ Klebsiella มาก) — ข้อนี้ตอบ E. coli ตามเฉลย (แหล่งจากท่อน้ำดี) — แต่ถ้าถาม \"pyogenic liver abscess โดยรวมในไทย\" ให้นึกถึง Klebsiella."},{"id":"red1-99","src":"red1","n":99,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"An 81-year-old female presented with left lower quadrant abdominal pain for 2 days and could not eat anything. She had a low-grade fever, anorexia, and nausea without vomiting. Physical examination revealed marked tenderness at the left lower quadrant area with localized guarding. The abdominal CT scan revealed a thick-walled sigmoid colon and a 5-cm abscess in the pelvis.\nWhat is the appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Sigmoidectomy"],["B","Bowel rest and antibiotics"],["C","Bowel rest and pain killers"],["D","Laparoscopic abdominal lavage"],["E","Percutaneous drainage and antibiotics"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Complicated diverticulitis Hinchey II (pelvic abscess ≥ 3–4 cm) → percutaneous drainage + ATB","e":"Hinchey I (pericolic abscess เล็ก < 3–4 cm) → ATB อย่างเดียว; Hinchey II (pelvic/distant abscess ใหญ่) → CT-guided percutaneous drainage + IV ATB แล้วพิจารณา elective sigmoidectomy; Hinchey III–IV (purulent/feculent peritonitis) → ผ่าตัด (Hartmann/primary anastomosis ± diverting stoma)."},{"id":"red1-100","src":"red1","n":100,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 45-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash.\nPE: BP 90/50 mmHg, pulse rate 120/min\nAbdomen: marked tenderness and generalized guarding\nFoley : Gross hematuria\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management in the next step?","opts":[["A","Peritoneal lavage"],["B","Selective abdominal arteriography"],["C","Computed tomography of the abdomen"],["D","Observe and serial Het"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Shock + generalized guarding (peritonitis) → laparotomy; gross hematuria ไม่เปลี่ยนการตัดสินใจ","e":"BP 90/50 PR 120 + peritonitis → exploratory laparotomy ทันที (ประเมิน GU injury ระหว่างผ่าตัด เช่น one-shot IVP/สำรวจ retroperitoneal hematoma). CT ใช้ในคน stable; DPL/observe ไม่เหมาะ."},{"id":"red1-101","src":"red1","n":101,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 20-year-old man underwent tumor removal at Lt. buttock region. The postoperative complication was nerve injury and he had weakness of the Lt. lower leg. Physical examination showed no voluntary muscle contraction of the Lt. leg (motor power gr.0).\nWhat is the most proper management to prevent muscle atrophy in this patient?","opts":[["A","Use foot board"],["B","Hot pack Lt. lower leg"],["C","Electrical stimulation Lt. leg"],["D","Ankle pumping exercise Lt. leg"],["E","Range of motion exercise Lt. leg"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"กล้ามเนื้อ power 0 (ไม่มี voluntary contraction) → ออกกำลังเองไม่ได้ → ใช้กระแสไฟกระตุ้น","e":"Disuse/denervation atrophy ในกล้ามเนื้อที่ motor power 0: electrical stimulation ช่วยให้กล้ามเนื้อหดตัว คงมวลกล้ามเนื้อระหว่างรอ nerve recovery. ROM exercise ป้องกัน contracture แต่ไม่ป้องกันกล้ามเนื้อลีบ; ankle pumping ต้องหดตัวเองได้; foot board ป้องกัน foot drop deformity."},{"id":"red1-102","src":"red1","n":102,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 60-year-old man underwent Whipple operation. After bed rest for 4 days, he felt dizziness every time he was in upright position. Physical examination showed drop of systolic BP from 120 to 100 mmHg and PR increase from 90 to 110 mmHg. What is the most proper management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Use air mattress"],["B","Repositioning every 2 hours"],["C","Stretching exercise of both legs"],["D","Continuous passive motion both legs You"],["E","Progressive upright with Fowler bed"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"นอนนาน → orthostatic hypotension (SBP ลด ≥ 20 หรือ HR เพิ่ม) จาก cardiovascular deconditioning","e":"แก้ด้วย progressive upright: ปรับเตียงยกหัวสูงขึ้นทีละน้อย (Fowler/tilt table) ให้ร่างกายปรับตัว + elastic stocking/abdominal binder + น้ำเพียงพอ. Air mattress/repositioning กันแผลกดทับ; CPM กัน joint stiffness."},{"id":"red1-103","src":"red1","n":103,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 60-year-old female had breast cancer with brain metastasis. Her physical status was bed ridden and not full consciousness. Which is the most proper management to prevent pressure ulcer for this patient?","opts":[["A","Keep dry skin"],["B","Use air mattress"],["C","Bed positioning"],["D","Range of motion exercise"],["E","Repositioning regularly every 2 hours"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"ป้องกัน pressure ulcer: หัวใจคือ \"ลดแรงกด\" ด้วยการพลิกตัวสม่ำเสมอ","e":"Repositioning ทุก 2 ชม. เป็นมาตรการหลักและสำคัญที่สุด (ลดระยะเวลาที่ผิวหนังถูกกด) ร่วมกับ air mattress, ดูแลผิวให้แห้ง, โภชนาการ. ตัวเลือก B, C, A เป็นมาตรการเสริม; ROM กันข้อติด."},{"id":"red1-104","src":"red1","n":104,"cat":"rehab","stem":"What is a pathophysiology of pressure ulcer that occurs from shearing force?","opts":[["A","Venous thrombosis"],["B","Atherosclerosis with occlusion"],["C","Inflammatory process and vasculitis"],["D","Perpendicular compressive force with ischemia"],["E","Transverse skin distortion and perforating arterial disruption"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Shearing = แรงขนานผิวหนัง (เช่น เลื่อนตัวลงเตียงตอนยกหัวสูง)","e":"Shear force ทำให้ชั้นผิวหนังเคลื่อนคนละทิศกับชั้นลึก → ผิวบิดเบี้ยว (transverse distortion) → perforating arteries ถูกยืด/ฉีกขาด → ischemia ชั้นลึก (พบที่ sacrum). Perpendicular compression = กลไกของ pressure (แรงกดตั้งฉาก). LP เคยวง D แต่ D คือ pressure ไม่ใช่ shear."},{"id":"red1-105","src":"red1","n":105,"cat":"vascular","stem":"55-year-old female had Rt.leg tenderness, swelling and erythema. Physical examination showed Homan's sign\nWhich is the most proper investigation for this patient?","opts":[["A","X-ray Rt. tibia"],["B","Duplex ultrasonography"],["C","CT scan abdomen"],["D","PT INR"],["E","CBC"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ขาบวมแดงเจ็บ + Homan's sign → สงสัย DVT → ยืนยันด้วย compression duplex US","e":"Duplex/compression ultrasound เป็น first-line ยืนยัน DVT (ใช้ร่วม Wells score ± D-dimer). Homan's sign ไม่ sensitive/specific. X-ray, CT abdomen, PT-INR, CBC ไม่ใช่การวินิจฉัย."},{"id":"red1-106","src":"red1","n":106,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A patient with chronic renal failure condition is coming for appendectomy. Which drug is the most appropriate?","opts":[["A","Fentanyl"],["B","Pethidine"],["C","Morphine"],["D","Diclofenac"],["E","Parecoxib"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ไตวาย → เลี่ยงยาที่มี active metabolite สะสม (morphine M6G, pethidine norpethidine) และ NSAIDs","e":"Fentanyl ถูก metabolize ที่ตับเป็น metabolite ที่ไม่ active → ปลอดภัยที่สุดใน CKD. Morphine → M6G สะสมทำให้กดหายใจนาน; pethidine → norpethidine ทำให้ชัก; diclofenac/parecoxib ทำให้ไตแย่ลง."},{"id":"red1-107","src":"red1","n":107,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 20-year-old, ASA class I may has had Carpal tunnel syndrome. He got brachial plexus anesthesia.\nWhat is the most appropriate pain medication for him?","opts":[["A","Paracetamol 1 gm ☉ q 6 hr."],["B","Morphine 3 mg IV q 2 hr."],["C","Fentanyl 50 mcg IV q 2 hr."],["D","Codeine 30 mg ☉ q 4 hr."],["E","Tramadol 100 mg ☉ q 6 hr."]],"key":"B","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ผ่าตัดเล็ก (carpal tunnel) + brachial plexus block (block คุมปวดได้ดีหลายชม.) → ปวดน้อย","e":"Minor surgery ที่มี regional anesthesia → ใช้ paracetamol 1 g PO q6h (± NSAID) เป็น basal analgesia เพียงพอ. Opioid IV ไม่จำเป็นและมีผลข้างเคียง. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = B แต่ไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 108 (โจทย์เดียวกัน) ไฮไลต์ paracetamol และ Day pain lesson ก็ยืนยัน A."},{"id":"red1-108","src":"red1","n":108,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 80-year-old man who has diagnosed colon cancer. He has got the chemotherapy and thrombocytopenia. He got appendectomy. You should not give","opts":[["A","Diclofenac"],["B","Tramadol"],["C","Morphine"],["D","Fentanyl"],["E","Paracetamol"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Thrombocytopenia + ผู้สูงอายุ + chemo → เลี่ยงยาที่ยับยั้งการทำงานของเกล็ดเลือด","e":"NSAIDs (diclofenac) ยับยั้ง COX-1 → platelet dysfunction + GI bleeding + AKI โดยเฉพาะผู้สูงอายุที่เกล็ดเลือดต่ำ → ห้ามให้. Tramadol, opioid, paracetamol ใช้ได้ (ปรับ dose ตามอายุ)."},{"id":"red1-109","src":"red1","n":109,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 65-year-old man with well-controlled hypertension got laparoscopic cholecystectomy for 1.5 hr. He got morphine 12 mg and vecuron 12 mg. The volatile anesthetic agent was turned off for 15 min. After that muscle relaxant reversal was given but the patient still has apnea and unconsciousness. What is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hyperosmolar coma"],["B","Metabolism acidosis"],["C","Residual muscle relaxant"],["D","Opioid overdose"],["E","Cerebrovascular accident"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Apnea + unconscious หลังให้ reversal แล้ว + ได้ morphine 12 mg (มาก) → opioid","e":"Morphine 12 mg ในผู้ป่วยสูงอายุในการผ่าตัด 1.5 ชม. = เกินขนาด → กดหายใจ + ไม่รู้สึกตัว + pupil เล็ก (ไฟล์เหลือง เติม \"pupils 1 mm\") → naloxone titrate. Residual NMB จะรู้สึกตัวแต่ขยับ/หายใจไม่ได้ (ไม่หมดสติ)."},{"id":"red1-110","src":"red1","n":110,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"At PACU, a patient who got ovarian cystectomy gains consciousness after we woke her up, RR 10/min, BP 150/90 mmHg, HR 96/min, SpO2 95% room air. VAS = 3\nWhich choice is correct?","opts":[["A","Sedation score"],["B","Morphine 3 mg IV"],["C","Nifedipine 10 mg SL"],["D","Naloxone 0.4 mg IV"],["E","O2 cannula 3 LPM"]],"key":"D","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"PACU ประเมิน: รู้สึกตัว (sedation 0–1), VAS 3 (ปวดน้อย), SpO₂ 95% room air → ให้ O₂ supplement","e":"หลัง GA ทุกรายควรได้ O₂ ใน PACU (SpO₂ 95% RA ยังต่ำกว่าเป้า, RR 10 ยังพอได้). ไม่ต้องให้ naloxone เพราะรู้สึกตัวดีและ RR ไม่ต่ำกว่า 10 (ต่ำกว่า 8–10 + sedation 3 จึงให้); VAS 3 ไม่ต้องให้ morphine; BP 150/90 มักจาก pain/emergence ไม่ต้องให้ nifedipine. ชุด 2 ข้อ 110 เฉลย = E; ชุด 1 ไฮไลต์ D (ขัดกัน) — LP = E."},{"id":"red1-111","src":"red1","n":111,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"What is the risk factor of postoperative nausea & vomiting (PONV).","opts":[["A","Male"],["B","Elderly"],["C","Regional anesthesia"],["D","Motion sickness history"],["E","Postoperative hypertension"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Apfel score: female, non-smoker, history PONV/motion sickness, postoperative opioid","e":"Risk factors ของ PONV: เพศหญิง, ไม่สูบบุหรี่, ประวัติ PONV หรือ motion sickness, ได้ opioid หลังผ่าตัด; อายุน้อย, volatile anesthetic/N₂O, ผ่าตัดนาน, laparoscopic/gynecologic. Male, elderly, regional anesthesia = เสี่ยง \"น้อย\"."},{"id":"red1-112","src":"red1","n":112,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"What is the most common cause of restlessness after general anesthesia?","opts":[["A","Hypoxia"],["B","Pain"],["C","Hypotension"],["D","Hypothermia"],["E","Electrolyte imbalance"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Restlessness/agitation หลัง GA ต้องตัด hypoxia ก่อนเสมอ แต่ \"สาเหตุที่พบบ่อยที่สุด\" = pain","e":"Emergence agitation ใน PACU สาเหตุพบบ่อยสุดคือ pain (รวมถึง bladder distension); ที่อันตรายต้องคิดเสมอคือ hypoxia/hypercarbia, hypotension, hypoglycemia. หลักปฏิบัติ: ประเมิน ABC/SpO₂ ก่อน แล้วค่อยให้ยาแก้ปวด."},{"id":"red1-113","src":"red1","n":113,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"At PACU, an 80-year-old woman has gained the consciousness after we woke her up, RR 10/min, stridor, pupil 2 mm both react to light, Spo, 96%, normal vital signs.\nWhat is the least likely cause to be happened?","opts":[["A","Secretion obstruction"],["B","Subglottic edema"],["C","Vocal cord edema"],["D","Opioid overdose"],["E","Residual neuromuscular blockade"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Stridor = ทางเดินหายใจส่วนบนอุด (mechanical) → opioid ไม่ทำให้มีเสียง stridor","e":"Stridor หลัง extubation: laryngeal/subglottic/vocal cord edema, secretion obstruction, laryngospasm, residual NMB (กล้ามเนื้อคอหย่อนอุดทางเดินหายใจ). Opioid overdose ทำให้ RR ช้า pupil เล็ก แต่ไม่ทำให้ stridor จึงเป็น least likely (แม้ pupil 2 mm). LP วง A (secretion) ไว้ — แต่ตามกลไกตอบ D สอดคล้องเฉลยไฟล์."},{"id":"red1-114","src":"red1","n":114,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 25-year-old woman who-has general anesthesia c endotracheal tube & balance anesthetic technique, after the question finish, extubation was done uneventfully. Patient complained that she had the hoarseness after the operation for 3 days.\nWhat is the cause?","opts":[["A","Vocal cord edema"],["B","Vocal cord polyp"],["C","Arytenoids dislocation"],["D","Nerve injury"],["E","Laryngeal nerve injury both sides"]],"key":"C","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Hoarseness หลัง intubate ธรรมดา 2–3 วัน → พบบ่อยสุด vocal cord edema/trauma ชั่วคราว","e":"Postintubation hoarseness ส่วนใหญ่จาก mucosal edema/laryngeal irritation หายใน 2–3 วัน. Arytenoid dislocation พบน้อย อาการแหบทันที + เจ็บเวลากลืน + breathy voice นานกว่า (ไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 116). Bilateral RLN injury → stridor. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = C แต่ LP ตอบ A (vocal cord edema) ซึ่งตรงหลักมากกว่าในโจทย์ที่ไม่มีอาการพิเศษ."},{"id":"red1-115","src":"red1","n":115,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 25-year-old woman who is diagnosed Hashimoto's thyroiditis got subtotal thyroidectomy. She has the seizure after the operation 6 hrs. What is the cause?","opts":[["A","Hypoxemia from vocal cord edema"],["B","Hypocalcemia"],["C","Hypercalcemia"],["D","Hyperventilation"],["E","Hyponatremia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ชักหลัง thyroidectomy ชั่วโมงแรกๆ → hypocalcemia จาก parathyroid injury/devascularization","e":"Hypoparathyroidism หลัง (sub)total thyroidectomy → perioral numbness, Chvostek/Trousseau, tetany, ชัก, prolonged QT → รักษา 10% calcium gluconate IV. มักเกิด 24–72 ชม. แต่เกิดเร็วได้. Vocal cord edema ทำให้ stridor มากกว่าชัก."},{"id":"red1-116","src":"red1","n":116,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Pituitary adrenal axis will be suppressed after taking prednisolone (5 mg) oral three times a day for at LEAST......?","opts":[["A","1 day."],["B","3 days."],["C","1 week."],["D","1 month."],["E","3 months."]],"key":"E","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"HPA suppression: prednisolone ≥ 20 mg/วัน (หรือ 15 mg) นาน ≥ 3 สัปดาห์","e":"Prednisolone 5 mg tid = 15 mg/วัน (> 7.5 mg) — เกณฑ์ที่ถือว่าอาจถูกกด: ≥ 20 mg/วัน ≥ 3 สัปดาห์ หรือ cushingoid; < 5 mg/วัน หรือ < 3 สัปดาห์ถือว่าไม่ถูกกด. ตัวเลือกแรกที่ ≥ 3 สัปดาห์ = 1 month. เฉลยไฟล์ = E (3 months), LP วง 3 months, รุ่นก่อนกา 3 days — เฉลยไม่ตรงกัน; ตอบตามหลัก D."},{"id":"red1-117","src":"red1","n":117,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which patient will probably have the MOST difficult endotracheal intubation","opts":[["A","No upper and lower teeth"],["B","Full neck flexion and extension"],["C","Interincisor gap 5 cm"],["D","Mallampati classification 4"],["E","Thyromental distance 6 cm"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Predictors ของ difficult intubation: Mallampati III–IV, TMD < 6 cm, IIG < 3 cm, คอขยับไม่ได้","e":"Mallampati class IV (เห็นแค่ hard palate) ทำนาย difficult laryngoscopy มากสุดในตัวเลือก. ไม่มีฟัน = difficult mask ventilation แต่ intubate ง่าย; neck movement เต็ม, IIG 5 cm, TMD 6 cm (ขอบเขตปกติ) ไม่บ่งยาก."},{"id":"red1-118","src":"red1","n":118,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 20-year-old man is brought to the operating room for the emergency appendectomy. He has no underlying disease. His Hb = 10.2 g/dL, Hct = 30%, WBC = 11000/mm 3 , PMN = 72%, L = 28%, normal urine examination and CXR.\nWhat is his ASA classification?","opts":[["A","1E"],["B","2E"],["C","3E"],["D","4E"],["E","5E"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ASA: ไม่มีโรคประจำตัว = I; ผ่าตัดฉุกเฉินเติม E","e":"ชายสุขภาพดี anemia เล็กน้อย/leukocytosis จาก appendicitis เป็นผลของโรคที่จะผ่าตัด ไม่ใช่ systemic disease → ASA 1E. (ASA II = mild systemic disease ควบคุมได้ เช่น HT/DM คุมได้, สูบบุหรี่, BMI 30–40)"},{"id":"red1-119","src":"red1","n":119,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which oral medication must be continued until the day of surgery?","opts":[["A","Atenolol"],["B","Enalapril"],["C","Aldactone"],["D","Furosemide"],["E","Losartan"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Beta-blocker ห้ามหยุดก่อนผ่าตัด (rebound tachycardia/ischemia)","e":"ยาที่ต้องกินต่อจนถึงเช้าวันผ่าตัด: beta-blocker, statin, CCB, antiepileptic, steroid. ACEI/ARB มักงดเช้าวันผ่าตัด (เสี่ยง refractory hypotension); diuretic (furosemide, spironolactone) งดวันผ่าตัด (hypovolemia/hypoK)."},{"id":"red1-120","src":"red1","n":120,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which is CORRECT regarding to preoperative preparation in diabetic patients?","opts":[["A","Check blood sugar every hour before surgery."],["B","Ranitidine 150 mg @ 1 hr. prior to OR"],["C","Administer IV Lactated Ringer' solution."],["D","Glibenclamide 1 tab @ 1 hr. prior to OR."],["E","Control blood sugar between 200-300 mg%."]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"DM → gastroparesis → เสี่ยง aspiration → ให้ H2 blocker/PPI ก่อนผ่าตัด","e":"เตรียมผู้ป่วยเบาหวาน: งด sulfonylurea (glibenclamide → hypoglycemia ตอน NPO), ใช้ insulin ปรับ, เป้า glucose 140–180 (< 200) mg/dL, เจาะ DTX ก่อนผ่าตัด/ทุก 1–2 ชม. ระหว่างผ่าตัด, ให้ fluid มี dextrose; aspiration prophylaxis (ranitidine) เหมาะเพราะ gastroparesis. LRS ไม่ใช่ข้อห้ามแต่ไม่ใช่หลักการเฉพาะ DM."},{"id":"red2-1","src":"red2","n":1,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 60-year-old poorly controlled hypertensive male presented with abrupt onset of severe chest pain that radiated to his back with right leg pain 2 hours before arrival.\nPE Left Right\nCommon femoral 0 2+\nPopliteal 0 2+\nDP/PT 0 2+\nWhat is the most likely cause of this symptom?","opts":[["A","Atrial fibrillation"],["B","Saddle embolism"],["C","Thoracic aortic dissection"],["D","Abdominal aortic aneurysm"],["E","Acute myocardial infarction"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"เจ็บอกร้าวทะลุหลัง (tearing) + HT คุมไม่ดี + pulse ขาข้างหนึ่งหาย → dissection ลามลงไปบัง iliac","e":"Aortic dissection (Stanford A/B ที่ลามลง abdominal aorta) ทำให้ branch occlusion → malperfusion ของขา (ALI) ได้. Saddle embolism ทำให้ pulse หายทั้งสองข้างและไม่มีเจ็บอกร้าวหลัง; AF ทำให้ emboli แต่ไม่อธิบายอาการเจ็บอก. วินิจฉัยด้วย CTA aorta."},{"id":"red2-2","src":"red2","n":2,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 35-year-old male was stabbed at the right arm 6 months ago. His arm was swollen for 2 months. PE:\nRight arm; Superficial vein dilatation, thrill at the scar of right arm.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Pseudoaneurysm"],["B","Arteriovenous fistula"],["C","Venous malformation"],["D","Cavernous hemangioma"],["E","Peripheral arterial disease"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Penetrating injury เก่า + superficial vein โป่ง + thrill/bruit ที่แผลเป็น = shunt ระหว่าง artery กับ vein","e":"Traumatic arteriovenous fistula: เลือดแดงไหลลัด vein → venous hypertension (เส้นเลือดดำโป่ง บวม), thrill/continuous machinery bruit, อาจมี high-output heart failure. Pseudoaneurysm = ก้อนเต้นตามชีพจร (pulsatile mass) มี systolic bruit; venous malformation เป็นแต่กำเนิด ไม่มี thrill."},{"id":"red2-3","src":"red2","n":3,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 75-year-old woman presents with left hemiparesis for 5 min with complete recovery. Her underlying diseases are coronary artery disease with clinically stable angina, poorly controlled hypertension, renal insufficiency, and dyslipidemia. PE: BP 140/70mmHg, PR 60/min Heart: regular, no murmur\nWhat is the most appropriate screening test to identify the causes in this patient?","opts":[["A","Echocardiography"],["B","Exercise stress test"],["C","CT brain with contrast"],["D","Coronary angiography"],["E","Duplex ultrasound carotid artery"]],"key":"C","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"TIA (hemiparesis หายใน < 24 ชม.) + atherosclerotic risk → หา carotid stenosis","e":"TIA ของ anterior circulation ในผู้สูงอายุที่มี HT/DLP/CAD → สาเหตุที่ต้องหาคือ carotid artery stenosis → screening = duplex ultrasound carotid (ถ้า ≥ 70% symptomatic → carotid endarterectomy). CT brain ควรทำเพื่อแยกเลือดออก แต่ \"with contrast\" ในไตบกพร่องไม่เหมาะ และไม่ได้หาสาเหตุ. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = C แต่ LP วง E และไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 76 (โจทย์เดียวกัน) ไฮไลต์ E."},{"id":"red2-4","src":"red2","n":4,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 32-year-old man presents at the emergency room after a car crash. His initial vital signs show BP 85/50 mmHg, P 110 beats/min, R 22/min, and BT 36.5°C. He has an open wound at his right thigh with continuous bleeding and a bruise at his left flank.\nWhich one is the appropriate management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Ringer's lactate solution 1 L IV through a 20-gauge IV catheter"],["B","Normal saline 2 L IV rate 80 ml/h and request for blood components"],["C","Hydroxyethyl starch 1 L IV in 1 hr."],["D","Ringer's lactate solution 1 L IV in 15-30 min"],["E","Ringer's lactate solution 1 L IV in 15-30 min and request for blood components"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Hemorrhagic shock class III (BP 85/50 HR 110 เลือดออกต่อเนื่อง) → crystalloid 1 L เร็ว + เตรียมเลือด","e":"ATLS: warm isotonic crystalloid 1 L (ไม่ใช่ 2 L แบบเดิม) ใน 15–30 นาที ผ่าน large-bore IV (≥ 18G ไม่ใช่ 20G) และ request blood products ทันที (early blood, 1:1:1). HES ห้ามใช้ (AKI, coagulopathy). อย่าลืมกด/ห้ามเลือดแผลต้นขาโดยตรง."},{"id":"red2-5","src":"red2","n":5,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 35-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. At the ED: BP 100/60 mmHg, P 120/min No neck vein engorgement\nLungs: Rt = Lt * Abd: Mild tenderness at Rt thoracoabdomen\nFAST as shown\nWhich of the following is the most likely?","opts":[["A","Cardiac tamponade"],["B","Hemopericardium"],["C","Hemoperitoneum"],["D","Hemomediastinum"],["E","Hemothorax"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q5-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ FAST: anechoic fluid ใน Morison's pouch (ระหว่างตับกับไต)","e":"Free fluid (anechoic stripe) ที่ hepatorenal recess = hemoperitoneum ในบริบท trauma. Tamponade/hemopericardium ดูใน subxiphoid view (มี JVD); hemothorax ดูเหนือ diaphragm. ผู้ป่วย BP 100/60 PR 120 → ถ้าไม่ตอบสนองต่อ resuscitation → laparotomy; ถ้าตอบสนอง → CT."},{"id":"red2-6","src":"red2","n":6,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 20-year-old man developed chest discomfort following subclavian vein catheterization. The chest X-ray showed:\nWhich one of the following is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hemothorax"],["B","Lung contusion"],["C","Pneumothorax"],["D","Mediastinal emphysema"],["E","Subcutaneous emphysema"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ภาวะแทรกซ้อนจากการใส่ subclavian line ที่พบบ่อยสุดคือ pneumothorax","e":"เจ็บ/แน่นอกหลังใส่ subclavian catheter → iatrogenic pneumothorax (CXR เห็น visceral pleural line). ต้อง CXR ทุกครั้งหลังใส่ CVC (ดูตำแหน่ง tip และ pneumothorax). Hemothorax เกิดได้ถ้าแทงโดน artery. (ภาพในไฟล์ต้นฉบับไม่ได้แนบมา)"},{"id":"red2-7","src":"red2","n":7,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 50-year-old female has end-stage renal disease. She was admitted for emergency cholecystectomy. EKG showed:\nWhich of the following is the cause of the abnormal EKG?","opts":[["A","Hypokalemia"],["B","Hyperkalemia"],["C","Hyponatremia"],["D","Hypernatremia"],["E","Hypermagnesemia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q7-1.jpg","img/mcq/s2-q7-2.jpg"],"t":"ESRD + EKG peaked T (ภาพ) = hyperkalemia","e":"ESRD → ขับ K ไม่ได้ → hyperK. EKG: tall peaked T → PR ยาว/P แบน → QRS กว้าง → sine wave → VF. ก่อนผ่าตัดต้องแก้: calcium gluconate (ถ้ามี EKG change), insulin+glucose, dialysis ก่อนผ่าตัด."},{"id":"red2-8","src":"red2","n":8,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old male suffered from a motorcycle crash 30 min PTA. The examination revealed vital signs of BP 80/30 mmHg, P 90 bpm, RR 32 bpm, and 0 sat 78%. He aspirated a lot of blood. The Glasgow Coma Scale score was E2V1M4.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate management for this patient?","opts":[["A","CT brain as soon as possible"],["B","Mannitol infusion"],["C","Hypertonic saline infusion"],["D","Intubation"],["E","Head elevation 45 degree"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Aspiration เลือด + SpO₂ 78% + GCS 7 → airway ก่อนทุกอย่าง","e":"ทั้ง airway อุด (เลือด), hypoxia และ GCS ≤ 8 = ข้อบ่งชี้ definitive airway (RSI + in-line c-spine stabilization). การรักษา ICP (mannitol, hypertonic, head up) และ CT brain มาทีหลัง; mannitol ห้ามใน hypotension."},{"id":"red2-9","src":"red2","n":9,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"All of the following increase the risk of perforation in patients with Ogilvie's syndrome EXCEPT?","opts":[["A","Old age"],["B","Diabetes mellitus"],["C","Chronic mesenteric ischemia"],["D","Delay in decompression"],["E","Increasing cecal diameter"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ปัจจัยเสี่ยง perforation ใน Ogilvie = อะไรที่ทำให้ cecum ขาดเลือด/ตึงนาน","e":"Risk ของ cecal perforation: cecal diameter > 12 cm, ระยะเวลาที่โป่ง (> 6 วัน, delay decompression), อายุมาก, ischemia (mesenteric ischemia). DM ไม่ได้เพิ่ม risk ของ perforation โดยตรง (แม้เป็น risk ของ pseudo-obstruction)."},{"id":"red2-10","src":"red2","n":10,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 56-year-old male presents with hematochezia for 3 hours. He has no underlying disease and is not taking any medications. At the ED his BP is 90/60 mmHg, PR is 120 beats/min, RR is 24/min, and the BT is 37.2°C. The physical examination of the abdomen reveals normal. The DRE and proctoscopy reveal a large amount of fresh blood but no anorectal lesion or hemorrhoid. His BP is still 90/60 mmHg, and the PR is 130 beats/min despite intensive fluid resuscitation and there is ongoing bleeding. Bile content without blood is obtained from a nasogastric tube.\nWhat is the appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Elective colonoscopy"],["B","Emergency colonoscopy at bedside"],["C","Mesenteric angiography for embolization"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy with sigmoidectomy"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy with total colectomy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"LGIB massive ที่ยัง unstable แม้ resuscitate → ห้าม colonoscopy → CTA/angiography + embolization","e":"Hematochezia + shock ไม่ตอบสนอง + NG bile ไม่มีเลือด (ตัด UGIB) → mesenteric angiography หา active bleeding + embolization (หรือ CTA ก่อนเพื่อหาตำแหน่ง). Colonoscopy ทำเมื่อ stable; blind total colectomy เป็นทางสุดท้ายเมื่อหาจุดไม่ได้และยังออก; sigmoidectomy โดยไม่รู้ตำแหน่งผิด."},{"id":"red2-11","src":"red2","n":11,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old male developed a fever on postoperative day 1 after right lobe hepatectomy. PE: BT 38.5°C, PR 82/min, RR 18/min, BP 110/60 mmHg Lung: clear both sides Abdomen: good surgical wound, soft, not tender, no guarding JP drain: serosanguinous fluid 100 mL/d\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","CT abdomen"],["B","PTBD drainage"],["C","Emergency reoperation"],["D","Hemoculture and empirical IV antibiotic"],["E","Oxygen therapy and deep breathing exercise"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"ไข้ POD1 + ปอดใส แผลดี = atelectasis → รักษาด้วย lung expansion","e":"Early postoperative fever จาก atelectasis/inflammation → incentive spirometry, deep breathing exercise, early ambulation, O₂, pain control. ไม่ต้อง CT/ATB/reoperation. ตรงกับชุด 1 ข้อ 93 (สาเหตุ = atelectasis)."},{"id":"red2-12","src":"red2","n":12,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old women had fever and abdominal pain for 3 days. V/S: BT 39°C, BP 86/60 mmHg, PR 100/min, RR 24/min; Physical exam:(icteric sclera and tenderness at the RUQ, Murphy sign negative, no hepatosplenomegaly; WBC 22,000, PMN 80, L Bands 10% LFTs: TB 5.02 mg%, DB 4.18 mg%, SGOT 120 U/L, SGPT 140 U/L, ALP 300 U/L\nWhich of following the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Acute cholecystitis"],["B","Acute cholangitis"],["C","Acute hepatitis"],["D","Liver abscess"],["E","Leptospirosis"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Reynolds' pentad = Charcot (ไข้ + RUQ pain + jaundice) + shock + (confusion)","e":"ไข้ 39 + RUQ tender + icteric + BP 86/60 + WBC 22,000 bands 10% + direct hyperbilirubinemia + ALP สูง → severe (Grade III) acute cholangitis → resuscitate, IV ATB, urgent biliary drainage (ERCP). Acute cholecystitis ไม่ค่อย jaundice และ Murphy +; liver abscess ไม่มี cholestatic jaundice เด่น."},{"id":"red2-13","src":"red2","n":13,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old man underwent excision of a sebaceous cyst. On post-operative day 3, he develops pain, warmth, redness, and tenderness with pus discharge from the wound.\nWhat is the most appropriate antibiotic?","opts":[["A","Gentamycin"],["B","Clindamycin"],["C","Cloxacillin"],["D","Norfloxacin"],["E","Amoxycillin"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"SSI ของแผล clean (ตัด sebaceous cyst) = S. aureus → anti-staphylococcal penicillin","e":"Cloxacillin/dicloxacillin (หรือ cephalexin) คลุม MSSA ซึ่งเป็นเชื้อหลักของ SSI แผล clean; ร่วมกับเปิดแผลระบายหนอง. Gentamicin/norfloxacin คลุม gram-negative; amoxicillin ถูก β-lactamase ของ staph ทำลาย; clindamycin ใช้ในคนแพ้ penicillin."},{"id":"red2-14","src":"red2","n":14,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 60-year-old Thai male has right leg pain for 7 days and a high grade fever for one day. His underlying diseases include DM and CKD. At the ER, his vital signs are BP 100/70 mmHg, PR 100 bpm, BT 39°C, and RR 30/min. Crepitation was found on examination at his right leg.\nWhat is the most important treatment?","opts":[["A","NSS resuscitation"],["B","High dose ertapenem administration"],["C","Emergency aggressive debridement"],["D","Emergency fasciotomy"],["E","Emergency Above knee amputation"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ขาปวด + ไข้ + crepitus + DM = necrotizing soft tissue infection → source control ด่วน","e":"Necrotizing fasciitis/gas gangrene: การรักษาที่สำคัญที่สุดคือ emergency aggressive surgical debridement (ซ้ำทุก 24–48 ชม.) ร่วมกับ broad-spectrum ATB และ resuscitation. Fasciotomy เป็นการลด compartment pressure ไม่ใช่การเอาเนื้อตายออก; AKA ทำเมื่อขาเสียหายจนรักษาไม่ได้/sepsis ไม่คุม. LP วง C (เฉลยเดิมกา fasciotomy)."},{"id":"red2-15","src":"red2","n":15,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 40-year-old male stepped on a nail while working 1 hour prior to visiting the ER. He has a history of full course tetanus toxoid administration 4 years ago\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Open the wound, apply wet dressing, and discharge"],["B","Suture the wound, give an oral antibiotic, and discharge"],["C","Irrigate the wound with betadine, give an oral antibiotic, and discharge"],["D","Open the wound, apply wet dressing, give an oral antibiotic and a single dose of tetanus toxoid"],["E","Dress the wound with betadine, give an oral antibiotic and a single dose of tetanus toxoid"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"TT ครบชุด 4 ปีก่อน (< 5 ปี) → ไม่ต้อง TT; ตะปูตำ → เปิดแผล wet dressing ไม่เย็บ ไม่ต้อง ATB","e":"แผลสกปรก: ให้ TT booster เมื่อ dose สุดท้าย > 5 ปี → 4 ปีจึงไม่ต้อง. Puncture wound ไม่ติดเชื้อ ไม่จำเป็นต้องให้ ATB; betadine ไม่ใช้ราดแผล; ห้ามเย็บแผลตะปูตำ."},{"id":"red2-16","src":"red2","n":16,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"Which of the following is the risk factor of adenocarcinoma of the esophagus?","opts":[["A","Achalasia"],["B","Barrett's esophagus"],["C","Corrosive stricture"],["D","Plummer-Vinson syndrome"],["E","Zenker's diverticulum"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Adenocarcinoma esophagus (distal 1/3) ← GERD → Barrett's (intestinal metaplasia)","e":"Barrett's esophagus = premalignant → esophageal adenocarcinoma (risk ~0.1–0.5%/ปี). อื่นๆ (achalasia, corrosive stricture, Plummer–Vinson, smoking/alcohol) เป็น risk ของ squamous cell carcinoma."},{"id":"red2-17","src":"red2","n":17,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"What is the early sign or symptom of acute gastric dilatation?","opts":[["A","Hiccup"],["B","Vomiting"],["C","Palpitation"],["D","Hypovolemic shock"],["E","Abdominal distension"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Acute gastric dilatation: อาการแรก = อาเจียน (regurgitation ปริมาณน้อยบ่อยๆ) ก่อนท้องอืด/shock","e":"พบหลังผ่าตัด/บาดเจ็บ/ใส่ gastric atony: เริ่มด้วย effortless vomiting/regurgitation ของเหลวสีดำ-เขียว, hiccup, ท้องอืด upper abdomen แล้วจึง hypovolemia/shock และ aspiration. รักษาด้วย NG decompression. (บางตำราจัด hiccup เป็นสัญญาณแรกได้ — แต่เฉลยไฟล์ = vomiting)"},{"id":"red2-18","src":"red2","n":18,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 30-year-old female presents with dysphagia. PE: anemia, atrophic oral mucosa, and spoon-shaped brittle fingernails.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","CA esophagus"],["B","Achalasia"],["C","Boerhaave's syndrome"],["D","Plummer-Vinson syndrome"],["E","Mallory-Weiss syndrome"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Dysphagia + iron deficiency (anemia, atrophic glossitis, koilonychia) = Plummer–Vinson","e":"Plummer–Vinson syndrome: triad dysphagia (post-cricoid web) + iron deficiency anemia + glossitis/koilonychia ในหญิงวัยกลางคน; เสี่ยง SCC. ตัวหลอก: achalasia (dysphagia ทั้ง solid/liquid ไม่มี anemia), Boerhaave/Mallory–Weiss (อาเจียนแรง)."},{"id":"red2-19","src":"red2","n":19,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 50-year-old female presents with progressive dysphagia that she has had for 2 years. Barium swallowing beak-like narrowing at the distal end of the esophagus Esophagoscopy: no tumor\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Esophageal stent"],["B","Esophageal balloon dilatation"],["C","Esophagectomy"],["D","Fundoplication"],["E","Conservative treatment"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Barium \"bird's beak\" + EGD ไม่มีก้อน (ตัด pseudoachalasia) = achalasia","e":"Achalasia: LES ไม่คลาย + aperistalsis; ยืนยันด้วย high-resolution manometry. รักษา: pneumatic balloon dilatation, laparoscopic Heller myotomy + partial fundoplication หรือ POEM; botox สำหรับผู้สูงอายุเสี่ยงสูง. Stent/esophagectomy สำหรับมะเร็ง/end-stage. ในตัวเลือกที่มี → balloon dilatation."},{"id":"red2-20","src":"red2","n":20,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 35-year-old presents with chest pain after heavy drinking and vomiting several times. PE: subcutaneous emphysema at the neck,\nCXR: pneumomediastinum\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Peptic ulcer perforation"],["B","Rupture of esophagus"],["C","Spontaneous pneumothorax"],["D","Tracheoesophageal fistula"],["E","Dissecting aneurysm"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"อาเจียนแรงหลังดื่มเหล้า + เจ็บอก + subcutaneous emphysema + pneumomediastinum","e":"Boerhaave syndrome (spontaneous esophageal rupture) – Mackler's triad: vomiting, chest pain, subcutaneous emphysema. ยืนยันด้วย water-soluble contrast swallow/CT; รักษาเร่งด่วน (ผ่าตัดซ่อม/drain + ATB + NPO). PU perforation จะเห็น free air ใต้กระบังลม ไม่ใช่ pneumomediastinum."},{"id":"red2-21","src":"red2","n":21,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"Which of the following statement(s) is true concerning esophageal neoplasms?","opts":[["A","Most enteral polyps are located at the esophagus"],["B","Most esophageal polyps are malignant"],["C","Most leiomyomas of the esophagus are malignant"],["D","An asymptomatic leiomyoma can be observed and followed"],["E","Primary treatment of esophageal GIST is tyrosine kinase inhibitor"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Benign esophageal tumor ที่พบมากที่สุด = leiomyoma (submucosal) ไม่ใช่ polyp","e":"Leiomyoma ส่วนใหญ่ benign ถ้าไม่มีอาการและเล็ก (< 2 cm) ติดตามได้; มีอาการ/โตขึ้น → enucleation (ห้าม biopsy ผ่าน mucosa ถ้าจะผ่าตัด). GI polyps ส่วนใหญ่อยู่ใน colon; esophageal polyp ส่วนใหญ่ benign (fibrovascular polyp); GIST ใน esophagus พบน้อย รักษาหลักด้วยการผ่าตัด (TKI = adjuvant/unresectable)."},{"id":"red2-22","src":"red2","n":22,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old man presented with progressive dysphagia for 1 month with weight loss of 3 kg in 1 month. EGD: As shown in the photo. While waiting for the pathology report, which one of the following is the most appropriate next step for the management?","opts":[["A","CT chest included upper abdomen"],["B","Chemotherapy"],["C","Radiotherapy"],["D","Esophagectomy"],["E","Percutaneous Endoscopic Gastrostomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q22-1.jpg"],"t":"ระหว่างรอผลชิ้นเนื้อ → staging ไปพร้อมกัน เพื่อเลือก curative vs palliative","e":"Esophageal cancer staging: CT chest + upper abdomen (ดู T4, node, liver/lung mets) ± PET-CT, EUS (T/N stage), bronchoscopy ถ้าก้อนอยู่ upper/mid ใกล้หลอดลม. ยังไม่มีผลชิ้นเนื้อจึงยังไม่ให้ chemo/RT/ผ่าตัด; PEG ใช้เมื่อกลืนไม่ได้และวางแผน palliative."},{"id":"red2-23","src":"red2","n":23,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 70-year-old-man has had progressive dysphagia for 2 months. Last month his weight decreased to 50 kg from 60 kg. Two weeks ago he noted a 3 cm mass at his left anterior neck. He has been an active smoker for 40 years.\nWhich is the most useful investigation for him?","opts":[["A","CT chest"],["B","Ultrasound neck"],["C","Barium swallow"],["D","Excisional biopsy mass at neck"],["E","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Progressive dysphagia + weight loss + Virchow-like node ในคนสูบบุหรี่ → หา primary + ชิ้นเนื้อ","e":"EGD ให้ทั้งการเห็นก้อนและ biopsy (most useful) — ยืนยันวินิจฉัย esophageal cancer; ต่อมน้ำเหลืองคอ (left supraclavicular) อาจเป็น metastasis ซึ่ง FNA ได้ภายหลัง. Barium swallow เห็นแค่ลักษณะตีบ; CT ใช้ staging; excisional biopsy คอเป็นหัตถการที่ใหญ่เกินไปเป็นขั้นแรก."},{"id":"red2-24","src":"red2","n":24,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"Where is the most common site of gastric cancer?","opts":[["A","Body"],["B","Cardia"],["C","Fundus"],["D","Antrum"],["E","Esophagogastric junction"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Gastric adenocarcinoma ตำแหน่งที่พบบ่อยที่สุด = distal stomach (antrum/pylorus)","e":"ตำแหน่งพบมากที่สุดคือ antrum (~40–50%) โดยเฉพาะ lesser curvature; แต่แนวโน้มในประเทศตะวันตกเพิ่ม proximal (cardia/GEJ) ซึ่งสัมพันธ์กับ GERD/obesity. ในไทย/เอเชียยังเป็น antrum."},{"id":"red2-25","src":"red2","n":25,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 60-year-old male has no difficulty defecating despite having adenocarcinoma of the middle rectum. His serum CEA level was 15 ng/mL The chest and abdominal CT scan reveals multiple metastases in both lungs and liver.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Low anterior resection"],["B","Abdominoperineal resection"],["C","Neoadjuvant chemo-RT"],["D","Chemotherapy"],["E","Radiotherapy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Stage IV (lung + liver mets หลายตำแหน่ง) + primary ไม่มีอาการอุด/เลือดออก → systemic therapy","e":"Metastatic rectal cancer ที่ unresectable และ primary ไม่มีอาการ → systemic chemotherapy (± targeted, ตาม RAS/BRAF/MSI) เป็นหลัก; ผ่าตัด primary เมื่อมีอาการ (อุด/เลือดออก/ทะลุ) หรือ oligometastasis resectable. Neoadjuvant chemoRT ใช้กับ locally advanced rectal ca ที่ไม่มี distant mets."},{"id":"red2-26","src":"red2","n":26,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"An 80-year-old male patient is diagnosed as adenocarcinoma at his transverse colon with invasion to the stomach and metastasis to the liver. No history of cancer is recorded in his family. The patient has 4 48-year-old son.\nWhich one of the following is the best advice for his son regarding the risk of colorectal cancer?","opts":[["A","Do nothing"],["B","Stool occult blood test"],["C","CT scan abdomen"],["D","Colonoscopy"],["E","Esophagogastroscopy and colonoscopy"]],"key":"A","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"CRC ใน \"อายุ ≥ 60\" ของ FDR 1 คน + ไม่มีประวัติครอบครัวอื่น → ความเสี่ยงต่ำ (average risk)","e":"Guideline: FDR เป็น CRC อายุ ≥ 60 ปี (1 คน) → screen แบบ average risk เริ่มอายุ 45–50 ปี. ลูกชายอายุ 48 → ควรเริ่ม screening ตามอายุ (FIT/colonoscopy) ... เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = A \"do nothing\" (ถือว่า average risk ไม่ต้องทำอะไรพิเศษ), LP วง D (colonoscopy เพราะ 48 ปีถึงวัย screening แล้ว). ตามแนวทางปัจจุบัน (เริ่ม screen ที่ 45) ตอบ D สมเหตุสมผลกว่า — แนวคิดข้อสอบคือ \"ไม่ต้องตรวจแบบ high-risk\"."},{"id":"red2-27","src":"red2","n":27,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 25-year-old male presented with change in stool caliber and old blood clot mixed in stool for 6 months. He also lost 6 kilograms in his body weight. His mother and aunt died from rectal cancer at 45- and 50-year-olds, respectively. The physical examination revealed multiple 0.3-cm masses at rectal mucosa with old blood clot.\nWhat is the appropriate investigation?","opts":[["A","Colonoscopy"],["B","Abdominal CT scan"],["C","Coagulogram testing"],["D","Complete blood count"],["E","Stool occult blood test"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"อายุน้อย + CRC ในญาติหลายคนอายุน้อย + มี polyp หลายอัน → hereditary syndrome → ดูทั้ง colon","e":"สงสัย hereditary CRC (Lynch/FAP/attenuated FAP) + มีอาการ (stool caliber เปลี่ยน เลือดปน น้ำหนักลด) → colonoscopy (ดูทั้งลำไส้ + biopsy) เป็นการตรวจที่เหมาะสมที่สุด. CT ใช้ staging ภายหลัง; FOBT ใช้คัดกรองคนไม่มีอาการ."},{"id":"red2-28","src":"red2","n":28,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 38-year-old Thai female was treated with modified radical mastectomy, Pathologic results: invasive ductal carcinoma 2 cm, axillary node positive 1/20 nodes, estrogen receptor negative, progesterone receptor negative, HER2 receptor negative.\nWhat is the next appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Surveillance"],["B","Adjuvant chemotherapy"],["C","Radiotherapy"],["D","Tamoxifen"],["E","Radiotherapy and tamoxifen"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Triple-negative breast cancer → ไม่มี hormonal therapy → chemo คือ systemic treatment หลัก","e":"TNBC, T1c (2 cm) N1 → adjuvant chemotherapy (anthracycline/taxane-based). Tamoxifen ใช้เฉพาะ ER/PR+. RT หลัง MRM (post-mastectomy RT) ใช้เมื่อ ≥ 4 nodes หรือ T3–4 (1–3 nodes พิจารณา) แต่ข้อสำคัญที่สุดในตัวเลือกคือ chemo."},{"id":"red2-29","src":"red2","n":29,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 25-year-old female presents with a mass at the right breast for 1 month. She has no pain and the mass has not increased in size.\nPE: Welf-circumscribed mass 3 cm in diameter at lower outer quadrant of right breast, firm consistency, and movable.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Fibrocystic change"],["B","Fibroadenoma"],["C","Intraductal papilloma"],["D","Phyllodes tumor"],["E","Carcinoma of right breast"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"หญิงอายุน้อย ก้อนกลม ขอบชัด firm เคลื่อนได้ดี (breast mouse) ไม่โต","e":"Fibroadenoma: พบมากสุดในหญิงอายุ 15–35, well-circumscribed, rubbery, highly mobile, ไม่เจ็บ. Phyllodes: ก้อนใหญ่โตเร็ว อายุมากกว่า (40s); fibrocystic: ก้อนเจ็บสัมพันธ์รอบเดือน; papilloma: nipple discharge."},{"id":"red2-30","src":"red2","n":30,"cat":"breast","stem":"For 2 months a 28-year-old female has had bilateral nipple discharge when squeezed. PE of the breasts: no mass, greenish nipple discharge from multiple ducts; no axillary node enlargement\nU/S breast: no mass, no duct dilatation. Which of the following is the most proper next management?","opts":[["A","Cytology from nipple discharge"],["B","Antibiotics"],["C","Observe"],["D","Occult blood test from nipple discharge"],["E","Mammography"]],"key":"D","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Discharge สองข้าง หลายรู สีเขียว ออกเมื่อบีบ ไม่มีก้อน U/S ปกติ = physiologic (duct ectasia/fibrocystic)","e":"Physiologic nipple discharge (bilateral, multiple ducts, provoked, ไม่ใช่เลือด, สีเขียว/เหลือง/ขาว) → reassure และแนะนำให้หยุดบีบ (observe). Pathologic = spontaneous, unilateral, single duct, bloody/serous → work up. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = D occult blood test; LP วง A cytology — ไม่จำเป็นในเคสนี้; ตามหลัก observe."},{"id":"red2-31","src":"red2","n":31,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 50-year-old woman underwent Rt. lobectomy of the thyroid. Following the operating, her voice disappears when she speaks for a while.\nWhich one of the following is the cause of her symptom?","opts":[["A","Injury of the superior thyroid artery"],["B","Injury of the middle thyroid vein"],["C","Injury of the inferior thyroid artery"],["D","Injury of the inferior thyroid vein"],["E","Injury of the thyrocervical trunk"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"เสียงหายเมื่อพูดนาน (voice fatigue) หลัง lobectomy → nerve injury: RLN สัมพันธ์กับ inferior thyroid artery","e":"Recurrent laryngeal nerve วิ่งใกล้ inferior thyroid artery (เสี่ยงขณะผูก ITA) → เสียงแหบ/อ่อนแรง. External branch ของ superior laryngeal nerve วิ่งคู่ superior thyroid artery → เสียงสูงไม่ได้/เสียงเหนื่อยง่าย (voice fatigue) — ข้อสอบนี้เฉลยเลือก ITA (RLN). Concept: STA ↔ EBSLN, ITA ↔ RLN."},{"id":"red2-32","src":"red2","n":32,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 24-year-old man presented with an abscess at the middle of the neck, superior to the thyroid cartilage. The symptom was off and on. The doctor prescribed an antibiotic until the abscess subsided, but the patient could still palpate a 2 cm mass at the location of the previous abscess.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Observe"],["B","X-ray film of the neck"],["C","Excisional biopsy"],["D","Sistrunk operation"],["E","Excision the mass and thyroidectomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ก้อน/abscess แนวกลางคอเหนือ thyroid cartilage เป็นๆหายๆ = infected thyroglossal duct cyst","e":"Thyroglossal duct cyst ที่เคยติดเชื้อ → หลังหายอักเสบ ทำ Sistrunk operation (ตัด cyst + tract + middle portion ของ hyoid bone) เพื่อลด recurrence. ทำ U/S ยืนยันว่ามี thyroid ปกติก่อน. Excision อย่างเดียวกลับเป็นซ้ำสูง."},{"id":"red2-33","src":"red2","n":33,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old man from the northeast region presented with progressive jaundice for 3 months. He noticed he had dark urine.\nPE\nHEENT: Marked jaundice, no lymphadenopathy\nAbd: liver 2 EB below RCM, A mass with cystic consistency was 5 cm in size at the RUQ and moved with respiration. DRE: Pale stool Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","CBD stone"],["B","Liver abscess"],["C","Parasitic infestation"],["D","Chronic cholecystitis"],["E","Periampullary carcinoma"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Progressive painless jaundice + palpable gallbladder (Courvoisier) + pale stool → malignant distal obstruction","e":"Courvoisier's law: GB โตคลำได้ + jaundice = มักไม่ใช่นิ่ว (นิ่วทำให้ GB fibrotic) → periampullary carcinoma (CA head pancreas, ampulla, distal CBD). CBD stone มักปวดและเหลืองเป็นพักๆ. Workup: U/S → CT pancreas protocol."},{"id":"red2-34","src":"red2","n":34,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents with progressive jaundice and symptoms of cholestasis for about 2 months. The physical examination revealed marked jaundice with a palpable gallbladder. LFTs: TB 18, PB76, AST 120, ALT 140, ALP 295, albumin 3.2, globulin 3.0\nWhich of the following is the most proper next management?","opts":[["A","CT whole abdomen"],["B","PTBD"],["C","ERCP"],["D","Liver biopsy"],["E","Gall bladder biopsy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Obstructive jaundice + palpable GB → สงสัย periampullary CA → CT whole abdomen (pancreas protocol) ก่อน intervention","e":"Imaging ก่อน (U/S แล้ว CT) เพื่อหาตำแหน่ง/ระยะและ resectability; ERCP/PTBD ใช้ระบายน้ำดีเมื่อจำเป็น (cholangitis, รอ neoadjuvant) และควรทำหลัง CT เพราะ stent ทำให้แปลภาพยาก + เพิ่ม infection (ดูชุด 1 ข้อ 14). Liver/GB biopsy ไม่ใช่."},{"id":"red2-35","src":"red2","n":35,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 40-year-old woman is found to have a 2-cm dominant nodule located in the right thyroid lobe. Cytologic evaluation of an FNA biopsy specimen reveals \"follicular neoplasm\"\nWhich one of the following is the best management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Core needle biopsy"],["B","I-131 ablation"],["C","Rt. lobectomy"],["D","Repeat FNA biopsy"],["E","Propylthiouracil"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"FNA \"follicular neoplasm\" (Bethesda IV) → แยก adenoma vs carcinoma ไม่ได้จาก cytology → ต้องดู capsular/vascular invasion","e":"Bethesda IV: diagnostic lobectomy (หรือ molecular testing) เพราะการวินิจฉัย follicular carcinoma ต้องดู capsular/vascular invasion จากชิ้นเนื้อทั้งก้อน. Repeat FNA/core biopsy ไม่ช่วยแยก; I-131 ใช้หลัง total thyroidectomy ในมะเร็ง."},{"id":"red2-36","src":"red2","n":36,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 28-year-old female presents with palpitation and weight loss of 2 kg in 6 months.\nPE: P 104/min, Diffuse enlargement of the thyroid gland. serum T3 = 1.4 (0.7 – 1.75) ng/dL, serum TSH 20.21 (0.64 – 3.660 mlU/L = 1\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Periodic follow-up"],["B","Repeat serum T4 and TSH"],["C","TRH stimulation test"],["D","Radioactive iodine"],["E","Antithyroid drug"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Hyperthyroid + diffuse goiter (Graves) — โจทย์ตัวเลขในไฟล์เพี้ยน (TSH ควรต่ำ)","e":"Graves' disease (palpitation, weight loss, tachycardia, diffuse goiter) รักษาได้ 3 ทาง: antithyroid drug, radioactive iodine, surgery. เฉลยรุ่นพี่ = D RAI แต่ในหญิงอายุน้อย 28 ปีส่วนใหญ่ first-line คือ ATD (E) — ระวังข้อนี้ ⚠ ข้อมูล lab ในไฟล์อ่านไม่ชัด."},{"id":"red2-37","src":"red2","n":37,"cat":"fluid","stem":"In addition to lactate, which substance is released from skeletal muscle during anaerobic glycolysis of glucose, which generates ATP and can be used by the liver as a precursor for hepatic gluconeogenesis?","opts":[["A","Arginine"],["B","Histidine"],["C","Alanine"],["D","Glutamine"],["E","Leucine"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Glucose–alanine cycle (Cahill cycle)","e":"กล้ามเนื้อเปลี่ยน pyruvate เป็น alanine (รับ amino group จากการสลาย protein) ส่งไปตับ → gluconeogenesis. Glutamine เป็น amino acid ที่ปล่อยจากกล้ามเนื้อมากที่สุดในภาวะ stress แต่ไปเป็นเชื้อเพลิงของ enterocyte/ไต; โจทย์ถามคู่กับ lactate (Cori cycle) จึงเป็น alanine."},{"id":"red2-38","src":"red2","n":38,"cat":"fluid","stem":"The symptoms of a chronic condition that develops after long-term protein-energy malnutrition include pedal edema, apathy, hepatic enlargement, skin atrophy, depigmentation, and decreased muscle mass. Which one is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Marasmus"],["B","Kwashiorkor"],["C","Short bowel syndrome"],["D","Inflammatory bowel disease"],["E","Mirizzi syndrome"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Protein deficiency (แต่ calorie พอ) → edema, hepatomegaly (fatty liver), depigmentation, apathy","e":"Kwashiorkor = protein malnutrition: hypoalbuminemia → pedal edema, fatty liver (hepatomegaly), skin/hair changes, apathy. Marasmus = protein-energy (calorie) deficiency → ผอมแห้ง สูญเสียไขมัน/กล้ามเนื้อ ไม่บวม."},{"id":"red2-39","src":"red2","n":39,"cat":"fluid","stem":"Which of the following is the cause of hypokalemia?","opts":[["A","After embolectomy for acute limb ischemia"],["B","Primary adrenal insufficiency"],["C","Renal failure"],["D","Angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors"],["E","Loop and thiazide diuretics"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Hypokalemia ← เสีย K ทางไต (diuretic) หรือ GI หรือ shift เข้าเซลล์","e":"Loop/thiazide diuretics เพิ่ม Na delivery ที่ distal nephron → K excretion → hypoK. ตัวเลือกอื่นทำให้ hyperK: reperfusion หลัง embolectomy (K จากกล้ามเนื้อ), adrenal insufficiency (ไม่มี aldosterone), renal failure, ACEI."},{"id":"red2-40","src":"red2","n":40,"cat":"fluid","stem":"Which of the following is the typical change of EKG in hyperkalemia?","opts":[["A","ST-segment elevation"],["B","Prominent waves"],["C","Narrowed or complexes, prominent P waves"],["D","Peaked T waves, shortened QT interval and prolonged PR interval"],["E","Peaked T waves, prolonged QT interval and shortened PR interval"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"HyperK: repolarization เร็ว → T สูงแหลม, QT สั้น; conduction ช้า → PR ยาว, QRS กว้าง","e":"ลำดับ EKG: peaked T + shortened QT → PR prolonged, P flattening → QRS widening → sine wave → VF/asystole. (Hypokalemia: T แบน, U wave, QT/QU ยาว). รุ่นพี่วง E แล้วแก้เป็น D."},{"id":"red2-41","src":"red2","n":41,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 22-year-old woman with severe traumatic brain injury was admitted to the ICU for neurointensive care. On the 7th day of hospitalization, the patient was hemodynamically stable but was producing large amount of urine. Diabetes insipidus was suspected and the patient's blood was tested.\nWhich of the following is the lowest serum sodium concentration (mmol/L) that most likely caused the symptoms in this patient?","opts":[["A","154"],["B","156"],["C","158"],["D","160"],["E","162"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Hypernatremia ทำให้มีอาการทางระบบประสาทเมื่อ Na > 158–160 mmol/L","e":"Hypernatremia ที่ Na > 160 มักมีอาการ (ซึม สับสน ชัก) จึงตอบ 160 ตามเฉลยรุ่นพี่ (iRAT มอ. ที่ตัวเลือกต่างกันเฉลย 165). Concept: อาการขึ้นกับความเร็วที่ Na เพิ่ม และ DI ใน TBI ปัสสาวะมาก Uosm ต่ำ."},{"id":"red2-42","src":"red2","n":42,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 65-year-old man was admitted to an ICU after a transthoraic esophagectomy for esophageal carcinoma. The surgery was uneventful but on the 2nd day after the operation, the blood chemistry results were:\nTest BUN Cr Na+ K+ Cl- HCO -3 Result 19 0.8 136 2.5 98 Ref. units (6-20 (0.67-1.17 (22-29 mg%) (3.4-4.5 mmol/L) (98-107 mg%) (136-145 mmol/L) mmol/L) mmol/L)\nWhich of the following is the estimated total body potassium deficit?","opts":[["A","60 mmol"],["B","70 mmol"],["C","80 mmol"],["D","90 mmol"],["E","100 mmol"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"สูตรคร่าวๆ: K ลด 0.3 mEq/L ≈ ขาด 100 mEq (หรือ ทุก 1 mEq/L ที่ต่ำ ≈ 100–200 mEq) — ข้อนี้ใช้ (เป้า − จริง) × 100","e":"เฉลยรุ่นพี่ใช้ (3.4 − 2.5) × 100 = 90 mmol (คิดจาก lower limit ปกติ 3.4). หลักให้ K: ทาง peripheral ไม่เกิน 10–20 mEq/h, ความเข้มข้น ≤ 40 mEq/L (peripheral); ตรวจ Mg ด้วยเสมอ."},{"id":"red2-43","src":"red2","n":43,"cat":"fluid","stem":"What is the main cation in the interstitial fluid?","opts":[["A","Magnesium"],["B","Potassium"],["C","Sodium"],["D","Protein"],["E","Calcium"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Interstitial fluid เป็นส่วนหนึ่งของ ECF → cation หลัก = Na⁺","e":"ECF (plasma + interstitial) มี Na⁺ ~140 mEq/L เป็น cation หลัก, Cl⁻/HCO₃⁻ เป็น anion หลัก; ICF มี K⁺ เป็น cation หลัก."},{"id":"red2-44","src":"red2","n":44,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 27-year-old man was brought to a trauma center immediately after sustaining a single gunshot to the abdomen. His BP was 90/60 mmHg and HR 140/min. While 2 liters of lactated Ringer's solution were being infused, the BP went down to 70/40 mmHg. The decision was made to transfer the patient to the operating room. Which of the following strategies of fluid therapy is the most appropriate while transferring the patient to the operating room?","opts":[["A","Administration of tranexamic acid"],["B","Activate a massive transfusion protocol"],["C","Change resuscitation fluid to normal saline solution"],["D","Switch resuscitation fluid to 5% human albumin solution"],["E","Continue fluid loading with 2 L of lactated Ringer's solution"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Non-responder ต่อ crystalloid 2 L (BP ยิ่งตก) → หยุด crystalloid → blood products (MTP)","e":"Hemorrhagic shock ที่ไม่ตอบสนอง → activate massive transfusion protocol (PRC:FFP:Plt 1:1:1) + TXA ภายใน 3 ชม. + ไป OR. การให้ crystalloid ต่อทำให้ dilutional coagulopathy/hypothermia/acidosis (lethal triad). TXA ถูกแต่ไม่ใช่ \"fluid strategy\" หลักในข้อนี้."},{"id":"red2-45","src":"red2","n":45,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 39-year-old policeman with transcranial gunshot wounds was admitted to a surgical intensive care unit. Over the first 3 days, the patient was hemodynamically stable but producing 600 mL/h of urine. The blood and urine tests revealed as shown in the chart.\nTest BUN Cr Na+ K+ Cl- HCO -3 Result 31 1.3 160 2.8 110 Ref. units (6-20 (0.67-1.17 (22-29 mg%) (3.4-4.5 mmol/L) (98-107 mg%) (136-145 mmol/L) mmol/L) mmol/L)\nUrine osmolality Serum osmolality Result 180 360 Ref. units 300-900 285-295 mOsm/kg mOsm/kg\nTest Diabetes insipidus was suspected and the urinary loss of free water needs to be determined.\nWhich of the following is the estimated free water clearance rate (mL/min) in this patient?","opts":[["A","5"],["B","6"],["C","7"],["D","8"],["E","9"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Free water clearance = V × (1 − Uosm/Posm)","e":"V = 600 mL/h = 10 mL/min; CH₂O = 10 × (1 − 180/360) = 10 × 0.5 = 5 mL/min. ค่าบวก = ไตขับ free water (DI). รักษา central DI: DDAVP + ทดแทน free water."},{"id":"red2-46","src":"red2","n":46,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 30-year-old female was diagnosed with symptomatic hyponatremia and received treatment in the hospital.\nWhat is the most serious consequence if the serum sodium rises too rapid?","opts":[["A","Brain swelling and herniation"],["B","Osmotic demyelination syndrome"],["C","Syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone (SIADH)"],["D","Central diabetic insipidus"],["E","Papilledema"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"แก้ hyponatremia เร็วเกิน → osmotic demyelination","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 40/95: แก้เกิน 8–10 mEq/L/24 ชม. → osmotic demyelination syndrome (CPM). กลุ่มเสี่ยง: alcoholism, malnutrition, hypokalemia, liver disease, Na < 120."},{"id":"red2-47","src":"red2","n":47,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 38-year-old HIV-positive male patient has developed constipation for 6 months. During the last 2 months, the patient noticed fresh blood following every bowel movement. On anoscopy, a soft pink tissue mass with contact bleeding was found at the 7 o'clock position.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Antibiotic cover gram negative aerobic and anaerobic bacteria"],["B","Bulk-forming agent and drink more water"],["C","Rubber band ligation"],["D","Hemorrhoidectomy"],["E","Suture stop bleeding"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Anoscopy: soft pink mass ที่ 7 o'clock เลือดออกเมื่อสัมผัส + constipation → internal hemorrhoid (ตำแหน่ง 3, 7, 11)","e":"Internal hemorrhoid (left lateral 3, right anterior 11, right posterior 7 o'clock) ร่วมกับ constipation → first-line = fiber/bulk-forming agent + น้ำ. ใน HIV ที่ CD4 ต่ำ ให้ระวังการทำหัตถการ (แผลหายช้า ติดเชื้อ) → conservative ก่อน. (Grade ไม่ระบุ ⇒ เริ่ม conservative)"},{"id":"red2-48","src":"red2","n":48,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 32-year-old female presents with recurrent rectal bleeding after difficult defecation for 3 months without other abnormal symptoms. The physical examination reveals grade I internal hemorrhoids with minimal fresh blood oozing.\nWhat is the most appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","High fiber diet with at least 1 liter of water/day"],["B","Sclerosing therapy"],["C","Osmotic laxative"],["D","Colonoscopy"],["E","Hemorrhoidectomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Hemorrhoid grade I + ปัญหาเบ่งถ่าย → dietary","e":"Grade I: high-fiber diet + น้ำ + ปรับพฤติกรรม (ไม่นั่งนาน ไม่เบ่ง) ± flavonoid. ไม่ต้อง colonoscopy ถ้าอายุน้อยไม่มี alarm feature. Sclerotherapy/RBL เมื่อ conservative ไม่ได้ผล."},{"id":"red2-49","src":"red2","n":49,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained in a motor cycle crash At the ER, he complained of dyspnea.\nPE: Engorged neck vein\nLungs : decrease BS at the right lung, tympanic on percussion\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Needle thoracocentesis at 2nd ICS, mid clavicular line"],["B","Needle thoracocentesis at 2nd ICS, anterior-mid axillary line"],["C","Needle thoracocentesis at 4th-5th ICS, anterior-mid axillary line"],["D","Pericardiocentesis"],["E","Tube thoracostomy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Tension pneumothorax (JVD + BS ลด + tympanic + dyspnea) → needle decompression ทันที","e":"ATLS 10th/11th: needle decompression ในผู้ใหญ่ที่ 4th–5th ICS anterior–mid axillary line (ทั้งนี้ตัวเลือกในไฟล์ใช้ \"2nd ICS anterior–mid axillary\" ไม่ตรง landmark) — เฉลยไฟล์ = C (4th–5th ICS AAL–MAL) ซึ่งตรง ATLS ใหม่. ⚠ ระบบจะบันทึกเฉลยไฟล์ C; 2nd ICS MCL คือตำแหน่งเดิม (ยังใช้ในเด็ก). ตามด้วย chest tube."},{"id":"red2-50","src":"red2","n":50,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"Which of the following is the best diagnostic tool for ischemic colitis?","opts":[["A","CT abdomen"],["B","Colonoscopy"],["C","Barium enema"],["D","MRI abdomen"],["E","Plain abdominal radiography"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Ischemic colitis: CT with IV contrast = first imaging; colonoscopy + biopsy = ยืนยัน","e":"ACG 2015: CT ใช้ประเมินเบื้องต้น (bowel wall thickening ตาม watershed, thumbprinting) และ colonoscopy ภายใน 48 ชม. เป็นการตรวจยืนยันที่ดีที่สุด (เห็น mucosa + biopsy). เฉลยไฟล์ = A (CT); LP วง B (colonoscopy) — ถ้าถาม \"best/confirm\" ตอบ colonoscopy ได้."},{"id":"red2-51","src":"red2","n":51,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 40-year-old man presented with heartburn off and on for 1 year.\nEGD:\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Proton pump inhibitor"],["B","Esophagectomy"],["C","Savary dilation"],["D","Botulinum toxin injection Steroid"],["E","Steroid"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q51-1.jpg"],"t":"Heartburn + EGD เห็น erosive esophagitis (ภาพ mucosal breaks ที่ GEJ) → PPI","e":"GERD with erosive esophagitis → PPI 8 สัปดาห์ (healing) + lifestyle modification. Savary dilation ใช้กับ stricture; botox สำหรับ achalasia; steroid สำหรับ eosinophilic esophagitis; esophagectomy ไม่เกี่ยว."},{"id":"red2-52","src":"red2","n":52,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 18-year-old man presented at the ED after ingestion of a liquid corrosive drain cleaner.\nPE: Stridor, hoarseness\nAbd: No guarding to tracheostomy\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Bronchoalveolar lavage"],["B","Gastroesophageal lavage"],["C","Parenteral corticosteroid"],["D","Exploratory celiotomy"],["E","Tracheostomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Corrosive + stridor + hoarseness (laryngeal edema) → airway — ถ้าเลือกได้ระหว่างตัวเลือก: surgical airway","e":"Airway compromise จาก corrosive ที่ larynx → intubation อาจยาก/อันตราย (เนื้อเยื่อบวม เปราะ) → tracheostomy (surgical airway) เป็นตัวเลือกที่ให้ใน set นี้ (เฉลยไฟล์ + LP = E). ห้าม lavage/induce vomiting; steroid ไม่ลด stricture ชัดเจน."},{"id":"red2-53","src":"red2","n":53,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 16-year-old woman had tight lower quadrant abdominal pain for 10 hours. This pain started gradually at RLQ with migration. She has anorexia, nausea, and vomiting but no diarrhea or dysuria. The physical examination revealed BT 37°C, RLQ tenderness without rebound tenderness, soft abdomen, with normoactive bowel sounds. UA was normal. CBC showed WBC count of 8,000/mm and PMN 70%.\nWhich of the following is the score of the Alvarado scale?","opts":[["A","2"],["B","5"],["C","7"],["D","8"],["E","10"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Alvarado ทีละตัว: migration 1 + anorexia 1 + N/V 1 + RLQ tender 2 + rebound 0 + temp 0 + WBC 0 + shift 0","e":"= 5 (เทียบชุด 1 ข้อ 53 ที่ไม่มี migration/A/N/V ได้ 2). WBC ต้อง > 10,000 และ PMN > 75% จึงได้คะแนน; BT ≥ 37.3 °C. Score 5–6 = equivocal → observe/imaging."},{"id":"red2-54","src":"red2","n":54,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 35-year-old male presents with RLQ pain for 5 days. He has had nausea and vomiting. He has a history of pulmonary TB and has been under treatment for 3 months.\nPE: BT 389C, BP 120/70, PR 90/min\nAbdomen: ill-defined mass at RLQ with tenderness\nCBC: WBC 12,000, PMN 85, bands 4, lymphs 11\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Acute appendicitis"],["B","TB cecum"],["C","Appendiceal abscess"],["D","CA colony"],["E","Diverticulitis"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ปวด RLQ 5 วัน + ก้อน RLQ กดเจ็บ + ไข้ + WBC สูง → appendiceal mass/abscess (แม้มีประวัติ TB)","e":"อาการเฉียบพลัน 5 วัน + PMN 85% เป็น acute bacterial process → appendiceal abscess. Ileocecal TB มักเป็นเรื้อรัง (weight loss, chronic diarrhea, doughy mass) ไม่ใช่ไข้สูงเฉียบพลัน PMN สูง (กำลังรักษา TB อยู่ 3 เดือนด้วย). CA colon อายุน้อยไม่น่าใช่."},{"id":"red2-55","src":"red2","n":55,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 25-year-old man presented with right lower quadrant pain for 5 days. He also had nausea and vomiting. Five days PTA he went to a private clinic and received oral antibiotics, but the pain persisted.\nPE: BT38.5°C, P 110/min\nAbd: Moderate distension and a 5-cm mass was palpated at the RLO and the abdomen was tender\nU/S: 5-cm hypoechoic mass with posterior enhancement and air-fluid level.\nWhich of the following is the best treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","Exploratory laparotomy"],["B","Percutaneous drainage"],["C","U/S guided biopsy"],["D","IV Antibiotics"],["E","Emergency appendectomy & Percutaneous drainage"]],"key":"D","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Appendiceal abscess ที่ระบายได้ (5 cm มี air-fluid level) → percutaneous drainage + ATB","e":"Perforated appendicitis with well-formed abscess (> 3 cm): CT/US-guided percutaneous drainage + IV ATB แล้วพิจารณา interval appendectomy ภายหลัง. IV ATB อย่างเดียวพอสำหรับ phlegmon/abscess เล็ก; emergency appendectomy ในระยะนี้ผ่าตัดยาก ภาวะแทรกซ้อนสูง. LP วง B (เฉลยไฟล์ Med46 = D)."},{"id":"red2-56","src":"red2","n":56,"cat":"hernia","stem":"What is a nomenclature for this type of inguinal hernia?","opts":[["A","Richter's hernia"],["B","Littre hernia"],["C","Sliding hernia"],["D","Ainyand's hernia"],["E","Spigelian hernia"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q56-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: มีเพียงผนังลำไส้บางส่วน (antimesenteric border) ติดอยู่ในช่องไส้เลื่อน","e":"Richter's hernia = ติดเฉพาะส่วนหนึ่งของผนังลำไส้ → อาจ strangulate/เน่าโดยไม่มีอาการอุดตัน (ลำไส้ยังเปิด). Littre = Meckel's diverticulum ใน hernia sac; Amyand = appendix ใน inguinal hernia; sliding = อวัยวะเป็นส่วนหนึ่งของผนังถุง; Spigelian = ผ่าน semilunar line."},{"id":"red2-57","src":"red2","n":57,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents with a right groin mass for 6 hours. He has no fever, no abdominal pain, and no clinical conditions of gut obstruction He has had the right groin mass off and on for 2 years. The physical examination showed BT 36.8°C, BP 120/80 mmHg, PR 80/min, RR 16/min and a groin mass that is 15 cm at his right groin and scrotum without tenderness or redness.\nWhat is the diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hydrocele"],["B","Incarcerated inguinal hernia"],["C","Strangulated inguinal hernia"],["D","Hematoma at scrotum"],["E","Femoral hernia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q57-1.jpg"],"t":"ก้อนขาหนีบ-อัณฑะดันไม่กลับ (6 ชม.) แต่ไม่มีอาการอุดตัน/ไม่มี inflammation","e":"Incarcerated = ดันกลับไม่ได้ แต่เลือดยังไปเลี้ยง (ไม่ปวดมาก ไม่แดง ไม่ไข้); strangulated = มี ischemia (ปวด กดเจ็บ แดง ไข้ ± gut obstruction). เคสนี้ไม่มี sign ของ strangulation → incarcerated inguinal hernia."},{"id":"red2-58","src":"red2","n":58,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 74-year-old man presents with a small bulge in his right groin that he first noticed 2 months earlier that ache slightly. His underlying diseases include COPD with pulmonary hypertension, atrial fibrillation on anticoagulant, and diabetes mellitus. On physical examination, he has a moderately sized reducible right inguinal hernia as well as a small reducible left inguinal hernia.\nWhich is the most appropriate management for this patient at this moment?","opts":[["A","Open right-sided tension-free repair"],["B","Open bilateral tension free repair"],["C","Transabdominal preperitoneal repair (TAPP)"],["D","Total extraperitoneal repair (TEP)"],["E","Non-operative management (observation)"]],"key":"A","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Bilateral inguinal hernia ในคนเสี่ยง GA สูง (COPD + PHT) → open repair ใต้ local/regional ทั้งสองข้างพร้อมกัน","e":"Laparoscopic (TAPP/TEP) ต้อง GA + pneumoperitoneum ไม่เหมาะกับ COPD/pulmonary hypertension. ผู้ป่วยมีอาการ (ache) → ควรผ่าตัด; เมื่อต้องผ่าตัดอยู่แล้วซ่อมทั้งสองข้างในครั้งเดียวด้วย open tension-free (Lichtenstein) ใต้ local anesthesia. Observation (watchful waiting) ใช้ในคนไม่มีอาการ/น้อยมาก — เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = A, LP วง E; บทเรียน Day 1 ตอบ B."},{"id":"red2-59","src":"red2","n":59,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 23-year-old male presents with right inguinal pain for 2 hours. He has had an intermittent right inguinal mass for 1 year and it became irreducible in the last 6 hours. The physical examination reveals erythema, warmth, and tenderness over the mass.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Reduce and follow-up"],["B","Reduce and elective inguinal hernia repair"],["C","Admit for antibiotic therapy"],["D","Repair inguinal hernia and/or bowel resection"],["E","Reduce and admit observing clinical signs/symptoms"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Irreducible + แดง ร้อน กดเจ็บ = strangulated → ห้าม reduce","e":"Strangulated hernia → emergency surgery: เปิดดูลำไส้, ประเมิน viability, resect ลำไส้ที่ตาย แล้ว repair hernia (มักไม่ใช้ mesh ถ้าปนเปื้อน). การดันกลับอาจทำให้ลำไส้ที่ตายแล้วกลับเข้าช่องท้อง (reduction en masse)."},{"id":"red2-60","src":"red2","n":60,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"What is the most common etiology of small bowel obstruction in adults?","opts":[["A","Adhesion band"],["B","Groin hernia"],["C","Internal hernia"],["D","Intussusception"],["E","Intestinal TB"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"SBO ผู้ใหญ่: adhesion > hernia > malignancy (ในคนที่เคยผ่าตัด)","e":"Adhesive band จากการผ่าตัดช่องท้องเดิมเป็นสาเหตุที่พบบ่อยที่สุดของ SBO ในผู้ใหญ่ (~60–75%); ในคนไม่เคยผ่าตัด hernia เป็นสาเหตุสำคัญ; intussusception พบในเด็ก."},{"id":"red2-61","src":"red2","n":61,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 40-year-man presented with nausea and vomiting for 8 hours. He complained of colicky pain every 10-15 min. He had flatus 3 hours ago. His last bowel movement was yesterday, and he has no fever. PE\nAbd: Old surgical scare at RLQ, mild tenderness at LUQ, hyperactive bowel sound. Abdominal film:\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Small bowel obstruction"],["B","Colonic obstruction"],["C","Small bowel ileus"],["D","Pseudo-colonic obstruction"],["E","Gallstone ileus"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q61-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ upright: SB loop โป่งหลาย loop + air-fluid level หลายระดับ (step-ladder) + ยังมีลม/อุจจาระใน colon บ้าง","e":"Colicky pain + vomiting + hyperactive BS + old scar + ภาพ multiple air-fluid levels ใน SB = small bowel obstruction (partial ยังผายลมได้). Ileus จะโป่งทั้ง SB และ colon + BS ลดลง; gallstone ileus มี pneumobilia."},{"id":"red2-62","src":"red2","n":62,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 23-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months ago presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea, and bilious vomiting with fever and obstipation. The physical examination revealed localized marked tenderness and guarding at the suprapubic area and mild abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds. An acute abdominal series revealed a 3 cm dilatation of one loop of the small bowel at the mid-part of the abdomen with no gas the colon or rectum.\nWhat is the most likely provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Paralytic ileus"],["B","Partial large bowel obstruction"],["C","Partial small bowel obstruction"],["D","Complete large bowel obstruction"],["E","Strangulated small bowel obstruction"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"SBO + ไข้ + tachycardia + localized peritonitis + complete (ไม่มีลมใน colon/rectum) = strangulation","e":"Signs ของ strangulation: ไข้, tachycardia, leukocytosis, peritoneal irritation/ปวดต่อเนื่อง, acidosis (lactate). One loop ที่โป่งค้าง (sentinel/closed loop) + obstipation = closed-loop/strangulated SBO → emergency laparotomy."},{"id":"red2-63","src":"red2","n":63,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 70-year-old female presented with abdominal distension, obstipation, and constipation for 1 day. On physical examination, there were no signs of peritonitis. DRE showed empty rectum.\nAbdominal film showed\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","CT abdomen x"],["B","Barium enema"],["C","Endoscopic decompression"],["D","Explore-lap with sigmoid resection"],["E","NG tube decompression and observe abdominal signs"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q63-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: colon รูป coffee bean / inverted U ใหญ่จาก pelvis = sigmoid volvulus ไม่มี peritonitis","e":"Sigmoid volvulus ไม่มี sign of ischemia/peritonitis → endoscopic detorsion (flexible sigmoidoscopy) + rectal tube แล้วจึงทำ elective sigmoidectomy ใน admission เดียวกัน (recurrence สูง). มี peritonitis/gangrene → emergency Hartmann's. CT ช่วยยืนยันได้แต่ไม่ใช่การรักษา. LP ✗ ใต้ E แต่ตามหลัก WSES = C (ตรงเฉลยไฟล์)."},{"id":"red2-64","src":"red2","n":64,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 40-year-old man presented with epigastrium pain for 4 hours after heavy alcohol drinking.\nPE: BT 38°C, No jaundice\nAbd: Mild distension and marked tenderness at the epigastrium\nAcute abdominal film: dilatation of the small bowel and transverse colon, no pneumoperitoneum\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Film abdomen left lateral decubitus"],["B","Retain NG tube and push air then repeat film abdomen"],["C","Serum amylase"],["D","Ultrasound abdomen"],["E","Gastroscopy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ดื่มเหล้าหนัก + ปวด epigastrium + ฟิล์ม colon cut-off/sentinel loop → สงสัย acute pancreatitis","e":"Plain film ใน pancreatitis: sentinel loop (localized SB ileus), colon cut-off sign (transverse colon โป่งถึง splenic flexure); ไม่มี free air ตัด perforation → serum amylase/lipase (> 3 เท่า) ยืนยัน. Gastroscopy ห้ามในสงสัย perforation."},{"id":"red2-65","src":"red2","n":65,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 22-year-old virgin female presented with severe anal pain during and after defecation for 4 months. She has always had constipation and passes hard stool. Sometimes, streaks of fresh blood were detected at the toilet paper.\nWhich was the suspected finding from anal physical examination?","opts":[["A","Bluish-purplish mass"],["B","Foul-smell discharge"],["C","Fibroepithelial polyp"],["D","Large ulcerative lesion"],["E","Cauliflower mass"]],"key":"B","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Anal pain ระหว่างและหลังถ่าย + เลือดสดเปื้อนกระดาษ + ท้องผูกเรื้อรัง 4 เดือน = chronic anal fissure","e":"Chronic fissure มี sentinel pile (fibroepithelial skin tag) ที่ปลายล่างของ fissure และ hypertrophied anal papilla ด้านบน. Bluish mass = thrombosed external hemorrhoid; foul discharge = fistula/abscess; cauliflower = condyloma; ulcerative lesion = CA/STD. เฉลยไฟล์ไฮไลต์ทั้ง B, C; ไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 55 ไฮไลต์ fibroepithelial polyp (C)."},{"id":"red2-66","src":"red2","n":66,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 55-year-old male presented with recurrent perianal drainage for 6 months. He had no abnormal bowel habit or other gastrointestinal symptoms. Physical examination revealed a small opening at 8 o clock at 3 cm from the anal verge.\nWhere was the most likely source of this pathology?","opts":[["A","4 o clock at anal verge"],["B","6 o clock at dentate line"],["C","8 o clock at anal verge"],["D","10 o clock at dentate line"],["E","12 o clock at anal verge"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Goodsall's rule: external opening หลังแนว transverse anal line → tract โค้งเข้า posterior midline (6 o'clock)","e":"Opening ที่ 8 o'clock (posterior half) ห่าง 3 cm → internal opening อยู่ที่ dentate line posterior midline 6 o'clock. Opening ใน anterior half (< 3 cm) → tract ตรงเข้า radial. (opening ห่าง > 3 cm แม้อยู่ anterior ก็มักโค้งไป posterior midline)"},{"id":"red2-67","src":"red2","n":67,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 46-year-old healthy female presented with painful bowel movement and a low grade fever for 2 days. The physical examination revealed a tender lump with a foul smell discharge at the perianal area with redness.\nWhat is the appropriate management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Incision and drainage"],["B","Antibiotics"],["C","Clot evacuation"],["D","Hemorrhoidectomy"],["E","Laxative drug"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ก้อนเจ็บ + แดง + ไข้ + มีหนองที่ perianal = perianal abscess","e":"Perianal abscess → incision and drainage (ไม่ต้องรอ fluctuation); ATB เสริมเฉพาะ cellulitis กว้าง, immunocompromised, DM, valvular disease. Clot evacuation สำหรับ thrombosed external hemorrhoid."},{"id":"red2-68","src":"red2","n":68,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 60-year-old male presented with severe generalized abdominal pain for 1 day. Two days ago, he had pain at periumbilical area that shifted to the right lower quadrant area during the next 6 hours. He also had a low-grade fever and nausea without vomiting. Today the pain has progressed. He has no history of abdominal surgery or underlying disease. Physical examination reveals loss of liver dullness with generalized severe tenderness and involuntary guarding at his abdomen.\nWhich is the suspected finding in his acute abdominal plain film?","opts":[["A","Pneumatosis intestinalis"],["B","String of pearl sign"],["C","Triangular sign => perforation"],["D","Step ladder pattern obstruction"],["E","Target sign"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Appendicitis 2 วัน → generalized peritonitis + loss of liver dullness = perforation มี free air","e":"Loss of liver dullness บ่งว่ามี free air → upright CXR/left lateral decubitus: free air ใต้ diaphragm; supine: Rigler sign, triangular sign (ลมรูปสามเหลี่ยมระหว่าง loop ลำไส้), football sign. String of pearls = SBO ที่มีน้ำมาก; step ladder = SBO; target sign = intussusception; pneumatosis = ischemia."},{"id":"red2-69","src":"red2","n":69,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old known case of cirrhosis presents with diffuse abdominal pain for 2 days, fever of 38.5°C and nausea and vomiting. Laboratory findings include a WBC count of 16,300 with 7% bands. On physical examination his abdomen is soft, but he has generalized tenderness with positive for shifting dullness.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Serial physical examination"],["B","Abdominal tapping"],["C","Abdominal computed tomography"],["D","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"],["E","Colonoscopy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Cirrhosis + ascites + ไข้ + ปวดท้อง → สงสัย SBP → diagnostic paracentesis ทันที","e":"Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis: ascitic PMN ≥ 250/mm³ ยืนยัน → IV cefotaxime/ceftriaxone + albumin. ต้อง tap ก่อนให้ ATB (เพาะเชื้อใน blood culture bottle). CT ใช้เมื่อสงสัย secondary peritonitis."},{"id":"red2-70","src":"red2","n":70,"cat":"infection","stem":"Which of following method can reduce risk of surgical site infection?","opts":[["A","Preoperative oral antibiotic at least 3 days"],["B","Antibiotic before incision less than 30 min"],["C","Glycemic control < 200 mg/dL in a non-diabetic patient"],["D","Irrigate abdominal wound with antibiotic"],["E","Supplemental warming to decrease bacterial colonization"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"มาตรการลด SSI ที่มีหลักฐาน: prophylaxis ภายใน 60 นาที, glycemic control < 200, normothermia, O₂, ไม่โกน","e":"WHO/CDC แนะนำ perioperative glycemic control (< 200 mg/dL) ทั้งในผู้ป่วยเบาหวานและไม่เป็นเบาหวาน. Oral ATB 3 วันไม่แนะนำ (ยกเว้น oral ATB + mechanical bowel prep ใน colorectal); irrigation แผลด้วย ATB ไม่แนะนำ; warming ลด SSI ผ่านการเพิ่ม tissue perfusion/immune function ไม่ใช่ลด colonization."},{"id":"red2-71","src":"red2","n":71,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 30-year-old man presented with progressive right low quadrant abdominal pain for 7 days, fever of 38.5°C, nausea, and vomiting. Laboratory findings included a WBC count of 18,300 with 7% bands. On physical examination his abdomen is soft, but he has marked tenderness with a mass in the right upper quadrant. A CT abdomen showed uni-loculated rim enhancing lesion 8 cm at RLQ.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Percutaneous drainage"],["B","Percutaneous aspiration"],["C","Laparotomy and drainage"],["D","Laparoscopy and drainage"],["E","Laparotomy and excision"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Appendiceal abscess ขนาดใหญ่ uniloculated (8 cm) ที่เข้าถึงได้ → percutaneous drainage","e":"Abscess > 3–4 cm → image-guided percutaneous drainage (catheter) + IV ATB; aspiration ครั้งเดียวมัก recurrence. Laparotomy เมื่อ drain ไม่ได้/peritonitis ทั่วไป/ไม่ดีขึ้น. (โจทย์เขียน mass ที่ right upper quadrant แต่ CT ที่ RLQ — retrocecal appendix)"},{"id":"red2-72","src":"red2","n":72,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old known case of cirrhosis presented with diffuse abdominal pain for 2 days, fever, nausea, and vomiting. On physical examination his abdomen was soft, but he had generalized tenderness with shifting dullness positive. An abdominal film showed no pneumoperitoneum. CBC: WBC count of 17,300 with 8% bands. Paracentesis was performed. Fluid analysis showed 500 WBCs/mL without organisms on Gram stain. Which one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Abdominal computed tomography"],["B","Intravenous antibiotic"],["C","Percutaneous drainage"],["D","Diagnostic laparoscopy"],["E","Laparotomy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Ascitic WBC 500 (PMN เกิน 250) + Gram stain ไม่พบเชื้อ + ไม่มี free air = SBP","e":"SBP (monomicrobial, ไม่ต้องผ่าตัด) → IV third-generation cephalosporin + albumin (1.5 g/kg day1, 1 g/kg day3). ถ้าสงสัย secondary peritonitis (polymicrobial, glucose < 50, LDH สูง, protein > 1 g/dL, free air) จึงทำ CT/ผ่าตัด."},{"id":"red2-73","src":"red2","n":73,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 58-year-old male presented with high grade fever and chills for 1 week,\nPE: BT 39.5°C, BP 135/min, RR 24/min\nHEENT: no jaundice Abdomen: marked tenderness at the right upper quadrant of the abdomen. U/S abdomen: multiple hypoechoic mass with rim enhancement 1-2 cm in size at the right lobe of the liver.\nWhat of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","IV antibiotics"],["B","Percutaneous drainage"],["C","Open drainage"],["D","Hepatectomy"],["E","Intra lesion injection with hypertonic solution"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Multiple small (1–2 cm) liver abscesses → ระบายไม่ได้/ไม่คุ้ม → IV ATB อย่างเดียว","e":"Pyogenic liver abscess ขนาด < 3–5 cm หรือหลายก้อนเล็ก → IV antibiotics (คลุม Klebsiella/E. coli/anaerobe) 4–6 สัปดาห์; abscess เดี่ยว > 5 cm → percutaneous drainage + ATB; open drainage เมื่อ rupture/ล้มเหลว. ควรหาแหล่ง (biliary, colon)."},{"id":"red2-74","src":"red2","n":74,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 42-year-old presents with RUQ pain and fever for 2 days.\nPE: Mild jaundice\nAbdomen: Tenderness at RUQ, no mass\nPE: WBC 10,000/mm', PMN 80, bands 2, lymphs 17, mono 1 LFT: bilirubin 3.00 mg/dL, direct bilirubin 2.4 mg/dL, SGOT 40 U/L, SGPT 40 U/L, alkaline phosphatase 120 U/L, total protein 8 g/dL, albumin 5 g/dL\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate initial investigation?","opts":[["A","Acute abdominal series of X-rays"],["B","Abdominal CT scan"],["C","Ultrasound of the liver and biliary system"],["D","ERCP"],["E","Upper GI-series"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"RUQ pain + fever + jaundice (direct hyperbilirubinemia) → U/S ก่อนเสมอ","e":"U/S hepatobiliary = initial investigation: ดู gallstone, CBD/IHD dilatation, liver abscess. ถ้า CBD dilated/สงสัยนิ่ว → MRCP/EUS/ERCP ตาม risk. ERCP เป็นหัตถการรักษา ไม่ใช่การตรวจแรก."},{"id":"red2-75","src":"red2","n":75,"cat":"hpb","stem":"What is the most appropriate initial investigation in the case of clinical suspicion of acute cholecystitis?","opts":[["A","CT scan of abdomen"],["B","Scintigraphy"],["C","Ultrasonography of hepatobiliary region"],["D","MRI of hepatobiliary region"],["E","Laparoscopy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Acute cholecystitis: first-line imaging = U/S (Tokyo 2018)","e":"U/S: GB wall > 4 mm, pericholecystic fluid, sonographic Murphy, GB distension, stone impacted. HIDA scan (scintigraphy) แม่นที่สุด (sensitivity สูงสุด) ใช้เมื่อ U/S ไม่ชัด; CT/MRI ใช้เมื่อสงสัย complication."},{"id":"red2-76","src":"red2","n":76,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 40-year-old female presented with RUQ abdominal pain that radiates to the right scapula for 1 day. She has a fever without jaundice\nPE: BT 38°C. PR 80/min. BP 120/80 mmHg, and moderate tenderness at the RUQ area.\nLFT: DB 0.8 mg%, TB 0.9 mg%, AST 30 U/L, ALT 25 U/L, ALP 80 U/L\nU/S abdomen shows multiple gallstones, gallbladder is 8x4-em in diameter, wall thickness is 4 mm with some pericholecystic fluid. The CBD is 5 mm in diameter.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Acute cholangitis"],["B","Acute cholecystitis"],["C","Choledocholithiasis"],["D","Pyogenic liver abscess"],["E","Symptomatic gallstone"]],"key":"A","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"RUQ pain + ไข้ + U/S: stones + wall thickness + pericholecystic fluid + CBD ปกติ + LFT ปกติ","e":"Tokyo criteria: local inflammation (RUQ pain/Murphy) + systemic (fever) + imaging → acute cholecystitis. ไม่เหลือง LFT ปกติ CBD 5 mm → ไม่ใช่ cholangitis/choledocholithiasis. รักษา: ATB + early laparoscopic cholecystectomy (ภายใน 72 ชม.–7 วัน)."},{"id":"red2-77","src":"red2","n":77,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 55-year-old obese female incidentally found a 2 cm polyp in the gall bladder from an annual checkup without any symptoms.\nWhich one of the following is the most proper management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Advice follow up"],["B","Extended cholecystectomy"],["C","Computed tomography of liver X"],["D","Laparoscopic cholecystectomy"],["E","Endoscopic retrograde cholangiography"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Gallbladder polyp ≥ 1 cm → เสี่ยงมะเร็ง → cholecystectomy","e":"GB polyp ≥ 10 mm (หรือ 6–9 mm + risk factor: อายุ > 50, PSC, Indian ethnicity, sessile) → laparoscopic cholecystectomy. Polyp > 18–20 mm สงสัยมะเร็งมาก อาจต้อง staging (CT) และ extended cholecystectomy ถ้ายืนยันมะเร็ง. Polyp < 6 mm ติดตาม U/S."},{"id":"red2-78","src":"red2","n":78,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 55-year-old man presented with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 1 day. Physical examination revealed good consciousness, T 38°C, P 100/min, RR 24/min, BP 120/80 mmHg. His abdomen was distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds. CBC: Hb 12 gm%, WBC 13,000/mm 3 , platelet 300,000 /mm 3 , BUN 20 mg%, Cr 1.5 mg% and amylase 1,500 IU/L; the CXR was normal. According to the Bedside Index for Severity of Acute Pancreatitis (BISAP) score, which one of the following is the score in this patient?","opts":[["A","0"],["B","1"],["C","2"],["D","3"],["E","4"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"BISAP 5 ข้อ: BUN > 25, Impaired mental status, SIRS ≥ 2, Age > 60, Pleural effusion","e":"BUN 20 (0), mental ดี (0), SIRS: T 38 (>38? = 38.0 ไม่เกิน → 0), HR 100 (>90 ✔), RR 24 (>20 ✔), WBC 13,000 (>12,000 ✔) → SIRS ≥ 2 = 1 คะแนน; อายุ 55 (0); CXR ปกติ (0) → BISAP = 1. ≥ 3 = severe risk."},{"id":"red2-79","src":"red2","n":79,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 1 day. Physical examination reveals good consciousness, T 38 °C, P 100/min, RR 24/min, BP 120/80 mmHg. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds. Lab: CBC: Hb 12 gm%, WBC 13,000/mm', platelet 300,000 /mm', BUN 20 mg%, Cr 1.5 mg%, and amylase 1,500 IU/L\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate analgesic drug?","opts":[["A","Opioid"],["B","Steroid"],["C","Gabapentin"],["D","Paracetamol"],["E","Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Acute pancreatitis ปวดรุนแรง → opioid ได้ (ไม่มีหลักฐานว่า morphine ทำให้แย่จริง)","e":"ปวดรุนแรงใน acute pancreatitis ใช้ opioid (morphine/fentanyl/hydromorphone) ได้อย่างปลอดภัย; NSAIDs เลี่ยงเพราะ AKI risk (Cr 1.5 แล้ว). Steroid ไม่มีบทบาท; paracetamol ไม่พอสำหรับ severe pain."},{"id":"red2-80","src":"red2","n":80,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 1 day. Physical examination reveals good consciousness. His vital signs are T 38°C, P 100/min, RR 24/min, BP 120/80 mmHg. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds.\nBlood chemistry: CBC: Hb 12 gm%, WBC 13,000 /mm\", platelet count 300,000/mm', BUN 20 mg%, Cr 1.5 mg%, and amylase 1,500 IU/L\nLFTs: total bilirubin 0.4mg/dL, direct bilirubin 0.2 mg/dL, ALP 50 U/L\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Nasogastric intubation"],["B","Intravenous analgesics"],["C","Intravenous antibiotics"],["D","Diagnostic laparoscopy"],["E","ERCP"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Mild acute pancreatitis ไม่ใช่ gallstone (LFT ปกติ) → supportive: fluid + analgesia + early feeding","e":"ตัวเลือกที่เหมาะคือ IV analgesics (ร่วมกับ fluid resuscitation). NG tube เฉพาะอาเจียน/ileus มาก; ไม่ให้ prophylactic ATB; ERCP ใช้ใน gallstone pancreatitis ที่มี cholangitis; diagnostic laparoscopy ไม่เกี่ยว."},{"id":"red2-81","src":"red2","n":81,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 63-year-old male with a history of aortic surgery from AAA presented with massive bloody stool. The physical examination shows BP 90/60 mmHg and PR 130/min.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Bleeding diverticulosis"],["B","Aortoenteric fistula"],["C","Variceal bleeding"],["D","Angiodysplasia"],["E","Bleeding peptic ulcer"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Massive GI bleed + ประวัติผ่าตัด aorta (graft) = aortoenteric fistula จนกว่าจะพิสูจน์ได้ว่าไม่ใช่","e":"Secondary aortoenteric fistula (graft กัดกร่อน 3rd/4th part duodenum) → \"herald bleed\" ตามด้วย massive bleeding. ต้อง EGD ถึง distal duodenum/CTA อย่างรวดเร็ว และผ่าตัด (เอา graft ออก + extra-anatomic bypass หรือ in situ). ตัวเลือกอื่นไม่สัมพันธ์กับประวัติ aortic graft."},{"id":"red2-82","src":"red2","n":82,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 24-year-old male has had severe anal pain during defecation for 3 days. Two years ago, the patient experienced this same kind of pain once. Last week he passed very hard stool without any bleeding. After that he has been suffering anal discomfort until now. The patient refuses to have his anus examined due to severe pain.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Antibiotic cover gram negative aerobic and anaerobic bacteria"],["B","Bulk-forming agent and drink more water"],["C","Colonoscopy"],["D","Examination under anesthesia"],["E","Hemorrhoidectomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ปวดมากเวลาถ่าย หลังถ่ายอุจจาระแข็ง ตรวจทวารไม่ได้เพราะเจ็บ = acute anal fissure","e":"Acute anal fissure: conservative (bulk-forming agent/fiber + น้ำ + sitz bath + topical anesthetic ± nitrate/diltiazem) หายได้ ~50–80%. ถ้าสงสัยอื่นหรือไม่ดีขึ้นจึงทำ EUA. Hemorrhoidectomy ใช้กับ hemorrhoid grade III–IV หรือ thrombosed external hemorrhoid < 72 ชม. (โจทย์ไม่มีก้อน). เฉลยไฟล์ไฮไลต์ทั้ง B, E; LP = B."},{"id":"red2-83","src":"red2","n":83,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 60-year-old male presented at the hospital with LLQ pain for 1 day.\nPE: T 38.5°C, P 100/min\nAbd: Localized guarding at LLQ Hypoactive bowel sounds PR: No mass\nAcute abdomen series: no free air, generalized small bowel dilatation without air-fluid level\nCT abdomen: 5 cm pericolic abscess around sigmoid colon\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Colostomy"],["B","Percutaneous drainage"],["C","Exploratory laparotomy with abdominal toilet"],["D","Colectomy with Hartmann procedure"],["E","NPO, NG decompression, and observation"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Diverticulitis Hinchey II (pericolic abscess 5 cm) → percutaneous drainage + ATB","e":"Abscess ≥ 3–4 cm ระบายด้วย CT-guided percutaneous drainage + IV ATB; Hinchey III–IV จึงผ่าตัด (Hartmann/resection + anastomosis). ไม่ทำ colostomy อย่างเดียว."},{"id":"red2-84","src":"red2","n":84,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents with rapid onset of left iliac fossa pain and fever for 1 day. He has tenderness in the left iliac fossa but there is no obvious palpable mass. Body temperature is 37.7°C, pulse 84 bpm, and white cell count 14,000. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Acute appendicitis"],["B","Sigmoid cancer"],["C","Crohn's disease of the colon"],["D","Acute sigmoid diverticulitis"],["E","Ureteric colic"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"LLQ pain + ไข้ต่ำ + WBC สูง ในผู้สูงอายุ = \"left-sided appendicitis\"","e":"Acute sigmoid diverticulitis เป็นสาเหตุที่พบบ่อยที่สุดของ LLQ pain + fever ในผู้สูงอายุ. Appendicitis ปวด RLQ; ureteric colic ปวด colicky ร้าวลงขาหนีบ ไม่มีไข้; Crohn's มักอายุน้อย; cancer มักไม่ acute."},{"id":"red2-85","src":"red2","n":85,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 60-year-old man with hypertension and dyslipidemia for 20 years presents with abdominal pain for 6 hours prior to arrival at the hospital. PE: BP 150/80 mmHg, PR 80/min, RR 20/min, BT 37.5'c\nAbdomen - - -\nAbdominal pulsatile mass 6 cm in maximal diameter with tenderness at aneurysm sac at left side No rebound Expansile pulsation - positive\nWhich of the following is the appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","CTA-abdomen"],["B","Set OR for open repair AAA"],["C","Observe clinical conditions"],["D","Follow-up with duplex color ultrasound abdomen in the next 6 months"],["E","Diagnose with angiography"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"AAA 6 cm + \"tender\" ที่ถุง aneurysm + ปวดท้อง = symptomatic AAA (impending rupture) → ผ่าตัดเร่งด่วน","e":"Symptomatic (tender) AAA ถือเป็น urgent repair แม้ hemodynamic ยัง stable. ถ้า stable มีเวลา → CTA เพื่อวางแผน EVAR vs open repair (เฉลยไฟล์ = A CTA); ถ้า unstable/สงสัย rupture → OR ทันทีโดยไม่ต้อง imaging. ⚠ เฉลยไฟล์ A — ในทางปฏิบัติ stable symptomatic AAA ทำ CTA ก่อนผ่าตัดเร่งด่วน ซึ่งสมเหตุสมผล; ตอบ A ได้ถ้าโจทย์เน้น \"stable\". (ระบบนี้ยึดเฉลยไฟล์ A)"},{"id":"red2-86","src":"red2","n":86,"cat":"vascular","stem":"Which one of the following is NOT the treatment for chronic femoropopliteal vein thrombosis?","opts":[["A","Swimming"],["B","Sclerotherapy"],["C","Elevated leg at night"],["D","Occlusive dressing with compressive dressing"],["E","Graduated compressive stocking pressure 20-30 mm Hg."]],"key":"E","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Chronic DVT/post-thrombotic → หลัก = compression + elevation + exercise; sclerotherapy เป็นการรักษา superficial varicose","e":"Post-thrombotic syndrome: compression stocking (20–30/30–40 mmHg), elevate leg, exercise (ว่ายน้ำ/เดิน calf muscle pump), wound care (compressive dressing) สำหรับ venous ulcer. Sclerotherapy ใช้กับ telangiectasia/varicose เส้นเล็ก ไม่ใช่การรักษา chronic DVT (และ deep vein ที่อุดทำให้ superficial vein เป็นทางเลี่ยง). เฉลยไม่ตรงกัน (Med46 = E, LP = A); ตอบตามหลัก B."},{"id":"red2-87","src":"red2","n":87,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 40-year-old male suffered from a motorcycle crash 30 min PTA. His motor response of the Glasgow Coma Scale was according to the figure. Where is his motor scale in GCS?","opts":[["A","M1"],["B","M2"],["C","M3"],["D","M4"],["E","M5"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q87-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: แขนงอเข้าหาตัว ข้อมือ/นิ้วงอ ขาเหยียด = decorticate (abnormal flexion)","e":"GCS M3 = abnormal flexion (decorticate posturing — รอยโรคเหนือ red nucleus); M2 = extension (decerebrate); M4 = withdrawal (normal flexion ถอยหนี). ภาพในข้อนี้เป็นท่างอแขน → M3."},{"id":"red2-88","src":"red2","n":88,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old man with a head injury was referred from an outside hospital. The patient opened his eyes when he received pain stimuli. He was intubated and could not follow commands. When his supraorbital notch was pressed, he extended his hand to his chin.\nWhat is his GCS?","opts":[["A","E 2 V NT M 5"],["B","E 2 V T M 5"],["C","E 2 V NT M 4"],["D","E 2 V T M 4"],["E","E 3 V T M 5"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ใส่ท่อ → V = \"T\" (หรือ VT/NT ในบางระบบ); มือขึ้นมาถึงคางเมื่อกด supraorbital = localize","e":"E2 (ลืมตาเมื่อเจ็บ), V: intubated → บันทึก VT (ไม่ประเมินได้; บางตำราเขียน NT = non-testable), M5 (localize: มือเคลื่อนข้ามแนวกลางขึ้นมาเหนือกระดูกไหปลาร้าไปยังจุดกระตุ้น). เฉลยไฟล์ = A \"E2 VNT M5\" (ตามระบบที่ มอ. ใช้)."},{"id":"red2-89","src":"red2","n":89,"cat":"chest","stem":"Which one of the following findings in a chest X-ray is most related to thoracic aortic injury?","opts":[["A","Pleural apical cup"],["B","Mediastinum at aortic knob >6 cm"],["C","Mediastinum at carina >7 cm"],["D","3 rd Rt rib fracture"],["E","NG tube deviated to the left"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"CXR signs of blunt aortic injury: widened mediastinum > 8 cm, obscured aortic knob, apical cap, trachea/NG ไปขวา, depressed left main bronchus, 1st–2nd rib fracture","e":"ในตัวเลือก: pleural apical cap (left apical cap จากเลือดลามขึ้นยอดปอด) สัมพันธ์มากที่สุด. Mediastinum > 6 cm ที่ aortic knob ไม่ใช่เกณฑ์ (> 8 cm ที่ระดับ aortic knob); NG ควรเบี่ยงไป \"ขวา\" ไม่ใช่ซ้าย; 1st/2nd rib fracture ไม่ใช่ 3rd."},{"id":"red2-90","src":"red2","n":90,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. He complained of chest tightness and tenderness at the left side of the chest wall. PE: RR 24/min, SaO2 92%, decreased BS at the left lung. Trachea is in the midline.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Rib fracture"],["B","Hemothorax"],["C","Cardiac tamponade"],["D","Simple pneumothorax"],["E","Tension pneumothorax"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q90-1.jpg"],"t":"เสียงปอดซ้ายลด + trachea กลาง + vitals พอได้ + ภาพ: visceral pleural line/deep sulcus (มาร์คสีน้ำเงิน)","e":"Simple pneumothorax (ไม่มี mediastinal shift, ไม่มี shock) → ICD. Tension จะมี trachea shift + hypotension + JVD; hemothorax เห็นเป็น opacity. ภาพมีเส้นขอบปอดยุบ → simple pneumothorax."},{"id":"red2-91","src":"red2","n":91,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 40-year-old man sustained injuries in a car crash. He complained of chest tightness and retrosternal pain. PE: RR 26/min\nWhich one of the following is the proper investigation in this patient?","opts":[["A","Aortography"],["B","ECHO cardiogram"],["C","CT angiography of the chest"],["D","CT angiography of the neck"],["E","Film lateral CXR"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q91-1.jpg"],"t":"Blunt chest + retrosternal pain + supine AP CXR mediastinum กว้าง → สงสัย blunt aortic injury","e":"CT angiography ของ chest เป็นมาตรฐานยืนยัน blunt thoracic aortic injury (เร็ว แม่นยำ sensitivity ~100%). Aortography เป็น gold standard เก่าแต่ invasive; TEE ใช้ใน OR/ผู้ป่วยที่ย้ายไม่ได้."},{"id":"red2-92","src":"red2","n":92,"cat":"trauma","stem":"Which of the following is the test that has the highest sensitivity to detect hollow viscus injury in trauma patients?","opts":[["A","Acute abdomen series film"],["B","Focused assessment sonography in trauma"],["C","CT scan abdomen"],["D","Diagnostic peritoneal lavage"],["E","Physical examination"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Hollow viscus injury: FAST/CT พลาดได้ (เลือดน้อย) → DPL ไวที่สุดต่อการบาดเจ็บในช่องท้อง (รวม hollow viscus ผ่าน WBC/bile/food fiber)","e":"DPL sensitivity ~98% สำหรับ intraperitoneal injury (positive: blood ≥ 10 mL, RBC > 100,000, WBC > 500, bile/bacteria/food). ข้อเสีย: ไม่บอกอวัยวะ, ไม่ดู retroperitoneum, invasive. CT ดี solid organ แต่พลาด hollow viscus/mesentery ได้. LP ✗ ใต้ A ซึ่งขัดหลัก."},{"id":"red2-93","src":"red2","n":93,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. At the ED, BP 70/50 mmHg, E1V3M5 FAST: as shown in the picture\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","CT scan"],["B","Exploratory laparotomy"],["C","DPL"],["D","Pericardial window"],["E","Pelvic binding"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q93-1.jpg"],"t":"Unstable (BP 70/50) + FAST positive (ภาพเห็นน้ำใน Morison's pouch) → laparotomy","e":"Hypotension + FAST + = intra-abdominal hemorrhage → exploratory laparotomy (damage control). ไม่ส่ง CT ในคน unstable; DPL ไม่จำเป็น; pericardial window สำหรับ tamponade; pelvic binding เมื่อมี pelvic fracture."},{"id":"red2-94","src":"red2","n":94,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 45-year-old man was involved in a motorcycle crash. His BP at presentation was 70/50 mmHg and P 130/min. FAST: No free fluid. DPL was performed and found 12 cm of blood\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Closely observes in the ICU"],["B","Exploratory laparotomy"],["C","Pelvic binding"],["D","Install 1 liter of NSS via DPL catheter"],["E","CT scan"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"DPL: gross blood ≥ 10 mL = positive → unstable + DPL + → laparotomy","e":"FAST ลบแต่ DPL ได้เลือด 12 mL (> 10 mL) = intraperitoneal hemorrhage ใน hypotension → exploratory laparotomy. Pelvic binding ถ้ามี pelvic instability (โจทย์ไม่บอก); การใส่ NSS 1 L ทาง DPL catheter ทำเมื่อ gross aspirate < 10 mL เพื่อดู lavage fluid."},{"id":"red2-95","src":"red2","n":95,"cat":"trauma","stem":"An 18-year-old male was brought to the emergency department with a stab wound at the epigastrium. He complained of marked tenderness at the belly. His abdomen is guarding with rigidity.\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Local wound exploration"],["B","Suture the abdominal wound"],["C","Intravenous antibiotic"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy"],["E","CT scan abdomen"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Penetrating abdominal injury + peritonitis (guarding rigidity) → laparotomy","e":"ข้อบ่งชี้ผ่าตัดทันทีในแผลแทงท้อง: hemodynamic instability, peritonitis, evisceration, GI bleed. Local wound exploration ใช้กับคน stable ไม่มี peritonitis; CT ใช้ใน stable ที่ตรวจท้องไม่ชัด."},{"id":"red2-96","src":"red2","n":96,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 21-year-old male who had a gunshot wound at the abdomen. He complained of tenderness at the abdomen. The physical examination shows marked paleness and cold clammy skin. His blood pressure is 70/40 mmHg, and the GCS is E2V2M4.\nWhich of the following is the highest priority in managing this patient?","opts":[["A","Secured the airway"],["B","Protect the cervical spine"],["C","Oxygen supplement"],["D","Stop the bleeding"],["E","Preventing hypothermia"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"GSW abdomen + hemorrhagic shock class IV (BP 70/40, cold clammy) — แม้ GCS ต่ำ แต่ภาวะคุกคามชีวิตเร็วที่สุดคือเลือดออก","e":"แนวคิด ATLS 11th/MARCH: life-threatening hemorrhage ต้องหยุดเลือดก่อน (X-ABCDE — exsanguinating hemorrhage control). GCS 8 อาจเป็นจาก shock (cerebral hypoperfusion). ในตัวเลือก \"highest priority\" = stop the bleeding (เฉลย LP + MCQSx48). (หลัก ABCDE เดิมจะตอบ airway — ระวังถ้าโจทย์ถามคนละแบบ)"},{"id":"red2-97","src":"red2","n":97,"cat":"vascular","stem":"What is the most likely diagnosis of this patient?","opts":[["A","Venous ulcer"],["B","Ischemic ulcer"],["C","Diabetic foot ulcer"],["D","Radiative ulcer"],["E","Marjolin ulcer"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/mcq/s2-q97-1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: แผลกลม ขอบ callus หนา ที่ฝ่าเท้าใต้ metatarsal head (จุดรับน้ำหนัก) = neuropathic DM foot ulcer","e":"Diabetic (neuropathic) foot ulcer: ตำแหน่ง pressure point (ใต้ MT head/hallux), ขอบ callus, ไม่เจ็บ, punched-out. Venous ulcer อยู่ gaiter area (medial malleolus) ขอบไม่เรียบมี exudate; ischemic ulcer อยู่ปลายนิ้ว/ส้นเท้า ซีด เจ็บมาก; Marjolin = SCC บนแผลเป็นเรื้อรัง."},{"id":"red2-98","src":"red2","n":98,"cat":"infection","stem":"What is the best way to overcome the effects of a chronic glucocorticoid medication regimen in a chronic ulcer patient.","opts":[["A","Vitamin A supplement"],["B","Vitamin C supplement"],["C","Vitamin E supplement"],["D","Collagen supplement"],["E","Tropical steroid"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Steroid ยับยั้ง inflammatory phase ของ wound healing → vitamin A ช่วยย้อนฤทธิ์","e":"Vitamin A (25,000 IU/วัน) ช่วยฟื้นฟู inflammatory response และ collagen synthesis ที่ถูกกดโดย glucocorticoid. Vitamin C จำเป็นต่อ collagen hydroxylation (ขาดแล้วแผลหายช้า) แต่ไม่ได้แก้ผล steroid."},{"id":"red2-99","src":"red2","n":99,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"What is the most important factor related to intraoperative cardiac arrests in adults undergoing noncardiac surgery?","opts":[["A","Age"],["B","Body mass index"],["C","ASA classification"],["D","Emergency surgery"],["E","Intraoperative blood loss"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ปัจจัยทำนาย perioperative cardiac arrest ที่แข็งแรงที่สุด = ASA physical status","e":"Intraoperative cardiac arrest สัมพันธ์มากที่สุดกับ ASA class ที่สูง (III–V) รวมถึง emergency surgery; ASA class สะท้อนโรคพื้นฐานของผู้ป่วยโดยรวม. อายุ, BMI, blood loss เป็นปัจจัยแต่น้อยกว่า."},{"id":"red2-100","src":"red2","n":100,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 72-year-old man has received low anterior resection for his rectal carcinoma. On the fifth post- operative day, the patient experienced pelvic and perineal pain after a bowel movement with soft- yellowish stool. PE: BT 39.5°C. PR 120/min, BP 110/70 mmHg, RR 22/min and moderate tenderness at the lower abdomen\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Pain killer"],["B","IV antibiotic cover gram negative bacteria"],["C","Intermittent catheterization"],["D","Stitch off abdominal wound"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"POD5 หลัง LAR + ไข้สูง + tachycardia + peritonitis (lower abdominal tenderness) + pelvic/perineal pain = anastomotic leak","e":"Anastomotic leak (POD 5–7) ที่มี peritonitis/sepsis → resuscitate + ATB + exploratory laparotomy (washout + diverting stoma/Hartmann). Leak ที่ contained เป็น abscess → percutaneous drainage. Painkiller/ATB อย่างเดียวไม่พอเมื่อมี generalized sign."},{"id":"red2-101","src":"red2","n":101,"cat":"rehab","stem":"52-year-old female with Rt. CA breast underwent MRM operation and concurrent chemoradiation therapy. After that she developed Rt. adhesive capsulitis and limited her shoulder movement in all directions. Which is the most proper management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Hot pack at Rt. Shoulder"],["B","Use shoulder abduction splint"],["C","Osteotomy operation Rt. shoulder"],["D","Strengthening exercise Rt. Deltoid"],["E","Passive stretching exercise Rt. shoulder"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Adhesive capsulitis (frozen shoulder) จำกัดทุกทิศ → stretch capsule","e":"Frozen shoulder หลัง MRM/RT: passive stretching exercise เพื่อเพิ่ม ROM ร่วมกับ heat/analgesic ก่อนยืด. Splint/immobilize ทำให้แย่ลง; strengthening ทำเมื่อ ROM ดีขึ้น; osteotomy ไม่เกี่ยว."},{"id":"red2-102","src":"red2","n":102,"cat":"rehab","stem":"60-year-old male underwent explore laparotomy with Whipple operation. After bed rest for 4 days, the patient felt dizziness every time he was upright. The physical examination showed drop of systolic blood pressure from 120 to 100 mmHg and HR increase from 90 to 110 mmHg.\nWhich is the most proper management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Use air mattress"],["B","Repositioning every 2 hours"],["C","Stretching exercise of both legs"],["D","Continuous passive motion both legs"],["E","Progressive upright with Fowler bed"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"นอนนาน 4 วัน → orthostatic hypotension → ค่อยๆ ปรับท่าขึ้น","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 102: progressive upright (ยกหัวเตียง Fowler ทีละขั้น/tilt table) + ขยับขา + elastic stocking + hydration."},{"id":"red2-103","src":"red2","n":103,"cat":"rehab","stem":"32-year-old female underwent thoracic surgery. Which activity would be most appropriate to prevent muscle atrophy both legs post-surgery?","opts":[["A","Leg bandaging"],["B","Electrical stimulation"],["C","Pneumatic compression"],["D","Ankle pumping exercise"],["E","Passive range of motion exercise"]],"key":"B","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ป้องกัน disuse atrophy/DVT ในคนที่ยังขยับขาได้เอง (หลังผ่าตัดทรวงอก) → active exercise","e":"ผู้ป่วยหลัง thoracic surgery กล้ามเนื้อขาปกติ → active exercise เช่น ankle pumping/active ROM ช่วยป้องกันกล้ามเนื้อลีบและ DVT. Electrical stimulation ใช้เมื่อหดตัวเองไม่ได้ (power 0); pneumatic compression/bandage ป้องกัน DVT ไม่ใช่ atrophy. เฉลยไฟล์ (Med46) = B, LP = E (passive ROM — แต่ passive ไม่ป้องกัน atrophy) — ตามหลักตอบ D."},{"id":"red2-104","src":"red2","n":104,"cat":"rehab","stem":"70-year-old male with CA colon underwent abdominal surgery I week ago. He reported dizziness when he moved himself from lying to sitting position. What is the cause of dizziness?","opts":[["A","Tachycardia"],["B","Truncal ataxia"],["C","Postural hypotension"],["D","Respiratory impairment"],["E","Benign paroxysmal positional vertigo"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ลุกนั่งแล้วเวียนหัวหลังนอนนาน = orthostatic (postural) hypotension จาก deconditioning","e":"Bed rest → plasma volume ลด, baroreflex เสื่อม, venous pooling → postural hypotension. BPPV เกิดเมื่อหันศีรษะ มี nystagmus; truncal ataxia = cerebellar."},{"id":"red2-105","src":"red2","n":105,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 55-year-old man status post abdominal surgery for 5 days, which of the following is the most common sign of cardiac deconditioning from bedrest?","opts":[["A","Polyuria"],["B","Dizziness"],["C","Tachycardia"],["D","Nausea vomiting"],["E","Postural hypotension"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Cardiovascular deconditioning: สัญญาณแรก/พบบ่อยสุด = resting HR เพิ่ม (~0.5 bpm/วัน)","e":"Bedrest → HR ขณะพักเพิ่ม, stroke volume ลด, VO₂max ลด, orthostatic intolerance. ตำรา rehab ระบุ tachycardia เป็น sign ที่พบบ่อยของ cardiac deconditioning; postural hypotension เป็นผลของ vascular/baroreflex. เฉลยไฟล์ = E (postural hypotension) — ข้อนี้กำกวม จำทั้งสองอย่าง."},{"id":"red2-106","src":"red2","n":106,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A patient with chronic renal failure/condition is coming for appendectomy.\nWhich drug is the most appropriate?","opts":[["A","Fentanyl"],["B","Pethidine"],["C","Morphine"],["D","Diclofenac"],["E","Parecoxib"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"CKD → fentanyl (ไม่มี active metabolite)","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 106: morphine (M6G), pethidine (norpethidine), NSAIDs/coxib ไม่เหมาะในไตวาย."},{"id":"red2-107","src":"red2","n":107,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 20-year-old, ASA class I may has had Carpal tunnel syndrome. He got brachial plexus anesthesia.\nWhat is the most appropriate pain medication for him?","opts":[["A","Paracetamol 1 gm ☉ q6 hr."],["B","Morphine 3 mg IV q 2 hr."],["C","Fentanyl 50 mcg IV q 2 hr."],["D","Codeine 30 mg ☉ q 4 hr."],["E","Tramadol 100 mg ☉ q 6 hr."]],"key":"B","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Minor surgery + brachial plexus block → paracetamol พอ","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 107 และไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 108 (ไฮไลต์ paracetamol). Opioid IV ไม่จำเป็นในผ่าตัดเล็กที่ block คุมปวดได้."},{"id":"red2-108","src":"red2","n":108,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 80-year-old man who has diagnosed colon cancer. He has got the chemotherapy and thrombocytopenia. He got appendectomy. You should not give ____________.","opts":[["A","Diclofenac"],["B","Tramadol"],["C","Morphine"],["D","Fentanyl"],["E","Paracetamol"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Thrombocytopenia → ห้าม NSAIDs","e":"Diclofenac ยับยั้ง platelet function + GI bleed + AKI ในผู้สูงอายุ → ห้าม."},{"id":"red2-109","src":"red2","n":109,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 65-year-old man with well-controlled hypertension got laparoscopic cholecystectomy for 1.5 hr. He got morphine 12 mg and vecuron 12 mg. The volatile anesthetic agent was turned off for 15 min. After that muscle relaxant reversal was given but the patient still has apnea and unconsciousness. What is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hyperosmolar coma"],["B","Metabolism acidosis"],["C","Residual muscle relaxant"],["D","Opioid overdose"],["E","Cerebrovascular accident"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Morphine 12 mg + reversal ให้แล้วยัง apnea/unconscious → opioid overdose","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 109. Residual NMB ผู้ป่วยจะตื่นแต่ขยับไม่ได้; opioid → apnea + ซึม + pinpoint pupil → naloxone."},{"id":"red2-110","src":"red2","n":110,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"At PACU, a patient who got ovarian cystectomy gains consciousness after we woke her up, RR 10/min, BP 150/90 mmHg, HR 96/min, Spo, 95% room air, VAS = 3.\nWhich choice is correct?","opts":[["A","Sedation score = 3"],["B","Morphine 3 mg IV"],["C","Nifedipine 10 mg SL"],["D","Naloxone 0.4 mg IV"],["E","O2 cannula 3 LPM"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"รู้สึกตัว VAS 3 SpO₂ 95% RA → ให้ O₂ cannula","e":"ไม่ต้อง naloxone (รู้สึกตัว RR 10 ยังยอมรับได้), ไม่ต้อง morphine (ปวดน้อย), BP สูงเล็กน้อยไม่ต้อง nifedipine. Sedation score ที่ถูกของคนตื่นดีคือ 0 ไม่ใช่ 3."},{"id":"red2-111","src":"red2","n":111,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"What is the risk factor of postoperative nausea & vomiting (PONY)","opts":[["A","Male"],["B","Elderly"],["C","Regional anesthesia"],["D","Motion sickness history"],["E","Postoperative hypertension"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Apfel: female, non-smoker, PONV/motion sickness history, postop opioid","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 111."},{"id":"red2-112","src":"red2","n":112,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"What is the most common cause of restlessness after general anesthesia?","opts":[["A","Hypoxia"],["B","Pain"],["C","Hypotension"],["D","Hypothermia"],["E","Electrolyte imbalance"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Restlessness หลัง GA พบบ่อยสุด = pain (แต่ต้องตัด hypoxia ก่อน)","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 112."},{"id":"red2-113","src":"red2","n":113,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"At PACU, a 80-year-old woman has gained the consciousness after we woke her up, RR 10/min, stridor, pupil 2 mm both react to light, SpO. 96%, normal vital signs.\nWhat is the least likely cause to be happened?","opts":[["A","Secretion obstruction"],["B","Subglottic edema"],["C","Vocal cord edema"],["D","Opioid overdose"],["E","Residual neuromuscular blockade"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Stridor = upper airway obstruction; opioid ไม่ทำให้ stridor","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 113."},{"id":"red2-114","src":"red2","n":114,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 25-year-old woman who has general anesthesia c endotracheal tube & balance anesthetic technique, after the question finish, extubation was done uneventfully. Patient complained that she had the hoarseness after the operation for 3 days.\nWhat is the cause?","opts":[["A","Vocal cord edema"],["B","Vocal cord polyp"],["C","Arytenoids dislocation"],["D","Nerve injury"],["E","Laryngeal nerve injury both sides"]],"key":"C","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Hoarseness 3 วันหลัง intubate ธรรมดา → vocal cord edema","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 114 (เฉลยไฟล์ C arytenoid dislocation; LP = A). Arytenoid dislocation ต้องมีลักษณะพิเศษ (แหบทันที นาน breathy เจ็บกลืน) ดูไฟล์เหลือง ข้อ 116."},{"id":"red2-115","src":"red2","n":115,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 25-year-old woman who is diagnosed Hashimoto's thyroiditis got subtotal thyroidectomy. She has the seizure after the operation 6 hrs. What is the cause?","opts":[["A","Hypoxemia from vocal cord edema"],["B","Hypocalcemia"],["C","Hypercalcemia"],["D","Hyperventilation"],["E","Hyponatremia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ชักหลัง thyroidectomy → hypocalcemia","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 115."},{"id":"red2-116","src":"red2","n":116,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Pituitary adrenal axis will be suppressed after taking prednisolone (5 mg) oral three times a day for at LEAST......?","opts":[["A","1 day."],["B","3 days."],["C","1 week."],["D","1 month."],["E","3 months."]],"key":"E","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"HPA suppression: ≥ 20 mg prednisolone ≥ 3 สัปดาห์","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 116 (เฉลยไม่ตรงกัน ตอบตามหลัก 1 month)."},{"id":"red2-117","src":"red2","n":117,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which patient will probably have the MOST difficult endotracheal intubation?","opts":[["A","No upper and lower teeth"],["B","Full neck flexion and extension"],["C","Interincisor gap 5 cm"],["D","Mallampati classification 4"],["E","Thyromental distance 6 cm"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Mallampati IV = predictor ที่ดีที่สุดในตัวเลือก","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 117."},{"id":"red2-118","src":"red2","n":118,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 20-yr-old man is brought to the operating room for the emergency appendectomy. He has no underlying disease. His Hb = 10.2 g/dL. Hct = 30%. WBC = 11000/mm PMN = 72%, L = 28%, normal urine examination and CXR. What is his ASA classification?","opts":[["A","1E"],["B","2E"],["C","3E"],["D","4E"],["E","5E"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ไม่มีโรค + emergency → ASA 1E","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 118."},{"id":"red2-119","src":"red2","n":119,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which oral medication must be continued until the day of surgery?","opts":[["A","Atenolol"],["B","Enalapril"],["C","Aldactone"],["D","Furosemide"],["E","Losartan"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Beta-blocker ต้องกินต่อถึงวันผ่าตัด","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 119."},{"id":"red2-120","src":"red2","n":120,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which is CORRECT regarding to preoperative preparation in diabetic patients?","opts":[["A","Check blood sugar every hour before surgery."],["B","Ranitidine 150 mg @ 1 hr. prior to OR."],["C","Administer IV Lactated Ringer' solution."],["D","Glibenclamide 1 tab @ 1 hr. prior to OR."],["E","Control blood sugar between 200-300 mg%"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"DM → gastroparesis → aspiration prophylaxis","e":"ซ้ำชุด 1 ข้อ 120."},{"id":"m51-1","src":"m51","n":1,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 30-year-old man admitted due to acute arterial occlusion at RT leg for 12 hours. Immediate post-embolectomy, the patient had oliguria and dark urine.\nWhich one of the following is most likely condition in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hypouricemia"],["B","Hyperkalemia"],["C","Hypercalcemia"],["D","Hypernatremia"],["E","Metabolic alkalosis"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Reperfusion หลัง ALI 12 ชม. + oliguria + ปัสสาวะสีเข้ม (myoglobinuria) → rhabdomyolysis + K สูง","e":"กล้ามเนื้อที่ขาดเลือดตาย ปล่อย K⁺, myoglobin, H⁺ (acidosis), phosphate, uric acid เข้ากระแสเลือดหลังเปิดหลอดเลือด → hyperkalemia, metabolic acidosis, hyperphosphatemia, hypocalcemia, hyperuricemia, AKI. ตัวเลือกอื่นกลับทิศทั้งหมด."},{"id":"m51-2","src":"m51","n":2,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 61-year-old male presents with hematochezia for 8 hours. He has no underlying disease and no taking any medication. At ED, Vital signs: BT 36.8oC BP 85/55 mmHg, PR 120 beats/min, RR 24/min.\nPE:\nAbdomen: unremarkable\nDRE and anoscopy: large amount of fresh blood and no anorectal lesion or hemorrhoid.\nWhat is the most proper management in fluid resuscitation?","opts":[["A","Gelofusine 1 L IV in 1 h"],["B","Normal saline 2 L IV rate 120 ml/h"],["C","Normal saline 1 L IV in 15-30 min and cross match"],["D","Acetate Ringer's solution 1 L IV in 15-30 min and cross match"],["E","Acetate Ringer's solution 1 L IV through triple lumen catheter"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"LGIB + shock (BP 85/55 HR 120) → isotonic crystalloid 1 L เร็ว + เตรียมเลือด","e":"ATLS: balanced/isotonic crystalloid 1 L ใน 15–30 นาที ผ่าน large-bore peripheral IV และ cross-match/request blood เร็ว. Acetate/Lactated Ringer (balanced) ดีกว่า NSS ปริมาณมาก (hyperchloremic acidosis) → D ดีกว่า C. Rate 120 mL/h ช้าเกินไป; triple-lumen CVC ยาวและแคบ → flow ต่ำกว่า peripheral large bore; colloid ไม่ดีกว่า."},{"id":"m51-3","src":"m51","n":3,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 35-year-old male was stabbed at the right arm 2 years ago. His arm was swollen for 4 months.\nPE: Right arm; Superficial vein dilatation, thrill at the scar of right arm. Distal pulses: radial 2+ ulnar 2+\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Pseudoaneurysm"],["B","Arteriovenous fistula"],["C","Venous malformation"],["D","Cavernous hemangioma"],["E","Peripheral arterial disease"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"บาดแผลแทงเก่า + vein โป่ง + thrill ที่แผลเป็น (+ distal pulse ปกติ) = AVF","e":"Traumatic AV fistula: continuous thrill/bruit, superficial venous dilatation, บวม, อาจมี distal ischemia (steal) หรือ high-output HF. Pseudoaneurysm = pulsatile mass + systolic bruit. ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 2."},{"id":"m51-4","src":"m51","n":4,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with gastric outlet obstruction with anuria\nV/S: BP 80/60mmHg, PR 120 /min, RR 24/min, BT 36.0 °C.\nLab results: BUN 40 mg/dL, Cr 1.3 mg/dL, Na+ 140 mEq/L, K+ 2.8 mEq/L, Cl- 82 mEq/L, HCO3- 30 mEq/L\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate IV fluid?","opts":[["A","0.9% NaCl"],["B","Gelofusine"],["C","Lactated Ringer 's solution"],["D","5%D/N/2 + KCL 40 mEq/1000 mL"],["E","10% DNSS + KCL 40 mEq/1000 mL"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"GOO + shock (BP 80/60) + anuria + hypochloremic hypokalemic alkalosis → ฟื้น volume ด้วย NSS ก่อน แล้วค่อยเติม K เมื่อปัสสาวะออก","e":"ลำดับ: แก้ hypovolemia/shock ด้วย 0.9% NaCl (ให้ Cl⁻ แก้ alkalosis ด้วย) → เมื่อปัสสาวะออกค่อยเติม KCl (ห้ามให้ K ในคน anuria). D (5%D/N/2 + KCl) เป็น maintenance/replacement หลัง resuscitate (ไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 43 ไม่มี shock/anuria จึงตอบ D). LRS มี lactate → alkalosis แย่ลง."},{"id":"m51-5","src":"m51","n":5,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained injuries in a car crash.\nPE: 80/50 mmHg, P 140/min;\nAbdomen: mild distension FAST: Free fluid at hepatorenal region\nWhich one of the following is the proper fluid resuscitation?","opts":[["A","5% D/NSS"],["B","Gelofusion"],["C","5% albumin"],["D","PRC transfusion"],["E","Cryoprecipitate"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Class III–IV hemorrhagic shock (BP 80/50 HR 140) + FAST + → ให้เลือด ไม่ใช่ crystalloid/colloid","e":"ATLS 11th: early blood product (PRC, balanced 1:1:1, MTP) ในผู้ป่วยที่ shock จากเลือดออก + ผ่าตัดหยุดเลือด. 5% D/NSS ไม่ใช่ resuscitation fluid; colloid/albumin ไม่ดีกว่า; cryoprecipitate ให้ตาม fibrinogen."},{"id":"m51-6","src":"m51","n":6,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 38-year-old man has a stab wound at 2.5 cm medial to nipple line on left chest 20 minutes. He complaints chest pain and dyspnea. On physical examination: restless, BP72/53 mmHg, HR 127/min, RR 28/min, oxygen saturation 94% at room air, trachea in midline, neck vein engorged, mild pale, cooled skin perfusion.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Lung laceration"],["B","Cardiac contusion"],["C","Cardiac tamponade"],["D","Massive hemothorax"],["E","Tension pneumothorax"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง = Cardiac contusion (B) — ยึดตามเฉลย","e":"เฉลยอาจารย์ (ไฟล์เหลือง) ตอบ B: cardiac contusion → shock + JVD จาก pump failure/RV dysfunction, trachea กลาง (ไม่ใช่ tension PTX), ไม่ใช่ massive hemothorax (neck vein จะแฟบ). ⚠ หมายเหตุ: ตามหลัก ATLS แผลถูกแทงใน cardiac box + Beck's triad (hypotension, JVD, muffled heart sound) มักคิดถึง cardiac tamponade (C) — contusion มักเกิดจาก blunt trauma. ถ้าเจอโจทย์นี้ซ้ำในสอบกองนี้ ให้ตอบตามเฉลย B; ถ้าโจทย์ให้ muffled heart sound/pulsus paradoxus หรือ FAST เห็น pericardial fluid → ตอบ tamponade"},{"id":"m51-7","src":"m51","n":7,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 20-year-old man developed chest discomfort after a motorcycle crash. The chest X-ray was done (shown below).\nWhich one of the following is the diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hemothorax"],["B","Lung contusion"],["C","Pneumothorax"],["D","Mediastinal emphysema"],["E","Subcutaneous emphysema"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image1.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ CXR: ปอดขวาไม่มี lung marking ที่ขอบนอก เห็น visceral pleural line","e":"Traumatic pneumothorax (simple). ถ้ามี trachea shift + shock = tension → needle decompression ทันที; simple → ICD (หรือ observe ถ้าเล็กและไม่ต้องใช้ ventilator)."},{"id":"m51-8","src":"m51","n":8,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 60-year-old man has had end stage renal disease for 2 years. He did not take hemodialysis for 5 days due to arterio-venous fistula thrombosis.\nWhich one of the following is most likely to happen in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hyperkalemia"],["B","Hypercalcemia"],["C","Metabolic alkalosis"],["D","Hemoconcentration"],["E","Hypophosphatemia"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ESRD ขาด dialysis 5 วัน → K⁺, H⁺, phosphate, volume คั่ง","e":"ไม่ได้ฟอกไต → hyperkalemia (อันตรายที่สุด), metabolic acidosis, hyperphosphatemia, hypocalcemia, volume overload (hemodilution ไม่ใช่ hemoconcentration). ต้อง EKG + K stat และ emergency dialysis (temporary catheter)."},{"id":"m51-9","src":"m51","n":9,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 70-year-old male was diagnosed as ARDS from COPD exacerbation. The patient's clinical condition had deteriorated into respiratory failure and septic shock with a high dose of an inotropic agent. Two days later the patient developed lower gastrointestinal hemorrhage. The plain X-ray of the abdomen shows thumb printing sign.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Ulcerative colitis"],["B","Pseudomembranous colitis"],["C","Inflammatory bowel disease"],["D","Mesenteric venous thrombosis"],["E","Nonocclusive mesenteric ischemia"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Septic shock + high-dose inotrope/vasopressor → splanchnic vasoconstriction → NOMI; thumbprinting = submucosal edema/hemorrhage","e":"Non-occlusive mesenteric ischemia: low-flow state (shock, HF, vasopressor, dialysis) ทำให้ mesenteric vasospasm ไม่มี thrombus/embolus. Thumbprinting บ่ง ischemic bowel. รักษา: แก้สาเหตุ ลด vasopressor, intra-arterial papaverine, ผ่าตัดถ้ามี necrosis. Pseudomembranous colitis ต้องมีประวัติ ATB + diarrhea."},{"id":"m51-10","src":"m51","n":10,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 72-year-old woman with underlying ischemic cardiomyopathy and arrhythmia presented with acute abdominal pain for 6 h.\nPE: BP 100/60 mmHg, PR 110 beats/min, RR 28/min, and BT 38.0 °C.\nAbdomen: tenderness at mid and lower abdomen.\nCBC shows WBC count 15,000 cells per cubic millimeter. ABG: metabolic acidosis. Abdominal\nCT scan: dilated small intestine and bowel wall thickening. Absent enhancement of ileal segment. Pneumatosis intestinalis was found.\nWhich one of the following is the appropriate management?","opts":[["A","IV antibiotics"],["B","IV antibiotics and adequate hydration"],["C","Exploratory laparotomy with lysis adhesion"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy with small bowel resection"],["E","Conservative management for small bowel obstruction"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"AF + acute abdominal pain + acidosis + CT: ileal segment ไม่ enhance + pneumatosis = transmural necrosis","e":"Acute mesenteric ischemia (embolic จาก AF/cardiomyopathy) ที่มี bowel infarction (absent enhancement, pneumatosis intestinalis, peritonitis, acidosis) → resuscitate + heparin + exploratory laparotomy with resection ลำไส้ที่ตาย (± embolectomy, second-look). ATB/hydration อย่างเดียวไม่พอ; ไม่ใช่ adhesive SBO."},{"id":"m51-11","src":"m51","n":11,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old male has abdominal pain at the right upper quadrant for 1 day, 9/10 intensity, radiating to the back, with no exacerbating or alleviating factors. He has had fever, anorexia and vomiting. PE tachycardia, dry lips.\nAbdomen: distended with mild tender at epigastrium, no guarding, no palpable masses, and hypoactive bowel sounds.\nWhat would be the next step in managing this patient?","opts":[["A","Upper GI study"],["B","Abdominal x-ray"],["C","Upper GI endoscopy"],["D","Abdominal ultrasound"],["E","Liver function tests and serum amylase"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"ปวด RUQ/epigastrium ร้าวหลัง + อาเจียน + ท้องอืด hypoactive BS → นึกถึง pancreatitis/biliary → blood test ก่อน","e":"Next step: LFT + serum amylase/lipase (แยก pancreatitis vs biliary) พร้อม U/S. ตัวเลือก E ให้ข้อมูลเร็วที่สุดและตรงจุด. Upper GI study/endoscopy ไม่ใช่ขั้นแรกในปวดท้องเฉียบพลันแบบนี้."},{"id":"m51-12","src":"m51","n":12,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30- year old man was referred form an outside hospital due to high grade liver injury. He underwent exploratory laparotomy to stop bleeding6 hr. ago. After the operation the drain output was 1000 ml. So the continuous bleeding was suspected. At the emergency department of your hospital.\nV/S: BP 80/50 mmHg, PR 130/min.\nWhich of the following should be the first prescription at the emergency department?","opts":[["A","FFP"],["B","PRC"],["C","Vitamin K"],["D","Tranexamic acid"],["E","Calcium Gluconate"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"เลือดออกต่อเนื่องหลังผ่าตัดตับ + shock → แทนที่สิ่งที่เสีย = เลือด","e":"Hemorrhagic shock (BP 80/50 HR 130, drain 1 L) → first prescription = PRC (ส่วนหนึ่งของ MTP 1:1:1) ขณะเตรียม re-exploration/angioembolization. FFP/cryo/TXA/calcium ให้ร่วมตาม protocol และ lab แต่สิ่งแรกที่ช่วยชีวิตคือเลือด. Vitamin K ออกฤทธิ์ช้า."},{"id":"m51-13","src":"m51","n":13,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old male underwent epidermal inclusion cyst excision 3 days ago. His underlying disease is diabetes. Today he developed redness, warmth, and pain at the incision site\nWhich organism is the most likely cause of this infection?","opts":[["A","Mixed organism"],["B","Staphylococcus aureus"],["C","Staphylococcus epidermidis"],["D","Pseudomonas pseudomallei"],["E","Beta hemolytic streptococcus"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"SSI แผล clean (ตัด EIC) วันที่ 3 = skin flora","e":"Staphylococcus aureus เป็นเชื้อหลักของ SSI clean wound (แม้ในคน DM). S. epidermidis มักสัมพันธ์กับ implant/foreign body; Burkholderia pseudomallei (melioidosis) เป็นตัวหลอกของคนไทย DM แต่ไม่ใช่ SSI ทั่วไป."},{"id":"m51-14","src":"m51","n":14,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old women had fever and abdominal pain for 3 days.\nV/S: BT 39°C, BP 86/60 mmHg, PR 100/min, RR 24 /min;\nPhysical exam: icteric sclera and tenderness at the RUQ, Murphy sign negative, no hepatosplenomegaly; WBC 22,000, PMN 80, L Bands 10%\nLFTs: TB 5.02 mg%, DB 4.18 mg%, SGOT 120 U/L, SGPT 140 U/L, ALP 300 U/L\nWhich of following the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Leptospirosis"],["B","Liver abscess"],["C","Acute hepatitis"],["D","Acute cholangitis"],["E","Acute cholecystitis"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Charcot triad + hypotension = Reynolds' pentad (ขาด confusion) → severe cholangitis","e":"ไข้ 39 + RUQ tenderness + icteric + BP 86/60 + WBC 22,000 bands 10% + DB เด่น ALP สูง → acute cholangitis (Tokyo grade III: มี organ dysfunction—shock). ตัวหลอก leptospirosis (ไข้ เหลือง ปวดกล้ามเนื้อ แต่ไม่มี RUQ tenderness เด่น, ALP ไม่สูงมาก)."},{"id":"m51-15","src":"m51","n":15,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 40-year-old male stepped on a nail while working 1 hour prior to visiting the ER. Four years ago he had a full course of Tetanus toxoid administration.\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Open the wound, apply wet dressing, and discharge"],["B","Suture the wound, give an oral antibiotic, and discharge"],["C","Irrigate the wound with betadine, give an oral antibiotic, and discharge"],["D","Dress the wound with betadine, give an oral antibiotic and a single dose of tetanus toxoid"],["E","Open the wound, apply wet dressing, give an oral antibiotic and a single dose of tetanus toxoid"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"TT ครบชุด 4 ปี (< 5 ปี) + puncture wound สะอาด","e":"ไม่ต้อง TT booster (ให้เมื่อแผลสกปรกและ > 5 ปี), ไม่ต้อง ATB, ห้ามเย็บ → เปิดแผล ล้าง wet dressing แล้วให้กลับบ้าน (ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 15)."},{"id":"m51-16","src":"m51","n":16,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 25-year-old man was cut by a kitchen knife at the right hand 2 hours ago. Wound: 1.5 cm long with 0.5 cm in depth (deep to subcutaneous tissue)\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Wet dressing"],["B","Suture wound"],["C","Occlusive dressing"],["D","Semi-occlusive dressing"],["E","Sterile surgical tape application"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"แผลมีดสะอาด ลึกถึง subcutaneous 2 ชม. → primary closure","e":"Clean laceration ภายใน 6–8 ชม. (มือ/หน้าได้นานกว่า) ไม่ปนเปื้อนมาก → irrigate + primary suture. Sterile tape ใช้แผลตื้นที่ไม่ตึง; wet dressing ใช้กับแผลสกปรก/ติดเชื้อที่ไม่เย็บ."},{"id":"m51-17","src":"m51","n":17,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 30-year-old female presents with dysphagia for 1 month.\nPE: anemia, atrophic oral mucosa, and spoon-shaped brittle finger nails.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Achalasia"],["B","CA esophagus"],["C","Boerhaave's syndrome"],["D","Mallory-Weiss syndrome"],["E","Plummer-Vinson syndrome"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Dysphagia + iron deficiency signs (anemia, atrophic mucosa, koilonychia) = Plummer–Vinson","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 18: Plummer–Vinson syndrome (post-cricoid web + IDA). รักษา iron + dilatation; เสี่ยง SCC."},{"id":"m51-18","src":"m51","n":18,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old woman presented with dysphagia for 3 months.\nBarium swallow: Thin shelf-like mucosal projection into the esophageal lumen.\nWhich of the following is the next management?","opts":[["A","Esophagoscopy"],["B","Esophagostomy"],["C","Esophagectomy"],["D","24-h-pH monitoring"],["E","Esophageal manometry"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Barium: thin shelf-like projection = esophageal web → ส่องกล้องยืนยัน/ตัด CA + dilate ได้ในคราวเดียว","e":"Web/ring ต้องทำ esophagoscopy (EGD) เพื่อยืนยัน แยก malignancy และรักษาด้วย dilatation ในคราวเดียว; ตรวจ iron deficiency ร่วม. pH monitoring/manometry ไม่เกี่ยว; esophagectomy เกินเหตุ."},{"id":"m51-19","src":"m51","n":19,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with non-bilious vomiting for 3 days.\nPE: BT 37 C, PR 80/min, RR 20/min, BP 90/60 mmHg.\nHEENT: mild pale. No lymphadenopathy\nAbdomen: Mild distension, normoactive bowel sound, soft, moderate tenderness at epigastrium with mass Acute abdomen film showed as picture below.\nWhat is the next management in this case?","opts":[["A","CT abdomen"],["B","Barium swallow"],["C","NG decompression"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy"],["E","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image2.jpg"],"t":"Non-bilious vomiting + epigastric mass + ฟิล์มกระเพาะโป่งมาก = gastric outlet obstruction","e":"GOO: NG decompression (ลดความดัน, ป้องกัน aspiration, วัด output) + IV fluid แก้ hypochloremic hypokalemic alkalosis เป็นขั้นแรก → แล้ว EGD + biopsy หาสาเหตุ (PUD vs gastric CA) และ CT staging. ห้ามส่องกล้องตอนกระเพาะเต็มอาหาร."},{"id":"m51-20","src":"m51","n":20,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old man presented with abdominal discomfort and heartburn for 6 months. He had weight loss of 3 kg in 6 months\nPE: mildly pale, no jaundice\nAbdomen: no mass\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Gastroscopy"],["B","Barium UGI study"],["C","CT whole abdomen"],["D","24-hr pH monitoring"],["E","Esophageal manometry"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Dyspepsia/heartburn อายุ ≥ 60 + weight loss + ซีด = alarm features → EGD","e":"Alarm features (อายุ > 55–60, weight loss, anemia, dysphagia, GI bleed, vomiting, ก้อน) → upper endoscopy + biopsy (หา gastric/esophageal CA). Barium/CT ไม่ได้ชิ้นเนื้อ; pH monitoring ใช้ GERD ที่ EGD ปกติ."},{"id":"m51-21","src":"m51","n":21,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 45-year-old patient with underlying systemic lupus erythematosus has had a slowly growing perianal mass for 2 years. He had a history of homosexual intercourse. The mass is occasionally itchy. After scratching, a small amount of blood and a small piece of gray tissue detached from the mass.\nPE: An anal exam as in the picture\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Electrocoagulation"],["B","Hemorrhoidectomy"],["C","Rubber band ligation"],["D","Lateral internal sphicterotomy"],["E","Antibiotic cover gram negative aerobic and anaerobic bacteria"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/m51/image3.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: cauliflower/warty lesion รอบทวาร ในคน MSM + immunosuppressed (SLE) = condyloma acuminata (HPV)","e":"Condyloma acuminata: เล็ก → topical (podophyllin/imiquimod); ใหญ่/ไม่ตอบสนอง/ภูมิคุ้มกันต่ำ → surgical excision/electrocoagulation (fulguration) และส่งชิ้นเนื้อ (ตัด Buschke–Löwenstein/SCC). ตรวจ HIV/STD ร่วม. ไม่ใช่ hemorrhoid/fissure."},{"id":"m51-22","src":"m51","n":22,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"The following picture shows an anal lesion in a 40-year-old patient with a history of anal pain and bleeding during defecation for 3 months. Anal exam as in the picture\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Fistula in ano"],["B","Acute anal fissure"],["C","Chronic anal fissure"],["D","Internal hemorrhoid"],["E","External hemorrhoid"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image4.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ: แผลแตก longitudinal ที่ posterior midline + skin tag + ประวัติ 3 เดือน = chronic","e":"Chronic anal fissure (> 6–8 สัปดาห์) features: sentinel pile, hypertrophied papilla, ขอบแผลนูนแข็ง เห็น internal sphincter fibers. รักษา: topical nitrate/CCB, botox, lateral internal sphincterotomy (gold standard)."},{"id":"m51-23","src":"m51","n":23,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 45-year-old woman presented with a palpable mass at right breast for 1 month.\nPE:\nBreast: a 3-cm-well defined smooth surface mass at the right breast Aspiration showed greenish fluid 5ml and the mass decreased in size to 1.5 cm after aspiration.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Excision"],["B","Tamoxifen"],["C","Mammography"],["D","Observe Excision"],["E","Send fluid for cytology"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Cyst aspiration: น้ำไม่ใช่เลือด + ก้อนหายหมด → observe; \"ก้อนเหลือ\" หรือ bloody → work-up ต่อ","e":"หลัง aspirate แล้วยังมี residual mass 1.5 cm → ต้องประเมินเพิ่ม: อายุ 45 → diagnostic mammography (+ U/S) แล้ว core biopsy/excision ของก้อนที่เหลือ. เฉลยไฮไลต์ C (mammography) ซึ่งเป็น next step ที่เหมาะ; cytology ของน้ำสีเขียวไม่จำเป็น (ส่งเฉพาะ bloody)."},{"id":"m51-24","src":"m51","n":24,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 25-year-old woman presented with high-grade fever for 4 days. During breastfeeding, she developed fever and breast pain.\nPE: BT 39C PR 110/min\nBreast: Swollen and tender left breast with fluctuation.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Ceftriaxone iv"],["B","Ciprofloxacin iv"],["C","Norfloxacin oral"],["D","Dicloxacillin oral"],["E","Amoxicillin + Clavulonic acid iv"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Lactational breast abscess + systemic (ไข้ 39 HR 110) → IV ATB คลุม S. aureus + drainage","e":"Breast abscess ระหว่างให้นม: ระบาย (needle aspiration/I&D) + ATB ที่คลุม S. aureus. ในตัวเลือก ผู้ป่วยมี systemic toxicity → IV amoxicillin-clavulanate (หรือ cloxacillin IV) เหมาะสม; dicloxacillin oral ใช้ใน mastitis ไม่รุนแรง; quinolone ไม่ใช่ first-line และเลี่ยงในแม่ให้นม."},{"id":"m51-25","src":"m51","n":25,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with Lt. breast mass with soreness for 2 weeks.\nPhysical examination showed a well-defined mass 4.0 cm at 3 o clock of the Lt. breast, cystic consistency, movable, mild tender. Breast ultrasound showed as picture.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Excision"],["B","Reassure"],["C","Aspiration"],["D","Oral antibiotic"],["E","Incisional and drainage"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image5.jpg"],"t":"U/S: anechoic, thin wall, posterior enhancement = simple cyst ที่ \"มีอาการ\" (เจ็บ) → aspiration","e":"Simple cyst ไม่มีอาการ → reassure; มีอาการเจ็บ/ก้อนใหญ่ → needle aspiration เพื่อบรรเทา (ไม่ต้องส่ง cytology ถ้าน้ำไม่ใช่เลือดและก้อนหายหมด). Excision ไม่จำเป็น; ไม่ใช่ abscess จึงไม่ต้อง I&D/ATB."},{"id":"m51-26","src":"m51","n":26,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 45-year-old female presented with right upper abdominal pain for a couple of weeks.\nPhysical examination showed normal. Transabdominal ultrasound revealed hyperechoic foci 5 mm without posterior acoustic shadow which did not move when the patient changed position.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Gallstones"],["B","Gallbladder polyp"],["C","Gallbladder cancer"],["D","Adenomyomatosis of gallbladder"],["E","Xanthogranulomatous cholecystitis"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Echogenic focus ใน GB \"ไม่มี acoustic shadow\" + \"ไม่ขยับตามท่า\" = polyp (นิ่วมี shadow และเคลื่อนที่)","e":"GB polyp: immobile, non-shadowing. นิ่ว: mobile + posterior acoustic shadow. Adenomyomatosis: comet-tail artifact + wall thickening. Polyp 5 mm → U/S follow-up."},{"id":"m51-27","src":"m51","n":27,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 40-year-old female screening ultrasound abdomen found round anechoic lesion, well-marginated with a thin wall and no internal vascularity on color Doppler (as figure)\nWhat's the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Liver abscess"],["B","Bile duct dilatation"],["C","Biliary cystadenoma"],["D","Simple hepatic cyst"],["E","Hepatocellular carcinoma"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":["img/m51/image6.jpg"],"t":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง = Liver abscess (A) — ยึดตามเฉลย","e":"เฉลยอาจารย์ (ไฟล์เหลือง) ตอบ A: liver abscess. ทบทวน U/S: abscess ระยะแรก/ที่ liquefy แล้วอาจเห็นเป็น hypo/anechoic lesion ขอบชัด ไม่มี flow ภายใน. ⚠ หมายเหตุ: ลักษณะ \"round anechoic, well-marginated, thin wall, no internal vascularity\" ในคนไม่มีอาการ ตามตำราตรงกับ simple hepatic cyst (D) — abscess มักผนังหนาไม่เรียบ มี debris/septation และมีไข้. ในสอบกองนี้ให้ตอบตามเฉลย A"},{"id":"m51-28","src":"m51","n":28,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old male presented with progressive dysphagia for 2 months. He had history of heavy smoking for 30 years. Esophagoscopy showed ulcerofungative mass at 25 cm from incisors\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis for this patient?","opts":[["A","Candida esophagitis"],["B","Sarcoma of the esophagus"],["C","Adenocarcinoma of the esophagus"],["D","Squamous cell carcinoma of the esophagus"],["E","Gastrointestinal stromal tumor (GIST) of the esophagus"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"สูบบุหรี่หนัก + ก้อนที่ 25 cm จาก incisors (mid-thoracic) = SCC","e":"SCC พบที่ upper/mid esophagus สัมพันธ์บุหรี่ แอลกอฮอล์ (พบมากสุดในไทย/เอเชีย); adenocarcinoma อยู่ distal/GEJ สัมพันธ์ GERD/Barrett/obesity. (Incisors → UES ~15 cm, carina ~25 cm, GEJ ~40 cm)"},{"id":"m51-29","src":"m51","n":29,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 76-year-old man presented with dysphagia for 6 months and cough for 1 month.\nBarium swallow: tracheoesophageal fistula\nEGD: Tumor at mid-thoracic esophagus\nPathological report: squamous cell carcinoma\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Palliative care"],["B","Chemotherapy"],["C","Esophagectomy"],["D","Radiation therapy"],["E","Esophageal stent placement"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"TE fistula = unresectable (T4b) → palliation ด้วย covered stent ปิด fistula","e":"Malignant tracheoesophageal fistula: self-expandable covered metal stent (esophageal ± airway) ปิดรูรั่ว ลด aspiration และให้กินได้ (ทางเลือก palliation ที่ดีที่สุด). Esophagectomy ทำไม่ได้; RT อาจทำให้ fistula แย่ลง; chemo อย่างเดียวไม่ปิดรูรั่ว."},{"id":"m51-30","src":"m51","n":30,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with chronic dyspepsia for 6 months. Esophagogastroduodenoscopy (EGD) showed ulcerofungative mass at the antrum.\nPathological report from tissue biopsy: adenocarcinoma of the stomach. PET scan showed liver metastasis.\nWhat is the appropriate treatment for this patient?","opts":[["A","Radiotherapy"],["B","Chemotherapy"],["C","Gastrectomy with hepatectomy"],["D","Gastrectomy with chemotherapy"],["E","Gastrectomy with hepatectomy and chemotherapy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Gastric CA + liver metastasis = stage IV → systemic chemotherapy","e":"Metastatic gastric cancer → palliative systemic chemotherapy (± trastuzumab ถ้า HER2+, immunotherapy). Gastrectomy เฉพาะ palliative (เลือดออก/อุด) ไม่ใช่ curative; RT ใช้บรรเทาเลือดออก/ปวด."},{"id":"m51-31","src":"m51","n":31,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 68-year-old man is diagnosed with adenocarcinoma of the gastric cardia\nPhysical examination\nHEENT: A firm, non-tender, fixed 2-cm lymph node is palpated in the left supraclavicular fossa.\nAbdomen: Normal\nDRE: A hard, nodular mass is palpated in the rectovesical pouch.\nWhat is the most appropriate interpretation of these clinical findings?","opts":[["A","Tuberculosis Lymph node"],["B","Localized nodal metastasis"],["C","Distance metastasis disease"],["D","Reactive lymphadenopathies"],["E","Synchronous second primary colorectal cancer"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Virchow's node (left supraclavicular) + Blumer's shelf (rectovesical pouch) = metastasis ไกล","e":"Signs ของ gastric CA ระยะแพร่กระจาย: Virchow's node, Blumer's shelf (drop metastasis ใน pouch of Douglas/rectovesical), Sister Mary Joseph nodule, Krukenberg tumor (ovary), Irish node (left axilla) → stage IV."},{"id":"m51-32","src":"m51","n":32,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A healthy 80-year-old male without any history of abdominal symptoms presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. He had anorexia and nausea but no vomiting, fever or obstipation. The physical examination revealed soft, not tender, moderate abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds and no rectal mass. Acute abdominal series revealed generalized small bowel and large bowel dilation down to the sigmoid colon with no gas in the rectum.\nWhat is the provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Diverticulitis"],["B","Rectal cancer"],["C","Paralytic ileus"],["D","Ulcerative colitis"],["E","Sigmoid volvulus"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"LBO (SB + colon โป่งถึง sigmoid ไม่มีลม rectum) ในผู้สูงอายุไม่มีอาการนำ — สาเหตุที่พบบ่อยที่สุดของ LBO = colorectal cancer","e":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง ไฮไลต์ rectal cancer: แม้ PR ไม่เจอก้อน (ก้อน rectosigmoid อาจอยู่สูงเกินนิ้ว) สาเหตุ LBO อันดับ 1 คือ CRC. ต่างจากไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 60 (เฉลย LP = sigmoid volvulus). ถ้าโจทย์ให้ภาพ coffee bean → volvulus. ⚠ โจทย์นี้กำกวม — ขั้นต่อไปจริงคือ CT abdomen."},{"id":"m51-33","src":"m51","n":33,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 40-year-old male has colonic carcinoma together with more than 100 adenomatous polyps throughout the entire length of his colon and rectum. His mother and sister also have these same problems.\nWhich of the following is advice regarding colorectal cancer risk for his 14-year-old daughter?","opts":[["A","Do nothing."],["B","Colonoscopy"],["C","Barium enema"],["D","Flexible sigmoidoscopy"],["E","Stool occult blood test"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"> 100 adenomatous polyps + ครอบครัว = FAP (APC, autosomal dominant) → screen ลูกตั้งแต่ 10–12 ปี","e":"FAP: เริ่ม flexible sigmoidoscopy (หรือ colonoscopy) ทุก 1–2 ปีตั้งแต่อายุ 10–12 ปี หรือ genetic testing APC; ถ้ามี polyp → prophylactic (procto)colectomy ช่วงวัยรุ่นตอนปลาย. ลูก 14 ปีจึงต้องตรวจ — sigmoidoscopy เพียงพอเพราะ polyp กระจายทั่ว (รวม rectosigmoid)."},{"id":"m51-34","src":"m51","n":34,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 50 year old female presented with right breast mass for 1 month.\nPE: A 2-cm irregular right breast mass was found that was movable with an ill-defined border. No axillary node enlargement was found. Mammography: 2-cm spiculated mass at the upper outer quadrant of Rt. breast FNA: positive for malignancy\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Radiation"],["B","Excisional biopsy"],["C","Total mastectomy"],["D","Neoadjuvant chemotherapy"],["E","Breast conserving surgery (BCS)"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"T1–2 (2 cm) N0 ไม่มี contraindication → breast conserving surgery (+ SLNB + RT)","e":"Early breast cancer ขนาดเล็กเทียบเต้านม → BCS (lumpectomy + margin negative) + sentinel lymph node biopsy + whole breast RT ได้ผลเทียบเท่า mastectomy. FNA positive แต่ปัจจุบันควรมี core biopsy เพื่อ receptor status ก่อน. Neoadjuvant chemo ใช้ใน LABC/TNBC/HER2+ บางกลุ่ม."},{"id":"m51-35","src":"m51","n":35,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 40-year-old female presents with a mass at the left breast for 1 month. She has no pain and the mass has grown rapidly\nPE: Well-circumscribed mass 5 cm in diameter at lower outer quadrant of left breast, firm consistency, and movable.\nU/S breast: Well defined lobulated mass with internal cystic component.\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Phyllodes tumor"],["B","Fibrocystic change"],["C","Giant fibroadenoma"],["D","Intraductal papilloma"],["E","Carcinoma of left breast"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ก้อน 5 cm โตเร็ว อายุ 40 ขอบชัด lobulated + cystic space ภายใน = phyllodes","e":"Phyllodes tumor: อายุ 40–50, โตเร็ว, ใหญ่, U/S lobulated มี cystic cleft. รักษา wide local excision margin ≥ 1 cm (ไม่ต้อง axillary dissection). Giant fibroadenoma พบในวัยรุ่น; fibroadenoma ปกติ < 3 cm อายุน้อย."},{"id":"m51-36","src":"m51","n":36,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 65-year-old male presented with mild abdominal distension, progressive jaundice and significant weight loss for 2 months. He had no history of abdominal surgery.\nGA: look cachexia\nHEENT: mark icteric sclera, no parotid gland enlargement\nAbdomen: palpable gallbladder, mild abdominal distension\nLFT: DB 15.56 mg%, TB 19.91 mg%, AST 165 U/L, ALT 60 U/L, ALP 480 U/L, TP 6.9 g/dL, Alb 3.1 g/dL\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate initial investigation?","opts":[["A","Acute abdomen series"],["B","Ultrasonography of upper abdomen"],["C","Percutaneous Transhepatic Cholangiography"],["D","Magnetic Resonance Cholangio pancreatography"],["E","Endoscopic Retrograde Cholangio pancreatography"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Obstructive jaundice → initial imaging = U/S (ดู IHD/CBD dilatation, ระดับการอุด)","e":"Jaundice + palpable GB + cachexia (สงสัย malignant distal obstruction) → U/S upper abdomen ก่อน แล้ว CT pancreas protocol/MRCP; ERCP/PTC เป็น invasive ใช้เพื่อระบาย/biopsy."},{"id":"m51-37","src":"m51","n":37,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 50-year-old male with a history of chronic hepatitis B infection presents after an incidental finding of a 3-cm-liver mass on ultrasound during his annual health check-up. Liver function is preserved, and there is no evidence of portal hypertension\nPhysical examination\nGA: well-appearing\nHEENT: not pale, anicteric sclera, no parotid gland enlargement\nAbdomen: no distension, no palpable mass, shifting dullness negative\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate further management?","opts":[["A","Biopsy"],["B","CT liver"],["C","Oral antibiotics"],["D","Schedule for surgery"],["E","Surveillance with ultrasonography"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"HBV carrier + liver mass > 1 cm → multiphasic CT/MRI (LI-RADS) ก่อน ไม่ต้อง biopsy","e":"ก้อน > 1 cm ในคนเสี่ยง HCC → dynamic (multiphase) CT หรือ MRI: arterial hyperenhancement + washout → วินิจฉัย HCC ได้โดยไม่ต้อง biopsy (biopsy เมื่อ imaging ไม่ชัด). จากนั้น staging (BCLC) แล้วพิจารณา resection."},{"id":"m51-38","src":"m51","n":38,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 35-year-old woman has a BMI of 31 kg/m² with progressive weight gain. She reports short sleep, frequent late-night eating, and low physical activity\nWhat is the most appropriate next step?","opts":[["A","Start anti-obesity medication"],["B","Prescribe a calorie-restricted diet"],["C","Screen for endocrine causes of obesity"],["D","Refer for metabolic and bariatric surgery"],["E","Assess weight-gain drivers and obesity-related complications"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Obesity management เริ่มจาก \"ประเมิน\" ก่อนรักษา (drivers + complications)","e":"แนวทางใหม่ (ระบบ clinical obesity): ประเมินสาเหตุที่ทำให้น้ำหนักขึ้น (นอนน้อย กินดึก ไม่ออกกำลัง ยา โรค) และภาวะแทรกซ้อน/ความเสี่ยง (DM, HT, OSA, NAFLD) แล้วจึงวางแผน lifestyle → pharmacotherapy → bariatric surgery ตามความรุนแรง. Endocrine screen ทำเมื่อมีข้อสงสัย ไม่ใช่ทุกราย."},{"id":"m51-39","src":"m51","n":39,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 42-year-old Thai woman has a BMI of 28 kg/m² and a waist circumference of 92 cm. She has no known underlying disease.\nWhich is the best interpretation of these findings?","opts":[["A","She has obesity with increased central adiposity"],["B","She is overweight based on her BMI classification"],["C","Her health risk is low because she has no known comorbidity"],["D","Her BMI alone accurately quantifies the degree of excess body fat"],["E","Her current findings are sufficient to classify her as having clinical obesity"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"เกณฑ์คนเอเชีย: BMI ≥ 25 = obesity; waist ≥ 80 cm (หญิง) / ≥ 90 cm (ชาย) = central obesity","e":"BMI 28 ในคนไทย = obese (Asia-Pacific: 23–24.9 overweight, ≥ 25 obese) + WC 92 cm → central adiposity. BMI ไม่ได้วัด body fat โดยตรง; \"clinical obesity\" ต้องมีความผิดปกติของอวัยวะ/การทำงานจากไขมันเกิน ซึ่งโจทย์ไม่มี."},{"id":"m51-40","src":"m51","n":40,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 39-year-old policeman with transcranial gunshot wounds was admitted to a surgical intensive care unit. Over the first 3 days, the patient was hemodynamically stable but producing 600 mL/h of urine. The blood and urine tests revealed as shown in the chart. Diabetes insipidus was suspected and the urinary loss of free water needs to be determined.\nWhich of the following is the estimated free water clearance rate (mL/min) in this patient?","opts":[["A","5"],["B","6"],["C","7"],["D","8"],["E","9"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Free water clearance = V × (1 − Uosm/Posm)","e":"600 mL/h = 10 mL/min → 10 × (1 − 180/360) = 5 mL/min (ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 45)."},{"id":"m51-41","src":"m51","n":41,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 68-year-old Thai male come to surgery clinic with a fatigue problem. He is a heavy smoker and has progressive dysphagia grade 4 for 3 months. He has weight lost 20 Kg. in 2 months.\nPhysical exam: BW 45 Kg.\nV/S: BT 36.4 C, BP 110/60 mmHg, PR 90 bpm, RR 20/min DTX 100 mg% BUN 20 mg%, Cr 1.2 mg% Electrolyte: Na 125 mmol/L, K 3.5 mmol/L, Cl 100 mmol/L, T-CO2 28 mmol/L (normal range of Na= 135-145 mmol/L)\nWhich choice is the proper fluid in sodium correction?","opts":[["A","3% NaCl IV drip rate 53 mL/hr"],["B","3% NaCl IV drip rate 28 mL/hr"],["C","0.9% NaCl IV drip rate 73 mL/hr"],["D","0.9% NaCl IV drip rate 53 mL/hr"],["E","0.45% NaCl IV drip rate 53 mL/hr"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Na 125 แบบ chronic + กินไม่ได้ น้ำหนักลด (hypovolemic) ไม่มีอาการรุนแรง → isotonic saline ไม่ใช่ 3%","e":"3% NaCl สงวนไว้สำหรับ severe symptomatic (ชัก ซึม). คำนวณแบบที่ข้อสอบใช้: TBW = 0.6 × 45 = 27 L; Na deficit = 27 × (135 − 125) = 270 mEq → NSS (154 mEq/L) ≈ 1.75 L/24 ชม. ≈ 73 mL/h. ต้องเจาะ Na ซ้ำทุก 4–6 ชม. และไม่ให้ Na ขึ้นเกิน 8–10 mEq/L ใน 24 ชม. (ผู้ป่วยขาดอาหาร = เสี่ยง ODS)."},{"id":"m51-42","src":"m51","n":42,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 39-year old lady with head trauma. Over the early days of admission, she remained unconscious and started to produce a large amount of urine on the 6th day of hospitalization. Blood chemistries were done and revealed as shown. A decision was made to correct the serum sodium to 140 mEq/L\nWhich of the following is the shortest time required to safely correct hypernatremia?","opts":[["A","6 hrs"],["B","22 hrs"],["C","30 hrs"],["D","34 hrs"],["E","38 hrs"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"แก้ hypernatremia ไม่เกิน ~0.5 mEq/L/h (≤ 10–12 mEq/L/วัน) → เวลา = ΔNa ÷ 0.5","e":"Central DI หลัง head trauma → hypernatremia. เวลาที่สั้นที่สุดที่ปลอดภัย = (Na เริ่มต้น − 140) / 0.5 ชม.; ตัวเลือก 34 ชม. ตรงกับ Na เริ่มต้น ≈ 157 mEq/L (ตารางผลเลือดในไฟล์ไม่ได้แนบมา). แก้เร็วเกิน → cerebral edema/ชัก."},{"id":"m51-43","src":"m51","n":43,"cat":"fluid","stem":"A 25-year-old man presented with head injury and pelvic fracture. He received 0.9%Nacl solution IV 100 mL/hour. Three days after the injury he had oliguria (urine 20 mL/hour).\nLab results: Na 120 mEq/L (3 days ago Na 140 mEq/L) Urine osmolarity 514 mOsm/L\nWhich of the following is the most proper treatment?","opts":[["A","DDAVP"],["B","Diuretic"],["C","3% NaCl"],["D","50% Albumin"],["E","Fluid restriction"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Head injury + Na ตกเร็ว (140→120 ใน 3 วัน) + Uosm สูง (514, ไม่ dilute) + oliguria → SIADH เฉียบพลัน","e":"Acute severe hyponatremia ในสมองบาดเจ็บ → 3% NaCl (เพิ่ม 4–6 mEq/L เพื่อลด brain edema). Fluid restriction เป็นการรักษา SIADH ไม่รุนแรง/เรื้อรัง; DDAVP ทำให้แย่ลง; diuretic อย่างเดียวไม่พอ. (เทียบไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 45)"},{"id":"m51-44","src":"m51","n":44,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 45-year-old man presented with acute, massive upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage. An urgent upper endoscopy reveals a 1-cm ulcer in the first part of the duodenum with active, brisk bleeding. Despite multiple endoscopic therapeutic attempts, the bleeding fails to stop, and the patient remains hemodynamically unstable. Interventional radiology for transcatheter arterial embolization is unavailable.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?","opts":[["A","Wedge excision of the ulcer"],["B","Subtotal gastrectomy with D2 lymph node dissection"],["C","Duodenotomy/Gastrotomy with cauterization and over-sewing of the bleeding site"],["D","Highly selective vagotomy combined with cauterization and over-sewing of the bleeding ulcer"],["E","Truncal vagotomy, pyloroplasty, combined with cauterization and over-sewing of the bleeding ulcer"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Bleeding duodenal ulcer ที่ endoscopy + IR ล้มเหลว → ผ่าตัดเพื่อ \"หยุดเลือด\" (oversew GDA)","e":"Duodenotomy (ผ่าน pylorus) + oversewing ulcer base (3-point ligation ของ gastroduodenal artery) + PPI/H. pylori eradication หลังผ่าตัด. การผ่าตัดลดกรด (vagotomy) ไม่จำเป็นในยุค PPI; gastrectomy + D2 ใช้กับมะเร็ง."},{"id":"m51-45","src":"m51","n":45,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 58 year-old man presents with dysphagia for solids for three months. He complains of weight loss. There is no other relevant medical history apart from heartburn for the previous five years. He has endoscopy which shows an esophageal stricture.\nWhich one of the followings is the most likely etiology?","opts":[["A","Achalasia"],["B","Esophagitis"],["C","Gastric ulcer"],["D","Esophageal web"],["E","Esophageal spasm"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Heartburn นาน 5 ปี → dysphagia ของแข็ง + stricture = peptic stricture","e":"Chronic GERD → reflux esophagitis → fibrosis → peptic stricture (distal) → dysphagia ต่อของแข็ง. ต้อง biopsy ตัด adenocarcinoma (Barrett) โดยเฉพาะเมื่อน้ำหนักลด. รักษา dilatation + PPI. Achalasia ไม่ใช่ stricture จาก GERD; web อยู่ส่วนต้น."},{"id":"m51-46","src":"m51","n":46,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 25-year-old woman presented with corrosive digestion 30 minutes before arrival. She refused to give a history. PE BT 38C, BP 120/80 mmHg, HR 110/bpm, RR 30/bpm,\nHEENT: erythematous lesion in the oral cavity. Crepitation around the neck.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Retained NG tube"],["B","Perform contrast study"],["C","Endotracheal intubation"],["D","Acid-base neutralization"],["E","Intravenous corticosteroid"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Corrosive + RR 30 + crepitation รอบคอ (สงสัย airway/esophageal injury) → secure airway","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 19: ABC ก่อน → endotracheal intubation (ใส่ภายใต้การมองเห็น). ห้าม neutralization, ห้ามใส่ NG แบบ blind, ห้าม induce vomiting; steroid ไม่มีบทบาทชัด; contrast study ทำเมื่อสงสัย perforation หลัง airway ปลอดภัย."},{"id":"m51-47","src":"m51","n":47,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 65-year-old-man presents with abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting for 12 hours. He passes stool 2 to 3 times/week.\nV/S: BT 38.3°c BP 125/80 mmHg, PR 115/min RR 12/min.\nAbdomen: mild abdominal distension with mark tender at Rt. lower quadrant.\nCBC: WBC 22,000/mm3 PMN 75% Lymphocyte 10% Band 3%\nU/S lower abdomen: normal appendix size 5 mm in diameter\nWhat is the most appropriate management","opts":[["A","IV antibiotic"],["B","CT whole abdomen"],["C","Emergency colonoscopy"],["D","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"],["E","Supportive treatment and pain control"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ผู้สูงอายุ + ไข้ + WBC 22,000 + RLQ tender แต่ U/S appendix ปกติ → ยังไม่วินิจฉัย → CT","e":"ผู้สูงอายุมี differential กว้าง (appendicitis ที่ U/S มองไม่เห็น, cecal diverticulitis, perforated cecal cancer) → CT abdomen with contrast. Emergency laparotomy โดยไม่มีวินิจฉัยใน stable patient ไม่เหมาะ; colonoscopy ห้ามในภาวะเฉียบพลันที่สงสัย perforation."},{"id":"m51-48","src":"m51","n":48,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 34-year-old female patient suffered from abdominal pain a week ago; no other gastrointestinal problems were noted. On\nPE: she had a fever, a mass of 6 cm was palpable in the right lower quadrant, appeared hard, tender and fixed.\nCBC: leucocytosis Ultrasonography: mixed-echoic mass at right lower quadrant with omental wall off, without abscess\nWhat is the appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","IV antibiotic therapy"],["B","Percutaneous drainage"],["C","Emergency open appendectomy"],["D","Exploratory laparotomy tumor removal"],["E","Emergency laparoscopic appendectomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Appendiceal mass/phlegmon (walled-off by omentum ไม่มี abscess) → conservative","e":"Appendiceal phlegmon → IV ATB + bowel rest (Ochsner–Sherren regimen) แล้วพิจารณา interval appendectomy/colonoscopy ในผู้สูงอายุ. Abscess ≥ 3 cm → percutaneous drainage; immediate appendectomy ใน phlegmon มีภาวะแทรกซ้อนสูง (อาจต้อง ileocecectomy)."},{"id":"m51-49","src":"m51","n":49,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 30-year-old male presented with right inguinal mass for 2 weeks. The mass was easily seen in the upright position but disappeared in the supine position. Some dull pain was associated with the mass. He reported no underlying diseases.\nPE: Reducible mass at the inguinal region that extends to the scrotal area without any signs of inflammation.\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","Elective surgery"],["B","Watchful waiting"],["C","Emergency surgery"],["D","Manual reduction with Fowler position"],["E","Medication is the most appropriate treatment"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Symptomatic reducible inguinal hernia ในคนหนุ่มสุขภาพดี → elective repair","e":"Inguinal hernia ที่มีอาการ (dull pain) → elective hernioplasty (tension-free mesh). Watchful waiting ใช้กับชายที่ไม่มีอาการ/อาการน้อยมาก; emergency surgery สำหรับ strangulation; ไม่มียารักษา."},{"id":"m51-50","src":"m51","n":50,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 40-year-old female presented with a history of a reducible mass at right groin for 1 month. Today she developed a non-reducible mass with pain at the mass.\nPE: A mass below the inguinal canal and mildly tender.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Femoral hernia"],["B","Richter's hernia"],["C","Pantaloon hernia"],["D","Direct inguinal hernia"],["E","Indirect inguinal hernia"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"หญิง + ก้อนใต้ inguinal ligament + ดันไม่เข้า = femoral hernia","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 55: femoral hernia เสี่ยง strangulation สูง → ผ่าตัด (urgent)."},{"id":"m51-51","src":"m51","n":51,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 70-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months ago presented with pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea and bilious vomiting without fever or obstipation.\nPhysical examination revealed soft, not tender, moderate abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds. Acute abdominal series revealed generalized small bowel dilation with some gas in a collapsed colon and no gas in rectum.\nWhat is the most provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Paralytic ileus"],["B","Partial small bowel obstruction"],["C","Partial large bowel obstruction"],["D","Complete large bowel obstruction"],["E","Closed loop small bowel obstruction"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"หลังผ่าตัด + SB dilatation ทั่ว + ยังมีลมใน colon (partial) + ท้องนุ่มไม่เจ็บ ไม่ไข้","e":"Partial adhesive SBO → NG + IV fluid + observe. Complete = ไม่มีลมใน colon; closed loop/strangulated = มีไข้ tachycardia tenderness; paralytic ileus = SB + colon โป่ง BS ลด."},{"id":"m51-52","src":"m51","n":52,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 23-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months ago presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea, and bilious vomiting without fever or obstipation.\nPE: BT 38.3 °C, PR 110/min\nAbdomen: Localized marked tenderness and guarding at RLQ, mild abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds. Acute abdominal series: 3 cm of one loop of the small bowel has dilation at the RLQ with some gas in a collapsed colon and no gas in the rectum.\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Observe"],["B","IV Antibiotics"],["C","CT abdomen"],["D","Rectal tube decompression"],["E","Emergency exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"SBO + ไข้ 38.3 + HR 110 + localized marked tenderness/guarding = sign of strangulation","e":"เมื่อมีไข้ tachycardia และ peritoneal sign ใน SBO → สงสัย strangulation (หรือ abscess) → emergency laparotomy (ไฮไลต์ E). CT ช่วยได้ใน stable แต่ไม่ควรเลื่อนการผ่าตัดเมื่อ clinical ชัด. (ไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 61 ตัวเลือกต่างกัน)"},{"id":"m51-53","src":"m51","n":53,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 23-year-old female with a history of appendectomy 3 months ago presented with abdominal pain for 2 days. She had anorexia, nausea, and bilious vomiting with fever and obstipation. The physical examination revealed localized marked tenderness and guarding at the suprapubic area and mild abdominal distension with hyperactive bowel sounds. An acute abdominal series revealed a 3 cm dilatation of one loop of the small bowel at the mid-part of the abdomen with no gas in the colon or rectum.\nWhat is the most likely provisional diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Paralytic ileus"],["B","Partial large bowel obstruction"],["C","Partial small bowel obstruction"],["D","Complete large bowel obstruction"],["E","Strangulated small bowel obstruction"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"SBO + ไข้ + obstipation + localized peritonitis + complete (ไม่มีลมใน colon/rectum)","e":"Strangulated small bowel obstruction (ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 62) → resuscitate + emergency laparotomy."},{"id":"m51-54","src":"m51","n":54,"cat":"hernia","stem":"A 35-year-old man with irreducible Lt. indirect inguinal hernia presented at the emergency room with colicky abdominal pain and vomiting for 8 hours.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Immediate surgery"],["B","Immediate manual reduction and observe"],["C","Immediate surgery after reduction has failed"],["D","Immediate manual reduction and elective surgery later"],["E","Conservative treatment (IV fluid, NG tube) and elective surgery later"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Irreducible hernia + gut obstruction (colicky pain + vomiting 8 ชม.) = obstructed/strangulated → ห้ามดันกลับ","e":"Incarcerated hernia ที่มี bowel obstruction หรือ sign of strangulation → immediate surgery (เปิดดู viability). การ reduce อาจดันลำไส้ที่ตายเข้าท้อง. Manual reduction (taxis) ทำได้เฉพาะ incarcerated < 6 ชม. ที่ไม่มี obstruction/strangulation."},{"id":"m51-55","src":"m51","n":55,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 22-year-old virgin female presented with severe anal pain during and after defecation for 4 months. She has always had constipation and passes hard stool. Sometimes, streaks of fresh blood were detected at the toilet paper.\nWhich was the suspected finding from anal physical examination?","opts":[["A","Cauliflower mass"],["B","Bluish-purplish mass"],["C","Foul-smell discharge"],["D","Fibroepithelial polyp"],["E","Large ulcerative lesion"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Chronic anal fissure (ปวดระหว่าง/หลังถ่าย เลือดสด ท้องผูก 4 เดือน) → sentinel pile","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 65: sentinel pile = fibroepithelial polyp/skin tag ที่ขอบล่างของ chronic fissure."},{"id":"m51-56","src":"m51","n":56,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 50-year-old female presented with an opening at 3 o'clock at the perianal area for 1 year which was 4 cm from the anal verge. Digital rectal examination revealed dimple at 3 o'clock.\nWhich one of the following is the curative sphincter saving operation in this patient?","opts":[["A","Fistulotomy"],["B","Fistulectomy"],["C","Cutting seton"],["D","Drainage seton"],["E","Ligation of intersphincteric fistula tract"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Transsphincteric fistula (ห่าง 4 cm, ผ่าน sphincter) ต้องการรักษาที่ \"รักษากล้ามเนื้อหูรูด\"","e":"LIFT (ligation of intersphincteric fistula tract) เป็น sphincter-sparing curative procedure สำหรับ transsphincteric fistula. Fistulotomy/fistulectomy ตัดกล้ามเนื้อหูรูด (เสี่ยง incontinence ถ้าเป็น high); cutting seton ตัดทีละน้อย; drainage seton ไม่ curative. อื่นๆ: advancement flap, fistula plug."},{"id":"m51-57","src":"m51","n":57,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 47-year-old male presented with occasional pain, swelling and discharge from an opening at his left buttock for 2 years.\nPE: He has normal anal sphincter tone. An opening at 4 o clock at 5 cm from the anal verge was found.\nWhat is the most definitive treatment?","opts":[["A","Fistulotomy"],["B","Laxative agent"],["C","Oral antibiotics"],["D","Incision and drainage"],["E","Lateral internal sphincterotomy"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Fistula-in-ano เรื้อรัง sphincter tone ปกติ → definitive = fistulotomy (ถ้าเป็น low/simple)","e":"Simple (intersphincteric/low transsphincteric) fistula ในคนหูรูดปกติ → fistulotomy (lay open) cure rate > 90%. Complex/high fistula หรือ anterior ในผู้หญิง → seton/LIFT/flap. ATB/laxative ไม่รักษา; I&D สำหรับ abscess; LIS สำหรับ fissure."},{"id":"m51-58","src":"m51","n":58,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"Patients complain of anal pain, physical exam showed an area of erythema and induration in the skin around the perianal area with point of maximal tenderness without mass.\nWhat's the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Oral antibiotic"],["B","Needle aspiration"],["C","Hemorrhoidectomy"],["D","Incision and drainage"],["E","Internal sphincterotomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Perianal erythema + induration + point of maximal tenderness (แม้คลำก้อนไม่ได้ชัด) = abscess","e":"Perianal/ischiorectal abscess ระยะแรกอาจไม่มี fluctuation → I&D ไม่ต้องรอ (ATB อย่างเดียวไม่พอ). ให้ ATB เสริมใน DM, immunocompromised, cellulitis กว้าง."},{"id":"m51-59","src":"m51","n":59,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 45-year-old male has bleeding per anus of 500 mL after hemorrhoidectomy 20 hours ago. He also has dizziness.\nPE: BP 90/60 mmHg, PR 120/min\nWhich one of the following is/are the most appropriate treatment(s)?","opts":[["A","Loperamide"],["B","Reassurance"],["C","OR to stop the bleeding"],["D","NPO , IV fluid , serial Hct"],["E","Vaseline gauze packing, observe rectal bleeding"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Primary/reactionary hemorrhage < 24 ชม. หลัง hemorrhoidectomy + shock → OR","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 47: เลือดออก 500 mL + BP ต่ำ → กลับห้องผ่าตัด ligate pedicle (ระหว่างนั้น resuscitate). Packing ใช้กับเลือดออกน้อยหรือชั่วคราว."},{"id":"m51-60","src":"m51","n":60,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 80-year-old male with bed ridden status from old cerebrovascular accident. He had had hard consistency of stool for 3 months with some fresh blood separate from stool and masses protude from his anus which need manual reduction. Digital rectal examination and anoscopy revealed lumps in the anal canal without bleeding. The colonoscopy at last 2 years had shown no abnormality.\nWhich of the followings is the appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","Sclerosing therapy"],["B","Rubber band ligation"],["C","Repeat colonoscopy"],["D","Lifestyle and diet modification"],["E","Discontinue antiplatelet long life"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Internal hemorrhoid ที่ต้องดันกลับ = grade III ในผู้สูงอายุติดเตียง (เสี่ยงผ่าตัด) → office procedure","e":"Grade III: rubber band ligation (โดยเฉพาะผู้ป่วยเสี่ยงสูงต่อการดมยา) หรือ hemorrhoidectomy; ร่วมกับแก้ท้องผูก. Colonoscopy 2 ปีก่อนปกติ ไม่ต้องทำซ้ำ; sclerotherapy เหมาะ grade I–II."},{"id":"m51-61","src":"m51","n":61,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 65-year-old man presented with acute cholecystitis and was admitted for iv antibiotics for 1 week. During admission he developed diarrhea after having his meal but he had good well-being. Stool exam: Numerous WBCs and numerous RBCs. The colonoscopy showed multiple ulcers and pseudomembrane formation at the sigmoid.\nWhich one of the following is the proper treatment in this patient?","opts":[["A","NPO and TPN"],["B","Vancomycin iv"],["C","Ciprofloxacin oral"],["D","Ceftriaxone 2 gm iv"],["E","Metronidazole oral"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Diarrhea หลังได้ ATB + pseudomembrane ที่ colonoscopy = C. difficile colitis (non-severe)","e":"C. difficile infection: หยุด ATB ที่ไม่จำเป็น + oral vancomycin หรือ fidaxomicin (ปัจจุบัน first-line); oral metronidazole ใช้ได้ใน non-severe เมื่อไม่มีตัวเลือกอื่น (เฉลยข้อนี้). IV vancomycin ไม่เข้า lumen ลำไส้ (ไม่ได้ผล); quinolone/ceftriaxone เป็นตัวกระตุ้นโรค."},{"id":"m51-62","src":"m51","n":62,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 28-year-old male had right lower abdominal pain and fever for 4 days. He took pain killers and antibiotics from private clinic. He has no underlying disease. Today, his abdominal pain is worse. At ED his blood pressure is 120/70 mmHg, pulse rate is 90 beats/min, respiratory rate is 24/min, and body temperature is 38.8 °C. Abdominal examination reveals marked tenderness at RLQ without guarding, and ill-defined mass at RLQ. Digital rectal examination is normal.\nCBC shows leukocytosis\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Enterocolitis"],["B","Colonic cancer"],["C","Ileal tuberculosis"],["D","Acute appendicitis"],["E","Appendicealphlegmon"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"RLQ pain 4 วัน + ไข้ + ill-defined mass (ไม่มี abscess ชัด) หลังกิน ATB = appendiceal phlegmon","e":"Appendiceal phlegmon = inflammatory mass (appendix + omentum + ลำไส้) ไม่มี pus collection → IV ATB conservative. ถ้ามี collection ชัด = abscess. TB ileum เรื้อรัง; acute appendicitis ปกติไม่คลำก้อน."},{"id":"m51-63","src":"m51","n":63,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 75-year-old male presented with severe generalized abdominal pain for 1 day. Two days ago he had pain at peri-umbilical area that shifted to the right lower quadrant area during the next 6 hours. He also had a low grade fever and nausea without vomiting. Today the pain was progressing. He had no history of abdominal surgery. The physical examination revealed generalized hypertympanic on percussion, severe tenderness and involuntary guarding at his abdomen\nWhat is the most appropriate initial investigation for diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Plain KUB"],["B","Abdominal MRI"],["C","Abdominal ultrasound"],["D","Acute abdomen series"],["E","Diagnostic peritoneal lavage"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Generalized peritonitis + hypertympanic (สงสัย free air) → plain film ชุด acute abdomen series ก่อน","e":"Acute abdomen series (upright CXR + supine + upright/decubitus abdomen) หา pneumoperitoneum, obstruction pattern ได้เร็วและถูก. Plain KUB ท่าเดียว (supine) มักพลาด free air; MRI ไม่ใช่ใน emergency; DPL ใช้ใน trauma."},{"id":"m51-64","src":"m51","n":64,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 60-year-old women had fever and abdominal pain for 3 days.\nV/S: BT 39°C,BP 86/60 mmHg, PR 100/min, RR 24 /min;\nPhysical exam: icteric sclera and tenderness at the RUQ, Murphy sign negative, no hepatosplenomegaly; WBC 22,000, PMN 80, L Bands 10%\nLFTs: TB 5.02 mg%, DB 4.18 mg%, AST 120 U/L, ALT 140 U/L, ALP 300 U/L\nU/S: CBD dilatation, multiple gallstones in gallbladder\nWhich of following the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","MRCP"],["B","CT abdomen"],["C","Cholecystostomy"],["D","Urgent ERCP drainage"],["E","Emergency cholecystectomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Severe cholangitis (shock) + CBD dilated + gallstones → urgent biliary drainage","e":"Tokyo 2018 grade III cholangitis → resuscitation + IV ATB + urgent (≤ 24 ชม.) ERCP drainage (sphincterotomy/stent); PTBD ถ้า ERCP ทำไม่ได้. Cholecystectomy ทำภายหลัง (interval) เมื่อหาย; MRCP ไม่จำเป็นเมื่อข้อบ่งชี้ ERCP ชัด."},{"id":"m51-65","src":"m51","n":65,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 54-year-old female presented with acute cholecystitis. Intravenous antibiotics were administered. On the second day after treatment, her abdominal pain got worse.\nPE: BP130/70 mmHg, PR105 beats/min, RR 24/min, BT 39.0 °C.\nAbdomen: marked tenderness at RUQ with Murphy's sign positive.\nCBC: WBC count rose from 14,000 to 21,000 cells per cubic millimeter. Abdominal ultrasonography: markedly distended gallbladder with multiple gallstones without common bile duct dilatation.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Cholecystectomy"],["B","Open cholecystostomy"],["C","Cholecystotomy with stone removal"],["D","Change antibiotics to high-level broad-spectrum antibiotics"],["E","Endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography with stone removal and stent insertion"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Acute cholecystitis ที่แย่ลงแม้ได้ ATB (ไข้ WBC เพิ่ม GB โตมาก) ในคนที่ผ่าตัดได้ → cholecystectomy","e":"Failure ของ medical treatment (ไม่ดีขึ้น 24–48 ชม.) ในผู้ป่วย fit → urgent laparoscopic cholecystectomy (Tokyo grade II). Cholecystostomy (percutaneous) ใช้ในคนเสี่ยงผ่าตัดสูง/grade III ที่มี organ failure. ERCP ไม่ช่วยเพราะ CBD ปกติ."},{"id":"m51-66","src":"m51","n":66,"cat":"hpb","stem":"What is the most appropriate initial investigation in the case of clinical suspicion of acute cholecystitis?","opts":[["A","Scintigraphy"],["B","Laparoscopy"],["C","CT scan of abdomen"],["D","MRI of hepatobiliary region"],["E","Ultrasonography of hepatobiliary region"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Acute cholecystitis → U/S first-line","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 75: U/S hepatobiliary เป็นการตรวจแรก; HIDA เมื่อ U/S ไม่ชัด."},{"id":"m51-67","src":"m51","n":67,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 50-year-old male who has a history of acute pancreatitis 6 weeks ago. Abdominal ultrasound has been performed to identify gallstone but well-defined, unilocated pancreatic cyst size 3 cm has been found. He has no abdominal complaint\nGA: look well\nV/S: BT 36.8°c, BP 115/65 mmHg, PR 65/min, RR 12/min\nAbdomen: no distension, soft, not tender, no palpable mass\nWhat is the most proper next step management?","opts":[["A","IV antibiotics"],["B","Distal pancreatectomy"],["C","Percutaneous drainage"],["D","Reassure and follow-up"],["E","Endoscopic cystogastrostomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Pancreatic fluid collection หลัง pancreatitis 6 สัปดาห์ + ไม่มีอาการ → ไม่ต้องทำอะไร","e":"Pseudocyst ไม่มีอาการ (แม้ > 6 cm หรือนานกว่า 6 สัปดาห์) ส่วนใหญ่ติดตามได้ ยุบเองบ่อย. Drainage (endoscopic cystogastrostomy เป็นหลัก) ทำเมื่อมีอาการ (ปวด อิ่มเร็ว GOO), ติดเชื้อ, โตขึ้น, เลือดออก. ⚠ ซีสต์ที่ \"well-defined unilocular\" ต้องแยก cystic neoplasm ถ้าไม่มีประวัติ pancreatitis."},{"id":"m51-68","src":"m51","n":68,"cat":"hpb","stem":"A 45-year-old man presents with acute onset of a severe constant epigastric pain for 1 day after heavy alcohol drinking T 38°C, P 100/min, RR 24/min, BP 120/80 mmHg. His abdomen is distended with epigastric tenderness, no guarding, and hypoactive bowel sounds. Blood tests:\nCBC: Hb 12 gm%, WBC 13,000/mm3, platelet count 300,000/mm3, glucose 180 mg%, LDH 400 IU/L, AST 300 IU/L, and amylase 1,500 IU/L According to Ranson's prognostic signs of pancreatitis at admission, which one of the following is the score in this patient?","opts":[["A","1"],["B","2"],["C","3"],["D","4"],["E","5"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Ranson on admission (non-gallstone): Age > 55, WBC > 16,000, Glucose > 200, LDH > 350, AST > 250","e":"อายุ 45 (0), WBC 13,000 (0), glucose 180 (0), LDH 400 (1), AST 300 (1) → 2 คะแนน. (ที่ 48 ชม.: Hct ลด > 10%, BUN เพิ่ม > 5, Ca < 8, PaO₂ < 60, base deficit > 4, fluid sequestration > 6 L) ≥ 3 = severe."},{"id":"m51-69","src":"m51","n":69,"cat":"upper-gi","stem":"A 60-year-old male presented with hematemesis for 6 hours with epigastrium pain.\nPE:\nGA: Good consciousness,\nV/S: BP 110/60 mmHg, RR 24/min, PR 100/min, SpO2 95%\nHEENT: mild pale, anicteric sclera\nAbdomen: soft, mild tender at epigastrium, no mass. Hct at ER 30%.\nWhat is the proper management?","opts":[["A","Upper GI study"],["B","Barium esophagography"],["C","Endotracheal intubation"],["D","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"],["E","Computed tomography of chest"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Hematemesis + Hct 30% + vital stable → resuscitate + EGD ภายใน 24 ชม.","e":"Acute UGIB: ABC → IV PPI → upper endoscopy (diagnostic + therapeutic) ภายใน 24 ชม. (≤ 12 ชม. ถ้า high risk). Intubation เฉพาะ massive hematemesis/ซึม (airway protection). Barium/UGI study ห้าม (บังภาพ endoscopy)."},{"id":"m51-70","src":"m51","n":70,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 70-year-old male was diagnosed as ARDS from bacterial pneumonia. The patient's clinical condition had deteriorated into respiratory failure and septic shock with a high dose of an vassopressor agent. Two days later the patient developed lower gastrointestinal hemorrhage. The plain X-ray of the abdomen shows thumb printing sign.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Ulcerative colitis"],["B","Pseudomembranous colitis"],["C","Inflammatory bowel disease"],["D","Mesenteric venous thrombosis"],["E","Nonocclusive mesenteric ischemia"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Shock + vasopressor สูง → NOMI (thumbprinting)","e":"ซ้ำข้อ 9: non-occlusive mesenteric ischemia."},{"id":"m51-71","src":"m51","n":71,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 73-year-old female presented with abdominal distension and massive bloody stool. NG lavage revealed bile content without blood. BP 110/70 mmHg and PR 100/min.\nWhat is the most likely cause of bleeding?","opts":[["A","Anal fissure"],["B","Enterocolitis"],["C","Diverticulosis"],["D","Internal hemorrhoid"],["E","Malignant neoplasm of rectum"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Massive painless hematochezia ในผู้สูงอายุ (NG = bile ไม่มีเลือด) = diverticular bleeding","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 77: diverticulosis เป็นสาเหตุ massive LGIB ที่พบบ่อยที่สุดในผู้สูงอายุ (right-sided diverticula เลือดออกบ่อย)."},{"id":"m51-72","src":"m51","n":72,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 78-year-old male passed more than 200 ml of fresh blood per his rectum follow by yellowish soft form stool in 4 hours. He had no abnormal medical history nor known underlying disease. He denied taking any herbal or medicine.\nPhysical examination revealed BT 37C PR 100/min RR 26/min BP 100/60 mmHg. Digital rectal examination was unremarkable but anoscopy demonstrated grade III of internal hemorrhoids without active bleeding and minimal yellowish stool.\nWhich of the followings is the initial investigation in this patient?","opts":[["A","Hematocrit"],["B","CT angiography"],["C","Radionuclide scintigraphy"],["D","Esophagogastroduodenoscopy"],["E","Selective mesenteric angiography"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"LGIB ผู้สูงอายุ HR 100 BP 100/60 → initial investigation = Hct/CBC (ประเมินความรุนแรง) + resuscitate","e":"ขั้นแรกของ GI bleeding ทุกราย: ประเมิน hemodynamic + ส่ง CBC/Hct, coagulation, group match. Hemorrhoid grade III ไม่ active bleeding อาจไม่ใช่สาเหตุของเลือด 200 mL → ต้องตามด้วย colonoscopy ± CTA/EGD. CTA/scintigraphy/angiography ใช้เมื่อ active bleeding ต่อเนื่อง."},{"id":"m51-73","src":"m51","n":73,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 65-year-old man presented with abdominal pain for 1 day.\nPE: BP 120/70 mmHg, PR 110 beats/min, RR 24/min, BT 38.5 °C. Dry lips and mouth.\nAbdomen: moderate distension, generalized tenderness and markedly tender at LLQ.\nCBC: WBC count 19,000 cells per cubic millimeter. UA: orange color, Specific gravity 1.030, otherwise normal. Abdominal\nCT scan shows: outpunching lesions at sigmoid colon with fat stranding and large amount of intraperitoneal fluid and air.\nWhat is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","IV antibiotics"],["B","Exploratory laparotomy"],["C","Tap release intraperitoneal fluid"],["D","Colonoscopy with closure of perforated site"],["E","Percutaneous drainage and colonic stent placement"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Diverticulitis + free intraperitoneal air + large fluid (Hinchey III–IV) + SIRS → ผ่าตัด","e":"Perforated diverticulitis with generalized peritonitis → resuscitate + ATB + emergency laparotomy (Hartmann procedure หรือ resection + primary anastomosis ± diverting ileostomy). Percutaneous drainage ใช้กับ abscess (Hinchey II) ไม่ใช่ free perforation; colonoscopy ห้าม."},{"id":"m51-74","src":"m51","n":74,"cat":"colorectal","stem":"A 60-year-old woman presents with a 1-day history of acute LLQ abdominal pain.\nPE:\nV/S: BT 39.0°C, BP 110/60 mmHg, PR 100/min, RR 20/min\nGA: Good consciousness\nHEENT: not pale, anicteric sclera\nAbdomen: Mild abdominal distension with hypoactive bowel sounds. Moderate tenderness in the LLQ with localized guarding. No palpable mass.\nCT scan of the abdomen: showed multiple out pouching lesion at sigmoid colon with pericolic fat stranding and hypoechoic lesion 5x5 cm near sigmoid colon with rim enhancement.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate management?","opts":[["A","IV pain killer"],["B","Colonoscopy"],["C","IV antibiotic alone"],["D","Percutaneous drainage"],["E","Exploratory laparotomy"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Diverticulitis + rim-enhancing collection 5 × 5 cm (Hinchey II) → percutaneous drainage","e":"Abscess ≥ 3–4 cm → CT-guided percutaneous drainage + IV ATB (ไม่มี generalized peritonitis). ATB อย่างเดียวพอใน abscess < 3 cm. ผ่าตัดเมื่อ drainage ไม่ได้/ล้มเหลว หรือ peritonitis."},{"id":"m51-75","src":"m51","n":75,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 60-year-old women with poorly controlled hypertension and a history of myocardial infarction presents with incidental finding of abdominal aortic aneurysm that is 4 cm in maximal diameter and 5.5 cm in length.\nWhat is the most appropriate management in this patient?","opts":[["A","CTA aorta"],["B","MRI abdomen"],["C","Echocardiography"],["D","Exercise stress test"],["E","Follow-up ultrasound"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"AAA 4 cm ไม่มีอาการ → surveillance US","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 80: ผ่าตัดเมื่อ ≥ 5.5 cm (ชาย) / ≥ 5.0 cm (หญิง), โต > 1 cm/ปี หรือมีอาการ."},{"id":"m51-76","src":"m51","n":76,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 75-year-old woman presents with left hemiparesis for 5 min with complete recovery. Past medical history were including diabetes mellitus, hypertension, renal insufficiency, and dyslipidemia.\nPE: BP 140/70mmHg, PR 60/min Heart: regular, no murmur\nWhat is the most appropriate screening test to identify the causes in this patient?","opts":[["A","MRA brain"],["B","EEG monitoring"],["C","Echocardiography"],["D","CT scan brain with contrast"],["E","Duplex ultrasound carotid artery"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"TIA ของ carotid territory → carotid duplex","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 2 ข้อ 3: duplex ultrasound carotid เป็น screening test หา carotid stenosis (≥ 70% symptomatic → CEA ภายใน 2 สัปดาห์)."},{"id":"m51-77","src":"m51","n":77,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 70-year-old female presented with moderate intermittent claudication of Rt leg.\nPhysical examination revealed diminished pulses in Rt leg and ABI was 0.65.\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment?","opts":[["A","Warfarin"],["B","Leg elevation"],["C","Cilostazol therapy"],["D","Compressive stocking"],["E","Percutaneous transluminal angioplasty (PTA)"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Intermittent claudication (ABI 0.65 = moderate PAD) → best medical therapy + exercise ก่อน","e":"Claudication: ลด risk factor (เลิกบุหรี่, statin, antiplatelet, คุม DM/HT), supervised exercise therapy, cilostazol (เพิ่มระยะเดิน; ห้ามใน heart failure). Revascularization (PTA) เมื่อ lifestyle-limiting ไม่ตอบสนองการรักษา หรือ CLTI. Warfarin/compression stocking ไม่ใช่การรักษา PAD (stocking อาจทำให้แย่)."},{"id":"m51-78","src":"m51","n":78,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 58-year-old man with history of prostate cancer presents with left leg swelling and heaviness for the past 3 days.\nPhysical exam showed moderate pitting edema at left leg, no redness and no ulcer.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Cellulitis"],["B","Lymphedema"],["C","May-Thurner syndrome"],["D","Acute deep vein thrombosis"],["E","Primary chronic venous insufficiency"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Malignancy (prostate CA) + ขาข้างเดียวบวมเฉียบพลัน 3 วัน pitting edema = DVT จนกว่าจะพิสูจน์ได้ว่าไม่ใช่","e":"Acute DVT (Wells: active cancer +1, pitting edema +1, ...) → compression duplex US. Cellulitis จะแดงร้อนมีไข้; lymphedema เป็นเรื้อรัง non-pitting ภายหลัง; May–Thurner เป็นสาเหตุเฉพาะ (left iliac vein ถูก right common iliac artery กด) พบในหญิงอายุน้อย."},{"id":"m51-79","src":"m51","n":79,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 42-year-old female presented with aching pain, leg heaviness, and fatigue in both lower limbs after standing for long hours at work. Symptoms improve after leg elevation. Duplex ultrasound demonstrates isolated reflux of the great saphenous vein.\nPhysical examination shows visible varicose veins without edema or skin changes.\nWhat is the most appropriate initial management?","opts":[["A","Compressive stocking"],["B","Observation and follow up"],["C","Catheter-directed thrombolysis"],["D","Surgical deep venous valve reconstruction"],["E","Endovenous thermal ablation of the incompetent great saphenous vein"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง = Compressive stocking (A) — initial management","e":"เฉลยอาจารย์ (ไฟล์เหลือง) ตอบ A: symptomatic varicose vein ไม่มี edema/skin change (CEAP C2) → initial management = conservative: compression stocking (20–30 mmHg), ยกขา, ออกกำลังกาย, หลีกเลี่ยงยืนนาน; ถ้าไม่ดีขึ้น (มัก 3 เดือน) หรือมี complication → endovenous thermal ablation (RFA/EVLA) ของ GSV ที่ reflux. Catheter-directed thrombolysis ใช้กับ acute DVT; deep venous valve reconstruction แทบไม่ใช้. หมายเหตุ: guideline SVS/AVF 2022 ยอมให้ทำ ablation ได้เลยโดยไม่ต้องลอง compression ก่อน แต่คำถาม \"initial management\" ในสอบนี้ = compression"},{"id":"m51-80","src":"m51","n":80,"cat":"vascular","stem":"A 20-year-old-man was shot with machine gun at left thigh 1 hour. His left thigh was deformity and swelling. His left pedal pulses were normal.\nPE: BP at the left arm 120/60 mmHg and BP above the left ankle 80/60 mmHg\nWhat is the most appropriate management for this patient?","opts":[["A","MRI of the left leg"],["B","Give the vasodilator drug"],["C","Emergency vascular exploration"],["D","Close observation and reevaluation"],["E","CT angiography of the left lower extremity"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Penetrating extremity trauma: hard sign → OR; soft sign/ABI (API) < 0.9 → CTA","e":"Arterial pressure index (ankle/arm) = 80/120 = 0.67 (< 0.9) โดยไม่มี hard sign (pulse ยังคลำได้ ไม่มี pulsatile bleeding/expanding hematoma) → CT angiography. Hard signs (pulseless, pulsatile bleeding, expanding hematoma, thrill/bruit, distal ischemia) → emergency exploration."},{"id":"m51-81","src":"m51","n":81,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 25-year-old man was stabbed at Rt thoracoabdominal area\nWhich one of the following diagnostic tests should NOT be performed?","opts":[["A","DPL"],["B","eFAST"],["C","CT scan"],["D","Local wound exploration"],["E","Serial physical examination"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Thoracoabdominal stab → ห้าม probe แผล","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 87: local wound exploration ใช้กับ anterior abdominal wall เท่านั้น; ในบริเวณ thoracoabdominal อาจทำให้ pneumothorax และประเมิน diaphragm ไม่ได้ → ใช้ eFAST/CT/DPL/serial exam/laparoscopy."},{"id":"m51-82","src":"m51","n":82,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 59-year-old man is brought to the resuscitation bay after a fall from a height of 5 meters. During the primary survey, he complains of epigastric pain and left chest wall tenderness, with normal breath sounds. His blood pressure is 85/60 mmHg, and pulse rate is 120 bpm. The e-FAST is positive in the hepatorenal and splenorenal recesses. According to ATLS principles, which of the following represents the most appropriate next step in management?","opts":[["A","Apply a pelvic binder"],["B","Perform a diagnostic peritoneal lavage (DPL)"],["C","Request CT scan of the chest and abdomen"],["D","Perform a needle decompression at left chest"],["E","Administer a 300 ml bolus of warmed isotonic crystalloid"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Unstable + eFAST + (ไม่มี laparotomy ในตัวเลือก) → resuscitation ตาม ATLS 11 ระหว่างเตรียม OR","e":"ATLS 11th: ใน hemorrhagic shock ให้ warmed isotonic crystalloid เป็น bolus เล็ก (เช่น 250–500 mL) เป็นสะพานไปสู่ blood products และ definitive hemorrhage control (permissive hypotension). Pelvic binder ใช้เมื่อสงสัย pelvic fracture (โจทย์ไม่บอก); CT ห้ามในคน unstable; DPL ไม่จำเป็นเมื่อ FAST +; breath sound ปกติไม่ต้อง needle decompression."},{"id":"m51-83","src":"m51","n":83,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 28-year-old male presents after being ejected from a truck. He has been intubated for airway protection with tube depth 21 cm and end tidal CO2 is 40 mmHg. After intubated, his RR is 36/min and SpO2 80%. His breath sound decreases at left lung with subcutaneous emphysema. His BP is 80/60 mmHg, HR 110 bpm.\nWhat is the most appropriate management for this patient after re-evaluation?","opts":[["A","eFAST"],["B","Re-intubation"],["C","Film CXR and Pelvis"],["D","Left chest tube insertion"],["E","Open large bore IV for resuscitation"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Intubated + desaturation + BS ซ้ายลด + subcutaneous emphysema + hypotension → pneumothorax (tension) ข้างซ้าย","e":"ท่อลึก 21 cm และ EtCO₂ 40 → ท่อน่าจะอยู่ถูกตำแหน่ง (ไม่ใช่ right mainstem) → หลังใส่ positive pressure ventilation pneumothorax โตเป็น tension → decompress + left chest tube (ATLS: finger thoracostomy/needle แล้ว ICD). Re-intubation ไม่แก้ปัญหา."},{"id":"m51-84","src":"m51","n":84,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 25-year-old man sustained injuries in a motorcycle crash. He complained of tenderness at the Rt side of the chest wall.\nPE: RR 30/min, SaO2 94%, equal breath sounds at both lungs CXR:\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hemothorax"],["B","Lung contusion"],["C","Diaphragmatic injury"],["D","Massive hemothorax"],["E","Thoracic aortic injury"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":["img/m51/image7.jpg"],"t":"CXR: patchy opacity ปอดขวาใต้ตำแหน่งกระแทก + breath sound เท่ากัน","e":"Lung contusion (ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 85): รักษา O₂, pain control, pulmonary toilet, ระวัง fluid overload; ARDS/pneumonia ตามมาได้."},{"id":"m51-85","src":"m51","n":85,"cat":"trauma","stem":"What is the most appropriate tool to diagnose blunt cardiac injury?","opts":[["A","CXR"],["B","2D ECHO"],["C","EKG 12 leads"],["D","Trop-T level"],["E","Transesophgeal ECHO"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Blunt cardiac injury: screening = 12-lead ECG (+ troponin)","e":"EAST: ทุกรายที่สงสัย BCI ทำ ECG 12 lead (ผิดปกติ → admit monitor 24–48 ชม.) ร่วมกับ troponin I; ถ้าทั้งคู่ปกติ ตัด BCI ได้. Echo ใช้เมื่อ hemodynamic ไม่ stable หรือ ECG/troponin ผิดปกติ เพื่อดู wall motion/tamponade."},{"id":"m51-86","src":"m51","n":86,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 30-year-old man presents to the emergency department after a motorcycle crash. During the primary survey, a bedside e-FAST examination is performed, as shown in the image below.\nWhich of the following is the most accurate interpretation of this finding?","opts":[["A","The result is equivocal"],["B","Positive at the cul-de-sac"],["C","Positive at the pericardial space"],["D","Positive at the Hepatorenal pouch"],["E","Negative at the splenorenal recess"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":["img/m51/image8.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ eFAST: anechoic stripe ระหว่างตับกับไตขวา (Morison's pouch)","e":"Positive FAST ที่ hepatorenal pouch (RUQ view ไวที่สุดในการหา hemoperitoneum ท่านอนหงาย). FAST 4 views: RUQ (Morison's), LUQ (splenorenal), pelvis (pouch of Douglas/rectovesical), subxiphoid (pericardium) + eFAST ดู lung sliding."},{"id":"m51-87","src":"m51","n":87,"cat":"trauma","stem":"A 25-year old man sustained in a motorcycle crash. The patient was yelling while the doctor performed physical examination\nPE: E1V3M4 BP 80/50mmHg PR 135/min Pupil Rt 5mm Lt 3 mm\nAbdomen: Abrasion wound 10x10 cm at RLQ, mild tenderness at suprapubic area Pelvis and Perineum: Scrotal hematoma, unstable when pelvic compressionwas performed\nWhich of the following is the proper management in the next step?","opts":[["A","Manitol iv"],["B","Apply pelvic fixation"],["C","Apply pelvic binding"],["D","Prescribe sedation drug"],["E","Endotracheal tube intubation"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Unstable pelvic ring (+ scrotal hematoma) + shock → pelvic binder ทันที (C ใน ABCDE)","e":"ผู้ป่วยตะโกนได้ (airway patent) แต่ BP 80/50 HR 135 + pelvis unstable = pelvic hemorrhage → pelvic binder ระดับ greater trochanter + resuscitate blood → angioembolization/preperitoneal packing/external fixation. GCS 8 + anisocoria ต้องดูแล airway ต่อ แต่ข้อนี้ไฮไลต์ binder. ห้ามสวน Foley ก่อนตัด urethral injury (scrotal hematoma)."},{"id":"m51-88","src":"m51","n":88,"cat":"infection","stem":"An 80-year-old man presented with fever and severe pain at right leg for 1 day following small punctured wound from rusty nail at right foot.\nPE: BT 39.0 C BP 130/80 mmHg PR 110 bpm RR 20/min\nRight leg: mark swelling with hemorrhagic bleb with palpable crepitus.\nWhat is the most proper management for this patient?","opts":[["A","Fasciotomy"],["B","Debridement"],["C","Compressive dressing"],["D","Excision of the bleb"],["E","Hyperbaric oxygen therapy"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ไข้ + ปวดมากเกินสัดส่วน + hemorrhagic bleb + crepitus = necrotizing soft tissue infection","e":"NSTI (gas-forming) → emergency surgical debridement (ตัดเนื้อตายจนถึงเนื้อดี) + broad-spectrum ATB + resuscitation; กลับไปดูซ้ำทุก 24–48 ชม. Hyperbaric O₂ เป็นเสริม; fasciotomy ไม่ได้เอาเนื้อตายออก; excision bleb ไม่พอ."},{"id":"m51-89","src":"m51","n":89,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 67-year-old female with a history of poorly controlled diabetes mellitus presented with progressive right leg pain\nPE: Vital signs: T = 39.2 °C, BP = 92/58 mmHg, HR = 124/min, RR = 26/min.\nRt leg: tense swelling, erythematous skin changes with hemorrhagic bleb formation, and areas of skin necrosis.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Cellulitis"],["B","Erysipelas"],["C","Pyomyositis"],["D","Diabetic foot ulcer"],["E","Necrotizing fasciitis"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"DM + ขาตึงบวม + hemorrhagic bleb + skin necrosis + septic shock = necrotizing fasciitis","e":"Hard signs ของ NF: bullae (hemorrhagic), skin necrosis, crepitus, anesthesia ของผิว, systemic toxicity/shock, ปวดเกินสิ่งที่เห็น. LRINEC score ช่วย แต่ clinical เป็นหลัก → debridement ด่วน. Cellulitis/erysipelas ไม่มี necrosis/bleb ที่มีเลือด."},{"id":"m51-90","src":"m51","n":90,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 50-year-old man underwent right lobe hepatectomy. At postoperative day 1 he developed a fever.\nPE: BT 38.5°C, RR 18/min, BP 110/60 mmHg, PR 82/min Lungs: clear\nAbdomen: good looking surgical site, soft, not tender, JP drain 100 mL of serosanguinous fluid\nWhat is the most likely cause of fever in this patient?","opts":[["A","Sepsis"],["B","Liver failure"],["C","Lung atelectasis"],["D","Pleural effusion"],["E","Intraabdominal collection"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ไข้ POD1 + ปอดใส แผลดี drain ปกติ → atelectasis","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงชุด 1 ข้อ 93: atelectasis/inflammation (Wind) POD 1–2 → incentive spirometry, deep breathing, early ambulation."},{"id":"m51-91","src":"m51","n":91,"cat":"infection","stem":"A 45-year-old man with a short bowel syndrome. He was admitted for total parenteral nutrition. During admission, he developed high-grade fever. Hemoculture was obtained from a peripheral route and the central line. The results showed Peripheral: Gram negative bacilli at 10 hours 30 minutes Central line: Gram negative bacilli at 11 hours 30 minutes\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate upper management?","opts":[["A","Remove the central line"],["B","Switch the TPN to a peripheral line"],["C","Flush the central line with antibiotics"],["D","Continue using the central line without doing anything else"],["E","Stop using the central line for 3 days then use the central line normally"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Differential time to positivity: CRBSI เมื่อ central line positive \"เร็วกว่า\" peripheral ≥ 2 ชม.","e":"ผลนี้ central line โตช้ากว่า peripheral (11:30 vs 10:30 ชม.) → ไม่เข้ากับ catheter-related bloodstream infection → หาแหล่งติดเชื้ออื่น (เช่น GN bacteremia จากลำไส้/translocation ใน short bowel) และให้ ATB ตามนั้น; ไม่ต้องถอด line (line ยังจำเป็นสำหรับ TPN). ถ้าเป็น CRBSI จาก GNB/S. aureus/Candida ต้องถอด line."},{"id":"m51-92","src":"m51","n":92,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 50-year-old woman presented with abdominal pain and vomiting for 3 days. Supine and upright plain abdominal radiography were performed.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Localized ileus"],["B","Generalized ileus"],["C","Small bowel obstruction"],["D","Large bowel obstruction"],["E","Nonspecific bowel gas pattern"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image9.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ supine + upright: SB loop โป่งหลายอัน (valvulae conniventes ตัดเต็มความกว้าง) + air-fluid levels + colon ไม่มีลม","e":"Small bowel obstruction: SB > 3 cm, step-ladder air-fluid levels, colon ยุบ. LBO: colon > 6 cm (cecum > 9 cm) haustra ไม่ตัดเต็มความกว้าง; ileus: SB + colon โป่งทั่วไม่มีจุดตัด."},{"id":"m51-93","src":"m51","n":93,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 58-year-old woman, underlying advanced cervical cancer with rectosigmoid colon invasion, presented with clinical gut obstruction for 5 days and sudden acute abdominal pain for 4 hours\nWhat is the most likely complication of large bowel obstruction in this patient?","opts":[["A","Ischemic bowel"],["B","Infectious colitis"],["C","Toxic megacolon"],["D","Ogilvie syndrome"],["E","Bowel perforation"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":["img/m51/image10.jpg"],"t":"LBO จากมะเร็งกดทับ 5 วัน + ปวดท้องเฉียบพลันรุนแรง + ภาพ free air ใต้กระบังลม","e":"Bowel perforation (มักที่ cecum ตามกฎ Laplace เมื่อ ileocecal valve competent = closed-loop LBO) → pneumoperitoneum บน upright CXR → resuscitate + ATB + emergency laparotomy. Toxic megacolon ต้องมี colitis; Ogilvie ไม่มีจุดอุดจริง."},{"id":"m51-94","src":"m51","n":94,"cat":"acute-abd","stem":"A 60-year-old woman presented with left sided abdominal pain. Plain abdominal Radiography was performed.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Left renal stone"],["B","Left UPJ stone"],["C","Left ureteric stone"],["D","Constipation with fecal impact"],["E","Pneumatosis intestinalis representing ischemic bowel"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":["img/m51/image11.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ KUB: calcific density ตามแนว ureter (ข้าง transverse process/บน pelvic brim) ข้างซ้าย","e":"Left ureteric stone — ตำแหน่งที่นิ่วติดบ่อย: UPJ, pelvic brim (iliac vessel crossing), UVJ. Renal stone อยู่ในเงาไต; phlebolith อยู่ใน pelvis ขอบเรียบมี central lucency (ตัวหลอก); fecal matter มีลวดลายลมปน."},{"id":"m51-95","src":"m51","n":95,"cat":"breast","stem":"A 25-year-old woman presents to the surgical clinic with a new palpable, mobile, firm, painless lump in the right breast. She is not pregnant and has no previous history of breast cancer.\nWhich imaging modality is the most appropriate initial examination?","opts":[["A","Breast MRI"],["B","Ductography"],["C","Breast ultrasound"],["D","Screening mammography alone"],["E","Diagnostic mammography alone"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง = Ductography (B) — ยึดตามเฉลย","e":"เฉลยอาจารย์ (ไฟล์เหลือง) ตอบ B. ⚠ หมายเหตุ: ตามหลัก ACR imaging ก้อนเต้านมใหม่ในหญิงอายุ < 30 ปี → breast ultrasound (C) เป็น initial imaging; ductography ใช้กับ pathologic (bloody/single-duct) nipple discharge; MRI ไม่ใช่ initial; mammography ไม่ไวในเต้านม dense ของคนอายุน้อย. เฉลยข้อนี้อาจคลาดเคลื่อน (ไฮไลต์ห่างจากตัวเลือก US เพียง 1 บรรทัด) — ถ้ามีไฟล์ต้นฉบับลองตรวจไฮไลต์อีกครั้ง; ในสอบจริงให้ตอบตามเฉลยกอง"},{"id":"m51-96","src":"m51","n":96,"cat":"breast","stem":"A screening mammogram demonstrates a mass that is visible on both CC and MLO views. The mass is irregular, high-density, and has spiculated margins with associated internal group of pleomorphic microcalcifications.\nWhat is the most appropriate BI-RADS assessment and management recommendation according to ACR BI-RADS® v2025 ?","opts":[["A","BI-RADS 1; routine screening"],["B","BI-RADS 2; routine screening"],["C","BI-RADS 3; short-term 6-month follow-up"],["D","BI-RADS 4; routine annual screening only"],["E","BI-RADS 5; biopsy and treatment planning"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"เฉลยไฟล์เหลือง = BI-RADS 4 (D) — ยึดตามเฉลย","e":"เฉลยอาจารย์ (ไฟล์เหลือง) ตอบ D. ⚠ หมายเหตุ: ตาม ACR BI-RADS — irregular + spiculated + pleomorphic microcalcification = highly suggestive of malignancy (BI-RADS 5, ≥ 95%) → biopsy; และ BI-RADS 4 เองก็ต้อง biopsy ไม่ใช่ routine annual screening. ตัวเลือก D จึงขัดกับระบบ BI-RADS — เฉลยข้อนี้อาจคลาดเคลื่อน (ไฮไลต์ห่างจาก E เพียง 1 บรรทัด) ถ้ามีไฟล์ต้นฉบับลองตรวจอีกครั้ง"},{"id":"m51-97","src":"m51","n":97,"cat":"breast","stem":"Which patient has a higher risk for breast cancer?","opts":[["A","A 25-year-old woman"],["B","Menopause at age 45"],["C","The first birth at age 26"],["D","Negative BRCA2 mutation"],["E","Has a father with breast cancer"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":[],"t":"Risk factor breast CA: อายุมาก, BRCA, family history (โดยเฉพาะ male breast cancer ในครอบครัว), early menarche/late menopause, nulliparity/first birth > 30","e":"พ่อเป็น breast cancer → บ่งถึง BRCA2 mutation ในครอบครัว → ความเสี่ยงสูง. อายุ 25 เสี่ยงต่ำ; menopause 45 (เร็ว) ลด risk; first birth 26 (< 30) ไม่เพิ่ม; BRCA2 negative ไม่เพิ่ม."},{"id":"m51-98","src":"m51","n":98,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 30-year-old man entered an emergency department after a motorcycle accident. The initial CXR showed moderate amount of hemothorax. Then intercostal drainage (ICD) was done. However, no hemothorax was obtained. A postprocedural CXR is shown below.\nWhat should you do next?","opts":[["A","Repeat CXR"],["B","Connect ICD system to a wall suction"],["C","Push ICD further into the pleural space"],["D","Perform simple drain flushes with 10 mL of 0.9% saline"],["E","Remove ICD and replace correctly into the pleural cavity"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":["img/m51/image12.jpg"],"t":"ICD ไม่ได้ hemothorax ออกเลย + CXR ปลายท่ออยู่นอก pleural cavity (subcutaneous/fissure) = malposition","e":"ถ้า ICD อยู่ผิดที่ (ในชั้น subcutaneous) ต้องถอดและใส่ใหม่ให้ถูกที่ (5th ICS anterior–mid axillary, เหนือขอบบนซี่โครง, ใช้นิ้วคลำยืนยันว่าเข้า pleura). ห้ามดันท่อเดิมเข้าไปเพิ่ม (ปนเปื้อน); suction/flush ไม่ช่วยเมื่อท่ออยู่นอกช่องปอด."},{"id":"m51-99","src":"m51","n":99,"cat":"chest","stem":"Where is the tip of a central venous catheter?","opts":[["A","Superior vena cava"],["B","Left subclavian vein"],["C","Right subclavian vein"],["D","Left internal jugular vein"],["E","Right internal jugular vein"]],"key":"E","ans":"E","imgs":["img/m51/image13.jpg"],"t":"ภาพ CXR: CVC เข้าจากคอขวาลงมาตามแนว IJ แต่ปลายยังอยู่ในคอ/เหนือ clavicle","e":"ปลาย catheter ที่ถูกต้องควรอยู่ distal SVC/cavoatrial junction (~ระดับ carina). ภาพนี้ tip อยู่ที่ right internal jugular vein (สั้นเกินไป) → ต้องปรับตำแหน่ง. เฉลยไฮไลต์ E."},{"id":"m51-100","src":"m51","n":100,"cat":"chest","stem":"A 65-year-old male who is day 3 post exploratory laparotomy with dyspnea. The CXR is shown below.\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Aspiration"],["B","Pneumonia"],["C","Pleural effusion"],["D","Pulmonary edema"],["E","Pulmonary embolism"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":["img/m51/image14.jpg"],"t":"POD3 หลัง laparotomy + dyspnea + CXR: bilateral perihilar haziness (bat-wing), vascular congestion","e":"Pulmonary edema จาก fluid overload ช่วง mobilization (POD 2–3 น้ำจาก third space กลับเข้าหลอดเลือด) หรือ cardiac → diuretic, ลด fluid, O₂. Pneumonia มัก lobar/unilateral + ไข้; effusion = blunt costophrenic angle; PE มักไม่มี CXR finding ชัด."},{"id":"m51-101","src":"m51","n":101,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 30-year-old male was in a car accident two days ago. He has a right femur fracture and is now in a long leg cast.\nWhat is the most appropriate treatment to prevent disuse muscle atrophy in this patient?","opts":[["A","Ankle pumping exercise"],["B","Continuous passive motion"],["C","Isotonic strengthening exercise"],["D","Isometric contraction of calf muscle"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Long leg cast ขยับข้อไม่ได้ → ออกกำลังโดยไม่ขยับข้อ = isometric","e":"Isometric (static) contraction ของกล้ามเนื้อใน cast (quadriceps setting, calf) ป้องกัน disuse atrophy ได้โดยไม่ต้องขยับข้อ. Ankle pumping/CPM/isotonic ต้องขยับข้อซึ่ง cast ไม่อนุญาต."},{"id":"m51-102","src":"m51","n":102,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 35-year-old male was in a motorcycle accident two days ago. He has complete paralysis of both legs due to a complete spinal cord injury.\nWhich of the following is correct for the prevention and treatment of deep vein thrombosis in this patient?","opts":[["A","Active ankle pumping should be prescribed for him"],["B","Wells' clinical score is not necessary if his leg is swelling"],["C","Intermittent pneumatic compression should be prescribed"],["D","Ultrasound Doppler should be performed on every patient with a spinal cord injury"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"Complete SCI = เสี่ยง VTE สูงมาก + ขาอ่อนแรง → mechanical + pharmacologic prophylaxis","e":"SCI: เริ่ม LMWH ภายใน 72 ชม. (ถ้าไม่มีข้อห้าม) ร่วมกับ intermittent pneumatic compression. ผู้ป่วยขยับขาเองไม่ได้ จึง active ankle pumping ไม่ได้; ขาบวมยังต้องใช้ Wells/ประเมิน; ไม่แนะนำ routine Doppler screening ทุกราย."},{"id":"m51-103","src":"m51","n":103,"cat":"rehab","stem":"A 60-year-old female with an intracranial meningioma underwent tumor removal surgery. She was comatose for one week. From the physical examination, no deconditioning conditions were found\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate rehabilitation program for this patient?","opts":[["A","Triflo exercise"],["B","Passive secretion clearance"],["C","Repositioning every 2 hours"],["D","Continuous passive motion device"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"ผู้ป่วยโคม่า (ยังไม่มี deconditioning) → ป้องกันแผลกดทับ/ภาวะแทรกซ้อนจากการนอนนิ่ง","e":"Repositioning ทุก 2 ชม. ป้องกัน pressure ulcer, atelectasis และ contracture บางส่วน — เป็นโปรแกรมพื้นฐานที่สำคัญสุดในผู้ป่วยไม่รู้สึกตัว. Triflo ต้องการความร่วมมือ; CPM ใช้หลังผ่าตัดข้อ; passive secretion clearance ทำเมื่อมีเสมหะ."},{"id":"m51-104","src":"m51","n":104,"cat":"rehab","stem":"Which patient is the best candidate to use continuous passive motion device to prevent joint contracture?","opts":[["A","A 20-year-old female post appendectomy for 2 days"],["B","A 25-year-old male had right tibia fracture on short leg slab"],["C","A 30-year-old female in a comatose state due to brain metastasis"],["D","A 35-year-old male post irrigation and drainage right knee due to septic arthritis"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"CPM ใช้หลังผ่าตัด/ติดเชื้อในข้อเพื่อกัน adhesion/stiffness (เช่น knee หลัง I&D septic arthritis, TKA)","e":"CPM: ข้อที่เสี่ยงข้อยึดหลังผ่าตัดในข้อ (septic arthritis หลัง arthrotomy/I&D, TKA, intra-articular fracture ที่ fix แล้ว). ไม่ใช้กับ fracture ที่อยู่ใน slab, หลัง appendectomy, หรือคนโคม่า (ใช้ ROM/positioning แทน)."},{"id":"m51-105","src":"m51","n":105,"cat":"rehab","stem":"Which one is correct for incentive spirometry?","opts":[["A","It had only a flow type"],["B","It could improve lung capacity"],["C","Need patient to force expiration"],["D","only effective when used for at least 30 minutes at a time"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Incentive spirometry = sustained maximal inspiration (หายใจเข้าช้า ลึก ค้าง)","e":"IS ช่วยเพิ่ม lung volume/inspiratory capacity ป้องกัน atelectasis หลังผ่าตัด. มีทั้ง flow-oriented (Triflo ลูกบอล) และ volume-oriented; เน้นหายใจเข้า ไม่ใช่ forced expiration; ใช้ 10 ครั้ง/ชม. ขณะตื่น ไม่ต้องนานครั้งละ 30 นาที."},{"id":"m51-106","src":"m51","n":106,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A healthy 24-year-old man had a femoral fracture. Following open reduction and internal fixation (ORIF), he has been receiving morphine 3 mg IV q 3 hours. Despite this, he still has severe pain (VAS 10/10).\nWhich of the following is NOT an appropriate management?","opts":[["A","Increase morphine to 5 mg IV q 3 hours."],["B","Add oral ibuprofen."],["C","Add oral paracetamol."],["D","Switch from morphine to fentanyl 30 mcg IV q 3 hours."],["E","Shorten the morphine interval from every 3 hours to every 2 hours"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ปวดเพราะ dose ไม่พอ → เพิ่ม dose/ความถี่ หรือเพิ่ม non-opioid; การเปลี่ยน full agonist ตัวเทียบเท่าไม่ช่วย","e":"Morphine 3 mg ≈ fentanyl 30 mcg (equianalgesic: morphine 5 mg = fentanyl 50 mcg) → switch ไม่ได้เพิ่มฤทธิ์ และ fentanyl ออกฤทธิ์สั้น q3h ไม่เหมาะ → ไม่เหมาะสม. เพิ่ม morphine/ถี่ขึ้น, เติม paracetamol/NSAIDs (multimodal) เหมาะสม."},{"id":"m51-107","src":"m51","n":107,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which of the following patients is least likely to develop opioid-induced respiratory depression?","opts":[["A","An elderly patient"],["B","A patient with chronic renal failure"],["C","A patient taking multiple medications"],["D","A patient with increased hepatic clearance"],["E","A patient who has recently received a sedative medication"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ใครเสี่ยงกดหายใจ \"น้อยสุด\" → คนที่กำจัดยาได้เร็ว","e":"Risk ของ opioid-induced respiratory depression: elderly, CKD/ตับบกพร่อง (ยาสะสม), polypharmacy, ได้ sedative ร่วม, OSA, opioid-naive. Increased hepatic clearance → ระดับยาลดเร็ว → เสี่ยงต่ำสุด."},{"id":"m51-108","src":"m51","n":108,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 20-year-old man (ASA Physical Status I) with Carpal tunnel syndrome is undergoing left carpal tunnel release under a brachial plexus block.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate postoperative analgesic regimen?","opts":[["A","Paracetamol 1 g PO q 6 hours"],["B","Morphine 3 mg IV q 2 hours"],["C","Fentanyl 50 mcg IV q 2 hours"],["D","Codeine 30 mg PO q 4 hours"],["E","Tramadol 100 mg PO q 6 hours"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"ผ่าตัดเล็ก + brachial plexus block → paracetamol PO","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงข้อ 107: block คุมปวดได้ดี ผ่าตัดเล็ก → paracetamol 1 g q6h (± NSAID) เพียงพอ; ไม่ต้องใช้ opioid IV."},{"id":"m51-109","src":"m51","n":109,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"An 80-year-old man with colon cancer is receiving chemotherapy and has developed thrombocytopenia. He undergoes an appendectomy.\nWhich of the following analgesics should NOT be administered postoperatively?","opts":[["A","Diclofenac"],["B","Tramadol"],["C","Morphine"],["D","Fentanyl"],["E","Paracetamol"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Thrombocytopenia + ผู้สูงอายุ + chemo → ห้าม NSAIDs","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงข้อ 108: diclofenac เพิ่ม bleeding (platelet dysfunction), GI bleed, AKI."},{"id":"m51-110","src":"m51","n":110,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 45-year-old woman undergoes total abdominal hysterectomy under general anesthesia. The anesthesiologist performs a bilateral transversus abdominis plane (TAP) block preoperatively and uses paracetamol and NSAIDs postoperatively.\nWhich of the following is the most likely rationale for this approach?","opts":[["A","TAP block completely eliminates the need for opioids postoperatively"],["B","TAP block is effective for visceral pain control and central sensitization"],["C","Multimodal analgesia reduces opioid-related side effects and improves recovery"],["D","Paracetamol and NSAIDs are sufficient alone for all abdominal surgeries"],["E","TAP block provides long-lasting analgesia for more than 48 hours"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"TAP block (somatic) + paracetamol + NSAIDs = multimodal analgesia","e":"Multimodal: ใช้ยา/เทคนิคหลายกลไก → opioid-sparing ลด N/V, ileus, กดหายใจ → recover เร็ว (ERAS). TAP block คุมเฉพาะ somatic pain ของผนังหน้าท้อง (ไม่คุม visceral), ฤทธิ์ ~6–24 ชม. ไม่ใช่ > 48 ชม. และไม่ได้กำจัดความต้องการ opioid ทั้งหมด."},{"id":"m51-111","src":"m51","n":111,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 50-year-old woman got a car accident. She has a crush injury to her right leg with an open wound exposing fractures of both the tibia and fibula. She is scheduled for urgent irrigation and debridement of the wound with external fixation. She had dinner 1 hour before the accident.\nWhat is the most appropriate anesthetic management?","opts":[["A","Delay surgery until 8 hours after her last solid meal."],["B","Delay surgery until 6 hours after she has finished drinking water."],["C","Proceed to surgery without any preoperative consideration."],["D","Proceed to surgery with prescribe metoclopramide and omeprazole IV injection before going to OR"],["E","Proceed with surgery after inserting a nasogastric tube to remove gastric contents."]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ผ่าตัดเร่งด่วน (open fracture) + full stomach (กินก่อนอุบัติเหตุ, trauma ทำให้ gastric emptying ช้า) → ไม่ต้องรอ NPO","e":"Trauma = full stomach เสมอ (การรอไม่ทำให้กระเพาะว่าง). ไปผ่าตัดต่อพร้อม aspiration prophylaxis (metoclopramide + PPI/H2RA IV, ± sodium citrate) และ rapid sequence induction with cricoid pressure หรือใช้ regional anesthesia. Open fracture ควร debride ภายใน 24 ชม. ไม่ควรเลื่อนตาม NPO."},{"id":"m51-112","src":"m51","n":112,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 24-year-old woman with a history of asthma is scheduled for an orthopedic procedure under general anesthesia.\nWhich of the following is LEAST likely to prevent bronchospasm?","opts":[["A","Beta 2 agonist nebulizer in the preoperative holding area"],["B","Beta 2 agonist inhaler before patient is lying down on the operating table"],["C","Use of laryngeal mask airway instead of endotracheal tube"],["D","Transtracheal lidocaine before intubation"],["E","Administration of opioids before intubation"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"ป้องกัน bronchospasm ในคนหอบหืด: bronchodilator ก่อน, หลีกเลี่ยงการกระตุ้น airway (LMA, ดมยาให้ลึกพอ, IV lidocaine/opioid ก่อน intubate)","e":"Transtracheal lidocaine (ฉีดผ่าน cricothyroid membrane) เองเป็นการกระตุ้น airway (ไอ) จึงช่วยน้อยที่สุด/อาจทำให้ bronchospasm; IV lidocaine ช่วย blunt reflex ได้ดีกว่า. β2-agonist ก่อนผ่าตัด, LMA แทน ETT, และ opioid ก่อน intubation ช่วยลด airway reactivity."},{"id":"m51-113","src":"m51","n":113,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 59-year-old man is scheduled for laparoscopic cholecystectomy.\nPhysical examination reveals obesity (BMI 34 kg/m2), a full beard, an intergingival gap of 4 cm, edentulous, full neck flexion and extension, thyromental distance of 7 cm, ULBT grade 1, Mallampati class 1, and neck circumference of 38 cm. How would you assess his airway?","opts":[["A","Easy mask ventilation, Easy intubation"],["B","Easy mask ventilation, Difficult intubation"],["C","Difficult mask ventilation, Easy intubation"],["D","Difficult mask ventilation, Difficult intubation"],["E","Require further radiologic investigation"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"แยกประเมิน mask ventilation (BONES: Beard, Obese, No teeth, Elderly, Snoring) vs intubation (MP, TMD, IIG, neck, ULBT)","e":"Beard + obesity (BMI 34) + edentulous + อายุ > 55 → difficult mask ventilation. แต่ MP 1, TMD 7 cm, IIG 4 cm, ULBT grade 1, คอขยับเต็ม → easy intubation (ไม่มีฟันทำให้ laryngoscopy ง่ายขึ้น)."},{"id":"m51-114","src":"m51","n":114,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 65-year-old woman with a history of poor controlled hypertension, diabetes mellitus, and stable angina is scheduled to undergo laparoscopic cholecystectomy. According to the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status Classification System, what is the most appropriate ASA physical status classification?","opts":[["A","ASA II"],["B","ASA III"],["C","ASA IV"],["D","ASA V"],["E","ASA VI"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ASA III = severe systemic disease (โรคที่คุมไม่ดี/หลายโรค จำกัดการทำงาน)","e":"Poorly controlled HT + DM + stable angina → ASA III. (ASA II = mild well-controlled disease เช่น HT/DM คุมได้; ASA IV = severe systemic disease ที่คุกคามชีวิตตลอดเวลา เช่น recent MI < 3 เดือน, unstable angina; ASA VI = brain dead organ donor)"},{"id":"m51-115","src":"m51","n":115,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 50-year-old woman with no other underlying disease is scheduled for a total abdominal hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy (TAH with BSO).\nPhysical examination reveals mild pale.\nWhich of the following preoperative investigations is LEAST indicated?","opts":[["A","Serum electrolytes"],["B","Complete blood count (CBC)"],["C","Chest X-ray"],["D","Electrocardiogram (ECG)"],["E","Hematocrit (Hct)"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"Preop lab ตามข้อบ่งชี้: CBC/Hct (ซีด + ผ่าตัดที่เสียเลือด), CXR/ECG ตามอายุ/โรค; electrolyte เมื่อมีโรคไต/ยาขับปัสสาวะ","e":"หญิง 50 ปีไม่มีโรค ไม่ได้ใช้ diuretic/ACEI ไม่มีโรคไต → serum electrolytes ไม่จำเป็น. CBC/Hct จำเป็นเพราะซีด + TAH-BSO เสียเลือดได้; ECG ตามเกณฑ์อายุ (≥ 45–50 ตามแนวทาง รพ.); CXR ตามแนวทาง มอ."},{"id":"m51-116","src":"m51","n":116,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 25-year-old woman underwent a salpingo-oophorectomy under general anesthesia with endotracheal intubation using a balanced anesthetic technique. Tracheal extubation was uneventful. She develops hoarseness immediately after surgery that persists for 4 days. She reports a breathy voice, vocal fatigue, and pain when swallowing.\nWhat is the most likely cause?","opts":[["A","Vocal cord edema"],["B","Vocal cord polyp"],["C","Arytenoid dislocation"],["D","Unilateral recurrent laryngeal nerve injury"],["E","Bilateral recurrent laryngeal nerve injury"]],"key":"C","ans":"C","imgs":[],"t":"แหบทันทีหลังผ่าตัด + นาน (4 วัน) + breathy voice + vocal fatigue + เจ็บกลืน (odynophagia) = arytenoid dislocation","e":"Arytenoid dislocation/subluxation จาก laryngoscope/ETT: แหบทันที, เสียงแหบลม (vocal cord ปิดไม่สนิท), ปวดเวลากลืน → laryngoscopy ยืนยัน และ closed reduction เร็ว. Vocal cord edema หายใน 2–3 วัน ไม่ breathy มาก; unilateral RLN injury จากผ่าตัดคอ."},{"id":"m51-117","src":"m51","n":117,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 65-year-old man with well-controlled hypertension undergoes a laparoscopic cholecystectomy under general anesthesia lasting 1.5 hours. During the procedure, he receives morphine 12 mg and vecuronium 12 mg. The volatile anesthetic is discontinued 15 minutes before the end of surgery. After administration of a neuromuscular blockade reversal agent for 15 minutes, he remains apneic and unconscious. His pupils are 1 mm bilaterally\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?","opts":[["A","Hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state"],["B","Metabolic acidosis"],["C","Residual neuromuscular blockade"],["D","Opioid overdose"],["E","Cerebrovascular accident"]],"key":"D","ans":"D","imgs":[],"t":"Apnea + unconscious + pinpoint pupils (1 mm) หลังได้ morphine 12 mg = opioid overdose","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงข้อ 109 (เติม pupils 1 mm ทำให้ชัด) → ช่วยหายใจ + naloxone titrate (40 mcg ซ้ำ) และเฝ้าระวัง renarcotization."},{"id":"m51-118","src":"m51","n":118,"cat":"thyroid","stem":"A 25-year-old woman with Hashimoto's thyroiditis undergoes subtotal thyroidectomy. Six hours after the operation, she has seizure.\nWhat is the most likely cause?","opts":[["A","Hypoxemia from vocal cord edema"],["B","Hypocalcemia"],["C","Hypercalcemia"],["D","Hyperventilation"],["E","Hyponatremia"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"ชักหลัง thyroidectomy 6 ชม. → hypocalcemia","e":"ซ้ำไฟล์แดงข้อ 115: hypoparathyroidism (temporary/permanent) → calcium gluconate IV."},{"id":"m51-119","src":"m51","n":119,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"A 45-year-old male undergoes an uneventful laparoscopic cholecystectomy under general anesthesia. At the recovery room, the nurse uses the Modified Aldrete Score to assess the patient's readiness for discharge.\nWhich of the following criteria is NOT included in the Modified Aldrete Score?","opts":[["A","Activity"],["B","Pain Level"],["C","Respiration"],["D","Oxygen Saturation"],["E","Blood pressure"]],"key":"B","ans":"B","imgs":[],"t":"Modified Aldrete (PACU discharge) 5 ข้อ: Activity, Respiration, Circulation (BP), Consciousness, O₂ saturation (Color)","e":"Pain ไม่อยู่ใน modified Aldrete score (แต่อยู่ใน PADSS ที่ใช้สำหรับ discharge กลับบ้าน ambulatory: vital signs, activity, N/V, pain, surgical bleeding). ผ่าน PACU เมื่อคะแนน ≥ 9."},{"id":"m51-120","src":"m51","n":120,"cat":"anesthesia","stem":"Which one is the risk factor of postdural puncture headache?","opts":[["A","Quincke needle"],["B","Male patient"],["C","Elderly patient"],["D","BMI > 25 kg/m2"],["E","Patient with mild cognitive impairment"]],"key":"A","ans":"A","imgs":[],"t":"PDPH เสี่ยงขึ้นเมื่อ: เข็มใหญ่, cutting needle (Quincke), ผู้หญิง, อายุน้อย, BMI ต่ำ, ตั้งครรภ์, เคยมี PDPH","e":"Quincke (cutting bevel) ตัดเส้นใย dura → รูรั่ว CSF มากกว่า pencil-point (Whitacre/Sprotte). ชาย, ผู้สูงอายุ, BMI สูง เสี่ยงน้อยลง."}];
